    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33417": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Programs in Human Resource Development",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Programs in Human Resource Development Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Programs in Human Resource Development To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Graduate Programs in Human Resource Development will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. Information about the HRD program and course curriculum are available at http://www.villanova.edu/artsci/hrd. All applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: ** A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. ** A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching and the time period during which the applicant expects to be available. ** Contact information for 3 references who will be contacted via email to submit confidential letters of recommendation after the applicant is interviewed. ** If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2020717F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Programs in Human Resource Development Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 153-Human Resource Development Position Summary: Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in the Graduate Programs for Human Resource Development in their online and on-campus evening program. The specific courses involved may vary from semester to semester and a detailed course list is available at http://www.villanova.edu/artsci/hrd. The applicant must be committed to excellence in human resource development education and hold at a minimum a master’s degree in human resources or related field. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching courses for the Graduate Programs in Human Resource Development fully online and/or on campus. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree in Human Resources or related field. The applicant must be committed to excellence in Human Resource Development. Preferred Qualifications: Advanced degree (Masters, JD, PhD, EdD) and previous teaching experience. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The Graduate Programs in Human Resource Development will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. Information about the HRD program and course curriculum are available at http://www.villanova.edu/artsci/hrd. All applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: * A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. * A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching and the time period during which the applicant expects to be available. * Contact information for 3 references who will be contacted via email to submit confidential letters of recommendation after the applicant is interviewed. * If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: 04/23/2020 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,160.00 – $2,230.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at .