    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36292": {
      "title": "Barista - Dixon Cabrini Campus",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Barista - Dixon Cabrini Campus Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Barista - Dixon Cabrini Campus To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. SCHEDULE during normal operating hours: Tuesday - Saturday 6am - 11:30am Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260235S Position Title: Barista - Dixon Cabrini Campus Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/9-months Avg Hours Week 25 Department: 837-Dining Services- Cabrini Campus Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people. Even as a part-time employee, you will receive access to certain benefits, including tuition assistance and more . The Barista is responsible for exceptional customer service at Holy Grounds locations which includes defined level of product knowledge, presentation and quality of product, speed of service, sales ability, and good customer relations skills. Responsible for operating Holy Grounds as an independent unit and assuming all the responsibilities with that role since a manager is not present at all times. This person will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the value of the Villanova Mission Statement and the Dining Services Mission Statement. This person will focus on our Core Values: Safety and Sanitation, Friendly Courteous Service, Quality, Meticulous Attention to Detail, and Safety. All of our associates should improve our systems and overall operation. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Provides excellent customer service that is efficient, friendly and speedy to Holy Grounds customers. Treat each customer as your highest priority, being mindful of customers who are waiting. Operates POS terminals and some locations while others use Grub Hub applications to receive orders. Actively shares coffee and tea knowledge while actively selling all products. Advises customers of new coffees or teas or featured items of the week. Prepares all drinks according to Holy Grounds standards. Maintains the cleanliness and attractiveness of the Holy Ground kiosk by keeping counters and displays cleaned and fully stocked. Makes sure all products are labeled correctly. NONESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Assist manager with scheduling of student associates. Responsible for enforcing the uniform standards of all student associates. Completes the tasks assigned at each shift, ensuring that everything is ready for the next shift. Enforces and practices all safety and sanitation policies and procedures for Villanova Dining Services. Monitors customer needs and responds to any concerns or questions in a friendly and courteous manner while attempting to resolve the issue immediately. Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: High School diploma or equivalent Specific Job Knowledge: Interest in coffee preferred. Will need to sample and test products for quality assurance. Minimum Work Experience: Cashiering experience or general food service experience of 1-2 years. Work Skills: Excellent communication and interpersonal skills Strong customer service skills Dress and grooming appropriate for Holy Grounds Concept Able to handle numerous tasks at once while prioritizing Equipment Knowledge: Will train on all coffee equipment. Preferred – POS and Grub Hub systems Preferred Qualifications: Serv Safe certification preferred. Cash register knowledge is preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery, and equipment used: Espresso machines, grinders, blenders, and cash registers Environmental conditions: Increased noise level around some equipment Cleaning chemicals used Physical requirements: Ability to lift up to 30 pounds independently. Ability to sit stand for extended periods. Ability to push/pull up to 30 pounds independently. Ability to use various chemicals. Manual Dexterity. Special Message to Applicants: SCHEDULE during normal operating hours: Tuesday – Saturday 6am – 11:30am Posting Date: 05/13/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $18.98 per hour. Shift differential for qualifying shifts. Salary Grade: 8 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
