    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33453": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Chemical Engineering",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Chemical Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Chemical Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The department of Chemical Engineering will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications. Please indicate your areas of teaching interest and expertise within the specified question in the application. Online applications are to include a letter of interest, the name and contact information for at least 3 references, current and complete curriculum vitae, and a statement describing your teaching philosophy including courses you are interested in teaching. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2014173F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Chemical Engineering Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 203-Chemical Engineering Position Summary: Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Chemical Engineering for graduate courses taught in the evening and/or undergraduate courses taught during the day. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and other duties which vary with specific courses. Minimum Qualifications: An earned doctorate in Chemical Engineering or a closely allied discipline is strongly preferred; master’s degree required. The applicant must be committed to excellence in engineering education. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The department of Chemical Engineering will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications. Please indicate your areas of teaching interest and expertise within the specified question in the application. Online applications are to include a letter of interest, the name and contact information for at least 3 references, current and complete curriculum vitae, and a statement describing your teaching philosophy including courses you are interested in teaching. Posting Date: 10/24/2014 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,650.00 – $2,600.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: N/A Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Brow