    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36377": {
      "title": "Temporary Researcher",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Temporary Researcher Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Temporary Researcher To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please submit your application at: http://jobs.villanova.edu : Application packages must include: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Academic Transcripts Names and contact information of three references Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260045T Position Title: Temporary Researcher Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: temporary Approximate Number of Hours per Week 5-10 Hours per Week Department: 098-EGR Endowed Chairs Supplemental Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Provide data analysis and oversight assistance on the campus monitoring project. Contribute to the dissemination of research findings through academic publications, presentations, and community outreach. Contribute to and assist on special projects including data analysis and publication. Perform other duties and assist with projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: PhD in water resources engineering, civil engineering or a related field. Work Experience: 1 year experience in civil engineering or a related field. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills): Highly motivated with strong written and oral communication skills Must be able to work independently and communicate proactively Specific Job Knowledge (e.g.; knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area): Understand hydrologic and water quality data and analysis techniques Skills working interdisciplinarily. Equipment Knowledge: Must be comfortable working on a computer Standard office equipment Preferred Qualifications: Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills): Good organizational skills. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery and equipment used: Computational modeling; must be comfortable working on a computer. Special Message to Applicants: Please submit your application at: http://jobs.villanova.edu : Application packages must include: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Academic Transcripts Names and contact information of three references EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: 09/16/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $34.67 per hour. Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Do you have a PHD in Engineering? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
