    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34106": {
      "title": "Lab Assistant / Peer Mentor",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Lab Assistant / Peer Mentor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Lab Assistant / Peer Mentor To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20255589V Position Title: Lab Assistant / Peer Mentor Posting Type Student Hours/week: 5-20 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2025-2026 Academic Year Location Mendel Science Center Detailed Work Schedule Monday – Friday during class times and preparation of lab. Hours may vary due to duties that are assigned. Number of positions: 8 Department: 183-Biology Contact Name: Traci Rayer / Aimee McStravog Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-7424 / 610-519-4832 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Basic lab work; clean glassware; process samples; assist with various types of analysis. Requirements: Attention to detail; able to follow directions; science major preferred, but not required. Previous lab experience a plus but not necessary. Additional Information: Must have good work ethic; includes summer, fall and spring semesters Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $10.00 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability (days, times)?