    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35596": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Biochemistry",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Biochemistry Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Assistant Professor of Biochemistry To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, please visit Villanova’s job portal (https://jobs.villanova.edu/). Review of applications will begin September 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled, and the starting date is expected to be August 2027. Applications must be submitted online and include: • Cover letter • Complete curriculum vitae • Teaching statement (teaching philosophy and methods, outcomes, goals, and development activities, if applicable) • Proposed research statement that demonstrates potential for high-quality scholarship while involving undergraduate and master’s students. Should include any necessary instrumentation to be purchased with startup funding; a list of current departmental instrumentation is on the departmental website. • Candidates will be expected to provide a statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions may support the University’s mission (and enduring principles) . Please refer to the departmental website and the Villanova University Mission Statement. • Undergraduate and graduate transcripts (unofficial acceptable for application). Transcripts can be uploaded as a scan/PDF as an “Other Document” to the HR site. • Must include contact information for 3 references who will be contacted via email to submit confidential letters of recommendation when the application is submitted. • Other supporting documents may be submitted online in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260055F Position Title: Assistant Professor of Biochemistry Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 184-Chemistry Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Villanova University invites applicants for a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor position in Biochemistry to teach in our department, which offers ACS -certified B.S. degrees in chemistry, ASBMB -accredited B.S. degrees in biochemistry, and M.S. degrees in chemistry. The successful candidate will receive a start-up package and a pre-tenure sabbatical. Please visit our webpage for information about the department. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect, and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will contribute to the vibrant curriculum of the department at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, teaching up to 15 contact hours per year (12 in the first year), with courses in biochemistry and in additional area(s) of specialty. The candidate will establish and maintain an active and productive research program, integrate undergraduate and master’s students into research, actively seek extramural funding, and effectively participate in departmental/university and professional service. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants should have a Ph.D. and postdoctoral experience in biochemistry or related fields. Applicants should show potential for success in teaching and research in a predominantly undergraduate liberal arts setting. Preferred Qualifications: At least two years of post-doctoral research experience (at the time of application) that broadens the candidate’s expertise. Experience teaching and mentoring undergraduates in both classroom and laboratory settings. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Some classes are taught in the evenings. Special Message to Applicants: To apply, please visit Villanova’s job portal (https://jobs.villanova.edu/). Review of applications will begin September 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled, and the starting date is expected to be August 2027. Applications must be submitted online and include: • Cover letter • Complete curriculum vitae • Teaching statement (teaching philosophy and methods, outcomes, goals, and development activities, if applicable) • Proposed research statement that demonstrates potential for high-quality scholarship while involving undergraduate and master’s students. Should include any necessary instrumentation to be purchased with startup funding; a list of current departmental instrumentation is on the departmental website. • Candidates will be expected to provide a statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions may support the University’s mission (and enduring principles) . Please refer to the departmental website and the Villanova University Mission Statement. • Undergraduate and graduate transcripts (unofficial acceptable for application). Transcripts can be uploaded as a scan/ PDF as an “Other Document” to the HR site. • Must include contact information for 3 references who will be contacted via email to submit confidential letters of recommendation when the application is submitted. • Other supporting documents may be submitted online in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: 07/08/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Statement of Research Interests Statement of Contribution to Mission Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36193": {
      "title": "Costume Crew",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Costume Crew Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Costume Crew To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260373V Position Title: Costume Crew Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10-15 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Mullen Center Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 6 Department: 176-Theatre - Winter Contact Name: Rosemarie McKelvey Contact Phone/Extension: 94394 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Sew costumes, paint shoes, build masks, make hats, cut out fabric from patterns, dye fabrics and jewelry making. Requirements: Must be able to sew, but we will provide training if needed. Must be willing to learn costume construction language. Good communication skills. Ability to work without supervision, dependable, and a sense of humor. Additional Information: Must be available on occasional nights and weekends. FIRST - YEAR STUDENTS PREFERRED . Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $11.25 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
