    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36563": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty Paralegal Certificate Program",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty Paralegal Certificate Program Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty Paralegal Certificate Program To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, please submit the following documents: Cover Letter / Letter of Interest indicating the course(s) you are interested in teaching and your order of expertise and preference Resume / CV Statement of Teaching Philosophy Contact information for three professional references Official transcripts will be required from all finalists for this position. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2020689F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty Paralegal Certificate Program Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 576-Dean, Professional Studies Position Summary: Villanova University invites passionate educators to join our esteemed Paralegal Certificate Program as an adjunct faculty member. We are looking for enthusiastic and dedicated legal professionals who are passionate about teaching and mentoring the next generation of paralegals. The Paralegal Certificate Program runs in two modalities: in-person day program and online evening program. In-person Day Program courses: In person on Villanova’s campus Four to six class sessions over two or three consecutive weeks. Online Evening Program courses: Online · One evening per week for six weeks Current course offerings include: Introduction to the Paralegal Profession Tort and Personal Injury Law Civil Procedure & Litigation Procedure Criminal Law Family Law Business Organizations Contract Law Intellectual Property Law Legal Research Legal Writing Office Coordination Real Estate Law Applicants should please specify the course(s) they are interested in teaching and rank them according to expertise in the area and teaching preference. Also please indicate in your cover letter if you are available to teach in-person day, online evening, or both. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. We are committed to diversity and inclusion as integral components of our mission. We seek candidates who understand, respect, and can contribute to our mission and values. Villanova University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer. If you are passionate about teaching and eager to contribute to the Villanova community, we encourage you to apply today! Duties and Responsibilities: Duties involved include, but are not limited to: Leading class and conducting all associated planning and grading Reviewing student work and assessing learning Participating in trainings and meetings (as needed) with College staff Attending Paralegal program faculty meetings Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree. Recent experience working as, or with, paralegals. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Excellent organizational skills. Preferred Qualifications: Proven ability to teach successfully in both the in-person and online settings Experience with instructional technology Graduate or professional degree Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: To apply, please submit the following documents: Cover Letter / Letter of Interest indicating the course(s) you are interested in teaching and your order of expertise and preference Resume / CV Statement of Teaching Philosophy Contact information for three professional references Official transcripts will be required from all finalists for this position. Posting Date: 02/28/2020 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Statement of Contribution to Mission Optional Documents Other Document Summary of Teaching Evaluations Writing Sample/Publications Statement of Research Interests Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
