    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33438": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Physics",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Physics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Physics To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Department of Physics will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications. All applicants must apply on line and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. 3. Statement of Teaching Philosophy. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20231055F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Physics Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/9-months Department: 186-Physics Position Summary: The Department of Physics seeks qualified individuals for its Adjunct Faculty Pool and welcomes applicants at any time. Available courses vary from semester to semester and include both laboratory and lecture courses. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and other duties which vary with specific courses. Minimum Qualifications: A Master’s degree in Physics or a closely related discipline is required. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Daytime and/or evening hours required. Special Message to Applicants: The Department of Physics will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications. All applicants must apply on line and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. 3. Statement of Teaching Philosophy. Posting Date: 07/20/2023 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,160.00 – $2,230.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other If your answer to the above question is \"Referred by a current employee\", please specify the full name of the employee below-only one name may be provided. (If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A) (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Transcripts Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
