    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34109": {
      "title": "Football Video Assistant - Creative/Photography",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Football Video Assistant - Creative/Photography Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Football Video Assistant - Creative/Photography To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20255600V Position Title: Football Video Assistant - Creative/Photography Posting Type Student Hours/week: 20 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2025-2026 Academic Year Location Andrew J. Talley Athletic Center Detailed Work Schedule Hours vary. Number of positions: 2 Department: 738-Football Contact Name: Joan McGuckin Contact Phone/Extension: 7787 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Assist the Football Staff with creative/social media (graphic design, video, photography) for practices and games. Requirements: Must be an enrolled Villanova student. Additional Information: Experience with Adobe Photoshop/Premiere Pro is encouraged but not required. Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $10.00/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest © 1990-20