    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36589": {
      "title": "Late Night Operations Manager -Donahue Market/Second Storey",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Late Night Operations Manager -Donahue Market/Second Storey Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Late Night Operations Manager -Donahue Market/Second Storey To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. SCHEDULE during normal operating hours: Friday/Saturday 2pm -1am Sunday/Monday 3pm – 2am Off Tuesday/Wednesday/Thursday Must be flexible with scheduling based on needs of operation and special events. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260463S Position Title: Late Night Operations Manager -Donahue Market/Second Storey Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 412-Dining Services Operations Position Summary: Founded in 1842 and recognized among the nation’s best colleges and universities, we are a mission-driven institution inspired by the values of truth, unity, love, and dedication to serving the common good. At Villanova, we believe our people are our most precious asset. That’s why we offer a vibrant and collaborative campus environment and invest in our employees through competitive compensation and comprehensive benefits that support your professional growth, personal well-being, and long-term success. Benefits include: • Generous paid time off and holidays • Tuition assistance for employees and eligible family members • Professional development opportunities • Retirement savings plan with University contributions • Well-being programs and resources • Flexible work options where appropriate We invite you to join a community where your contributions are valued, your growth is supported, and your work makes a meaningful difference. Learn more about the benefits of working at Villanova on our website. The Late Night Operations Manager will be responsible for the operation of 2nd Storey Convenience Store/Donahue Market. This includes but is not limited to: financial reporting, ordering, personnel management, sanitation, marketing, merchandising, product mix, vendors relations, and conducting inventory. Assists the General Manager in meeting and or/exceeding financial targets. This person will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the value of the Villanova Mission Statement and the Dining Services Mission Statement. This person will focus on our Core Values : Safety and Sanitation, Friendly Courteous Service, Quality, Meticulous Attention to Detail, and Safety. All of our associates should improve our systems and overall operation. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Personnel - Responsible for the supervision, hiring, scheduling, training, and termination of the staff for the store. Coordinates training of employees. Responsible for employee morale and friendly courteous service. Maintains the payroll for the full and part time associates and student staff. This includes updating and monitoring time, sick time, holiday and vacation. Provides supervision and coverage of the dining hall when required. Responsible for monitoring employees’ adherence to scheduled shifts and follow-ups with associates. Conducts weekly meetings with staff. Responsible for yearly evaluation of employees. Financial - Responsible for the timely processing of all invoices and C-Bords requisitions, daily revenue reports, maintain proper Grub Hub procedures, Operates point of sale registers. Manages in order to meet and/or exceed financial targets. Ordering/Inventory- Proper ordering procedures are followed for all vendors, proper inventory levels are maintained on store shelves, maintains and updates Cbord order books with correct par levels, inventories for ordering are conducted routine and monthly inventory compilation is done once a month. Product Mix - ensures that the correct product mix is being offered, seeks student and staff feedback, track industry trends and benchmarks within the local area and markets. Attends Retail Operations committee meetings. Responsible for the Micros computer menu management and product pricing. Runs daily and monthly product reports to track sales and compare to purchases. Marketing and Merchandising- Develops marketing and special promotions for both stores. Works with the GM and webmaster master in developing advertising for stores. Ensures that both stores are well merchandized and decorated. Food Safety and Sanitation- supervises food prep and production. Maintains accurate production sheets and temperature logs. Ensures that all products are wholesome and all product produced on premises are produced following our food safety and sanitation guidelines. Routinely inspects operations for board of health violations and regulations. Enforces safety and sanitation policies and procedures including daily, weekly, and monthly cleaning assignments. NONESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Monitors and ensures that all equipment and records are maintained in the unit. Monitors preventative maintenance contracts on equipment and pest elimination. Arranges for outside contractors for equipment maintenance and repairs. Coordinates maintenance and custodial issues. Perform additional duties and assists with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal education: High school diploma with 4 years of experience in food service fields. A 2 or 4 year degree preferred. Current ServSafe Certification preferred Specific Job Knowledge: Basic knowledge of food service safety and sanitation experience Work Skills: Demonstrates basic reading and writing proficiency needed to complete daily tasks. Maintains excellent personal hygiene and consistently adheres to established uniform and appearance standards. Follows instructions accurately and completes assigned responsibilities in a timely and dependable manner. Communicates clearly and appropriately with team members, customers and supervisors. Works independently with minimal supervision while maintaining accountability for quality and accuracy. Interacts effectively and respectfully with others in a dynamic, customer-facing environment. Equipment Knowledge: Basic knowledge of operating kitchen equipment and their functions. Ability to set up, operate, break down, and clean. Must possess the ability to properly use knives, slicer, soft serve machine, and pizza ovens. Preferred Qualifications: Serv Safe Certification, preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery, and equipment used: Knives, oven warmers, and grill and serving line Environmental conditions: Ability to use chemicals daily as required, and use proper protective equipment as called for by the specific chemical and task Physical requirements : Minimum lifting requirement of 30 pounds or more Standing for extended period of time Special Message to Applicants: SCHEDULE during normal operating hours: Friday/Saturday 2pm -1am Sunday/Monday 3pm – 2am Off Tuesday/Wednesday/Thursday Must be flexible with scheduling based on needs of operation and special events. Posting Date: 10/16/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: The approved range for this position is $59,800-66,900. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity.” Salary Grade: 14 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
