    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36569": {
      "title": "Personal Trainer",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Personal Trainer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Personal Trainer To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260280V Position Title: Personal Trainer Posting Type Student Hours/week: 2-8 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: N/A Department: 775-Athl - Intramurals Contact Name: Julia Gale Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-6561 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Help Villanova community members achieve their fitness goals through one-on-one training sessions and customizedprograms for all fitness levels. Requirements: CPR / AED NCCA Accredited CPT Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $38.00/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
