    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/26917": {
      "title": "STOVS - Mathematics Teacher",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | STOVS - Mathematics Teacher Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us STOVS - Mathematics Teacher To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2022951F Position Title: STOVS - Mathematics Teacher Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Work Schedule: temporary Department: 702 - Center for Access Success and Achievement Position Summary: Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. STOVS Math Instructor position is designed to teach college-level math (Calc & Stat) to students in the STOVS summer bridge program. The instructor will help prepare students for college math by focusing on important math concepts and practices that will enhance their understanding and abilities to solve mathematical problems at the collegiate level. The instructor will provide daily instruction for 2-hours a day, administering in-class assignments, take-home assignments, practice quizzes, and tests as needed. Duties and Responsibilities: Performs a variety of skilled duties to provide Math instruction and assistance to students with the goal of creating an optimal environment for student learning. • Instruct Math classes throughout the program (Monday- Friday 10am-12pm). • Host office hours as needed • Attend and participate in planning and feedback meetings. • Provide updates to STOVS director and professors regarding student concerns and needs. • Be available for student questions and concerns via email throughout the program Minimum Qualifications: • Must be available from July 6 – August 19, 2022 • Must have a strong background in Math. • Advanced knowledge of material in introductory Statistics, and Calculus I. • Experience and comfort in teaching students • Excellent interpersonal skills to relate easily & effectively with students and faculty. • Knowledge of issues of difference in higher education, particularly educational equity. • Use initiative to organize and follow through with complex tasks to meet deadlines. • Proven ability to use MS Office Suite and Adobe Acrobat. • Possess traits of good judgment that align with the University’s mission. • Employment subject to satisfactory background check. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 08/29/2022 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
