    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36470": {
      "title": "Zero Waste Coordinator",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Zero Waste Coordinator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Zero Waste Coordinator To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260287V Position Title: Zero Waste Coordinator Posting Type Student Hours/week: up to 20 hours per week (flexible) Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Villanova Stadium Detailed Work Schedule Flexible work schedule with most of time spent doing field work throughout campus. Number of positions: 4 Department: 801-FS - Trash Collection Contact Name: Albert Motel Contact Phone/Extension: 6105194466 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Student Recycling Coordinator will assist the Waste & Recycling Manager with various day to day operations. Responsibilities: Provide maintenance and updates to content on Villanova Recycling and Grounds Department websites as needed Support the Student Sustainability Committee ( SSC ) by attending group meetings as a representative from Villanova Recycling Research existing and available waste & recycling technologies and programs to evaluate potential of implementation on Villanova’s campus. Compile data and information for annual State and County recycling reports, or other reports as necessary. Provide support for campus sustainability events as needed. Conduct inventory of waste/recycling bins and signage throughout campus. Participate in and assist with organizing waste audits throughout campus to measure effectiveness of program and help identify opportunities for improving operations. Assist in leading, guiding, and training students, and/or volunteers working on campus recycling efforts. Outreach to campus community and other recycling offices on college campuses. Meet with or speak to other organizations regarding recycling initiatives and operations on campus. Requirements: Professional interest in sustainability, recycling, and campus engagement Strong desire to learn and enthusiasm for environmental education. Big picture thinking with creative ideas for student engagement. Organized, willing to take initiative, think and act proactively to solve problems and assess priorities, and manage a variety of tasks calmly and effectively. Experience making presentations and proposals, as well as presenting. Ability to work well independently and in a team setting Experience leading groups, organizing events, and managing large scale programs. Preferred: proficient with Microsoft office suite, Adobe Creative Cloud applications, and AEM authoring. Willing to train the right candidates. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: The job regularly requires walking or standing for several hours on a routine basis, or lifting of moderately heavy items or boxes (up to 40 pounds). Wage Rate: $13.00/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * Please explain what interests you about this position. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe in detail how your background and experience would be applicable for this position in a College/University setting. (Open Ended Question) * Are you proficient in all Microsoft Office products, including Excel, Power Point and Front Page? Yes, in all Yes, but on a limited basis Limited experience No eperience with Excel, Power Point and /or Front Page * Which School/College are you enrolled in at Villanova? College of Liberal Arts and Sciences Villanova School of Business College of Engineering College of Nursing School of Law * What is your class year? Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior None of the above * Please describe yourself and your work characteristics? (Open Ended Question) Do you have experience with maintaining or creating webpages? If yes, please describe (Open Ended Question) * Do you have experience with social networking, e-communication or interactive marketing in a business, academic or non profit environment? Yes, in all Yes, but on a limited basis No Are you proficient in Microsoft Excel? Yes No Do you have experience using Adobe Suite and/or Canva to design marketing materials? If so, please describe. (Open Ended Question) * Are you comfortable with lifting equipment that is at least 30lbs? Yes No Maybe How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the