    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35674": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Research Fellow- Lepage Center Fellow 2026-2027",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Undergraduate Research Fellow- Lepage Center Fellow 2026-2027 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Undergraduate Research Fellow- Lepage Center Fellow 2026-2027 To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260210V Position Title: Undergraduate Research Fellow- Lepage Center Fellow 2026-2027 Posting Type Student Hours/week: Average of 10 hours per week Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location St. Augustine Center Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 1 Department: 972-Lepage Center Contact Name: Kevin Fox Contact Phone/Extension: 6105194280 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Students majoring or minoring in History or Communications are invited to apply to be a Lepage Center Fellow at the Albert Lepage Center for History in the Public Interest for the 2026-27 academic year. The Lepage Center aims to bring historical scholarship and perspective to bear on contemporary events. The undergraduate fellow will work with the Center Director, the Assistant Director, and the Lepage graduate student fellow(s). Duties include: Plan and facilitate programs and events; Assist with marketing and promotion on the Hindsights blog and social media; Identify and communicate with undergraduate student clubs and groups to promote the Center; Attend weekly meetings; Other duties as assigned. One student fellow will be selected for the entirety of the academic year. Duties will be performed on dates that the university is open, and classes are in session, throughout the entirety of the fall 2025 and spring 2026 semesters. Students must meet Villanova, Pennsylvania and U.S. requirements for eligibility and receipt of payment. The selected fellow will work 10 hours per week (on average). Requirements: Students are required to be entering their junior or senior year at Villanova University. Students majoring or minoring in History (including Art History) or Communications are preferred. To be considered for the fellowship, please upload your resume and a one-page cover letter in this application. The undergraduate student fellow will formally apply to the position through Villanova University’s online recruitment system. The student will be interviewed by the Director and Assistant Director. Human Resources will coordinate onboarding and collect all required employment documentation. Additional Information: The fellow is strongly encouraged to apply to earn academic credit through the Ellis Center for Undergraduate Students (formerly OUS ). To earn academic credit, the accepted student must complete the online OUS Internship application . Once completed and accepted by this program, the student will be enrolled in HIS 2993, the three-credit History internship course, with grading and assignments designated by the appropriate faculty member of the History Department. For more information about the credits, please contact Kathryn Szumanski, Ellis Center Director of Professional Development kathryn.szumanski@villanova.edu Letters of recommendation are not required, but we do ask for the names of two History professors that can serve as references. Questions for about the position, the application, and the Lepage Center should be directed to Lepage Center Assistant Director Kevin Fox at lepage@villanova.edu Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $15/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 07/23/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * Please provide the information of two people we can contact as references for you. (Name and contact information) (Open Ended Question) * What is your class year? Freshman Sophomore Junior Senior None of the above * When are you expecting to graduate? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36218": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Research Assistant - 2026-2027 Internship",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Undergraduate Research Assistant - 2026-2027 Internship Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Undergraduate Research Assistant - 2026-2027 Internship To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260186V Position Title: Undergraduate Research Assistant - 2026-2027 Internship Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10-20 Eligibility: Work Study ONLY Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Drosdick Hall Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 2 Department: 204-Electrical and Computer Engineering Contact Name: Moeness Amin Contact Phone/Extension: 6105194363 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Center for advanced Communications, Colllege of Engineering, is offering a 2026/2027 internship for ECE major undergraduates to workin the Radar Lab, Drosdick 006. The work entails learning how to operate mmWave radar, conduct and participate in experiments, processing the data and interpreting the results using signal processing and machine learning. The internship supports around 10-15 hours a week with $15/hour. Please, contact Dr. Moeness Amin moeness.amin@villanova.edu if you are interested. Requirements: Attention to detail; able to follow directions; science major preferred, but not required. Previous lab experience a plus. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: 15.00 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 04/28/2027 Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
