    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36537": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor Specialization in Computational Communication",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Tenure Track Assistant Professor Specialization in Computational Communication Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Tenure Track Assistant Professor Specialization in Computational Communication To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All application materials will be collected online at https://jobs.villanova.edu . We will begin reviewing and will favor completed applications received on or before November 15, 2026 . Required materials include a cover letter, CV, 3 letters of recommendation, graduate school transcripts, sample publication(s), research statement, teaching philosophy, and summary of teaching evaluations. Finalists will be asked to submit a statement on their contribution to Villanova’s mission, reflecting on how their teaching, research, and service contributes to the University’s value orientation as discussed in the University’s statement on its mission and enduring commitments, found here: https://www1.villanova.edu/university/president/about-university.html For more details about the Communication Department’s undergraduate and graduate programs, as well as our faculty and staff, please consult our department webpage . Please direct all questions regarding the position to Dr. Qi Schlupp: qi.schlupp@villanova.edu . Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260081F Position Title: Tenure Track Assistant Professor Specialization in Computational Communication Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 145-Communication Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Department of Communication at Villanova University seeks applicants for a tenure-track position in Computational Communication at the rank of Assistant Professor to begin Fall 2027. With one of the largest undergraduate majors in the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences, the Department of Communication offers courses leading to the B.A. in Communication with opportunities to specialize in eight different areas of the discipline. The Department offers both a M.A. in Communication and a graduate certificate in Strategic Communication. Our faculty value excellence in teaching and research and seek applicants who can contribute to our supportive, collegial work environment. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: The teaching load is 2-2 the first year of the appointment and 3-2 beginning in the second year, with a focus on quantitative communication research methods and specialized electives. Candidates will be expected to pursue an active program of research in one or more of the areas indicated above. In support of this, Villanova offers the opportunity to apply for a semester-long sabbatical in the fourth year. Service responsibilities include student advising and mentoring, curriculum development and assessment, and other service meaningfully related to the candidate’s specialization and research interests. Minimum Qualifications: Successful applicants will have a terminal degree in Communication (Ph.D.), or allied discipline. ABD will be considered with degree completion by August 2027. They should demonstrate an active, theoretically grounded research agenda utilizing quantitative computational social science and big data analytics to investigate human communication processes, media ecosystems, and/or message dynamics. We welcome candidates working across core, applied, or interdisciplinary fields of communication and associated areas of inquiry, such as health, environment, and sports. Applicants must possess demonstrated technical expertise in one or more of the following areas: · Computational Text Analysis & NLP in Communication · Network Science & Digital-Trace Communication Data · Algorithmic & Machine Learning Approaches · Human-AI & Algorithmic Interaction · Emerging Computational Methods: Other advanced data science, artificial intelligence, or quantitative methodologies applied to communication phenomena not listed above Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: All application materials will be collected online at https://jobs.villanova.edu . We will begin reviewing and will favor completed applications received on or before November 15, 2026 . Required materials include a cover letter, CV, 3 letters of recommendation, graduate school transcripts, sample publication(s), research statement, teaching philosophy, and summary of teaching evaluations. Finalists will be asked to submit a statement on their contribution to Villanova’s mission, reflecting on how their teaching, research, and service contributes to the University’s value orientation as discussed in the University’s statement on its mission and enduring commitments, found here: https://www1.villanova.edu/university/president/about-university.html For more details about the Communication Department’s undergraduate and graduate programs, as well as our faculty and staff, please consult our department webpage . Please direct all questions regarding the position to Dr. Qi Schlupp: qi.schlupp@villanova.edu . Posting Date: 10/08/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 11/15/2026 Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Summary of Teaching Evaluations Transcripts Writing Sample/Publications Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document Other Document (2) Statement of Contribution to Mission © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33440": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Engineering Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Engineering Entrepreneurship Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Engineering Entrepreneurship To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Ignite Your Career at Villanova University! Whether undergraduate or graduate, faculty or staff, each community member brings with them a wealth of experiences that enrich our University and shift our perspectives. As a part of this community, your work will improve lives and ignite change! Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2023 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. We believe that an inclusive community fosters an understanding and appreciation for diversity among our students, faculty, staff and administrators. The Office of Diversity, Equity and Inclusion works to address issues of equity and justice in a variety of ways including workshops, events and employee resource groups Villanova’s most precious asset is our people. Even as a part-time employee, you will receive access to certain benefits, including tuition assistance and more . Please submit your applications at: http://jobs.villanova.edu . Application packages must include: Curriculum Vitae, Academic transcripts Statements on teaching philosophy The names and contact information of three references The review process is ongoing and will accept application throughout the year. As teaching vacancies arise, submitted applications will be considered. To learn more about our Engineering Entrepreneurship programs, please visit our website . Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20251253F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Engineering Entrepreneurship Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 201-Dean-Engineering Position Summary: The College of Engineering seeks qualified individuals for its adjunct faculty pool to teach classes in support of the Engineering Entrepreneurship program. The courses in the minor focus on a variety of topics including opportunity identification, technical and market feasibility, prototyping, and business and venture planning. Qualified individuals would provide instruction in both a lecture and hands-on workshop format. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching undergraduate level courses. Engineering Entrepreneurship with specific focus on Creativity and Innovation, and Social Entrepreneurship. Duties will vary with the specific courses being taught. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree required. The applicant must be committed to instilling the entrepreneurial mindset in engineering education. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience preferred. Expertise in Mission-driven business and or Social Enterprise is preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Ignite Your Career at Villanova University! Whether undergraduate or graduate, faculty or staff, each community member brings with them a wealth of experiences that enrich our University and shift our perspectives. As a part of this community, your work will improve lives and ignite change! Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2023 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. We believe that an inclusive community fosters an understanding and appreciation for diversity among our students, faculty, staff and administrators. The Office of Diversity, Equity and Inclusion works to address issues of equity and justice in a variety of ways including workshops, events and employee resource groups Villanova’s most precious asset is our people. Even as a part-time employee, you will receive access to certain benefits, including tuition assistance and more . Please submit your applications at: http://jobs.villanova.edu . Application packages must include: Curriculum Vitae, Academic transcripts Statements on teaching philosophy The names and contact information of three references The review process is ongoing and will accept application throughout the year. As teaching vacancies arise, submitted applications will be considered. To learn more about our Engineering Entrepreneurship programs, please visit our website . Posting Date: 07/21/2025 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,650.00 – $2,600.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: N/A Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
