    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36409": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Physics",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Physics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Physics To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu/ . In addition to a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of research interests, and statement of teaching philosophy, the applicant is asked to submit a statement on their contributions to Villanova University’s mission and enduring commitments. The University mission can be found here: https://www1.villanova.edu/university/president/about-university.html . The applicants should also arrange for three confidential letters of reference to be submitted on their behalf directly through this site. For finalists, official graduate and undergraduate transcripts will be required. Review of applications begins November 15, 2026 and continues until the position is filled Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260075F Position Title: Tenure-Track Assistant Professor in Physics Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 186-Physics Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Department of Physics at Villanova University invites applications for tenure-track Assistant Professor positions beginning in Fall 2027. We are seeking outstanding teacher-scholars to establish an innovative, externally-funded research program and to engage students as active participants in that research. The successful candidates will demonstrate strong potential for excellence in both teaching and scholarship and a commitment to contributing to the intellectual community of the department and university. We seek candidates whose research can complement and expand existing strengths in the department and provide compelling opportunities for student research. Applications in alignment with the Department’s strategic goal to expand strengths in quantum science and photonics are especially encouraged. Exceptional candidates in other areas of physics that would similarly strengthen the Department and strategic vision will also be considered. The Villanova Physics Department has active research programs in condensed matter physics, biological physics, photonics and quantum optics, and astrophysics and cosmology. Our faculty pursue research in a collaborative environment that emphasizes the integration of scholarship and undergraduate education. Students have opportunities to participate directly in faculty research programs, including through sustained research experiences and senior research projects. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: In addition to maintaining an active research agenda leading to publication, our new colleague will teach undergraduate courses in his/her area of expertise, as well as other departmental courses, in a way that fosters connections across the discipline and the Villanova community. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. is required as well as outstanding research potential and excellence in teaching. Preferred Qualifications: Post-doctoral experience in Physics or a closely aligned field is preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu/ . In addition to a cover letter, curriculum vitae, statement of research interests, and statement of teaching philosophy, the applicant is asked to submit a statement on their contributions to Villanova University’s mission and enduring commitments. The University mission can be found here: https://www1.villanova.edu/university/president/about-university.html . The applicants should also arrange for three confidential letters of reference to be submitted on their behalf directly through this site. For finalists, official graduate and undergraduate transcripts will be required. Review of applications begins November 15, 2026 and continues until the position is filled Posting Date: 09/21/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 5 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Statement of Contribution to Mission Optional Documents Other Document Summary of Teaching Evaluations Transcripts Writing Sample/Publications Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
