    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35418": {
      "title": "Athletics Study Hall Monitor",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Athletics Study Hall Monitor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Athletics Study Hall Monitor To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260239V Position Title: Athletics Study Hall Monitor Posting Type Student Hours/week: 6-18 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Andrew J. Talley Athletic Center Detailed Work Schedule Study Hall Monitors generally work 1-3 evenings per week, Sundays-Thursdays, from 3:45 pm-10:15pm. Monitors must be available to work the entire six-hour shift. Number of positions: 2-3 Department: 727-Athl - Administration Contact Name: Chuck Davis Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-7723 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Study Hall Monitors oversee Mandatory Study Hall and tutoring sessions in the Andrew J. Talley Athletic Center and report to the Office of Academic Support for Athletics. They are responsible for monitoring the facility, supervising students and tutors, and enforcing rules. Requirements: Specific Duties and Responsibilities: Oversee all student-athletes and tutors in study hall and maintain a quiet study environment Maintain accurate attendance records in the computer tracking system Monitor all tutor sessions taking place in the center Enforce study hall rules and follow proper protocol to report incidents Communicate regularly with the Academic Support for Athletics staff Implement necessary fire, safety, and evacuation protocol Secure building and facility space upon opening and closing hours Perform other duties as assigned Preferred Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Work well with individuals from diverse backgrounds Ability to use creative problem solving skills Strong leadership, organizational, and communication skills Preferred willingness to learn basic NCAA rules Additional Information: The Mandatory Study Hall Program provides a quiet area for varsity student-athletes to study or meet with tutors. Student-athletes that fall below a minimum grade point average are required to complete a designated number of study hall hours each week. Graduate or law students Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $15/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 06/30/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have another job on campus? If yes, how many hours per week? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
