    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36484": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Mathematics - Tenure Track",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Mathematics - Tenure Track Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Assistant Professor of Mathematics - Tenure Track To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applications are to include: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Copies of academic transcripts (undergraduate and graduate). Three professional references (four maximum). At least one should be able to address the candidate’s disciplinary expertise, and at least one reference should have seen the candidate deliver or design classroom instruction. References will be contacted via email to submit confidential letters of recommendation when the application is submitted. Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests For finalists, an official graduate transcript and a statement of contribution to Villanova’s Mission and Enduring Commitments will be required. An email will be sent to your references with a secure web link asking that they submit confidential letters of recommendation. Review of applications begins upon receipt and continues until the position is filled. We invite you to apply by November 1, 2026, for full consideration. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260079F Position Title: Assistant Professor of Mathematics - Tenure Track Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 185-Mathematics & Statistics Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Department of Mathematics and Statistics at Villanova University invites applications for two tenure track positions in Mathematics with the rank of Assistant Professor. The positions begin in August 2027. The teaching load is 12 credits for the first year, with a standard load of 15 credits per year thereafter. Candidates from all areas of Mathematics, Applied Mathematics, and related fields, such as Operations Research and Financial Mathematics, are invited to apply. For one position, preference will be given to candidates with research interests broadly in applied math. Join a dynamic group of mathematicians with research interests spanning applied and theoretical fields! Our program features a robust undergraduate major in mathematics, a well-established MA in Mathematics, and an undergraduate minor. We run a highly-successful program of faculty-mentored undergraduate research that is supported by an endowment. Graduates of our program pursue further studies in mathematics, or a related field, or enter careers in industries including healthcare, business, sports, consulting, and education. Our department currently has 46 full-time faculty members in mathematics and statistics. Villanova values excellence in teaching, supporting it through teaching development and grant opportunities as well as small class sizes. The department, known for its collegiality, provides a caring and inclusive community in which faculty and students of all backgrounds can learn and succeed. Further information can be found at https://math.villanova.edu . Villanova is located 12 miles west of Philadelphia, which is the nation’s sixth largest city and home to many historical and cultural attractions. There is easy access to the Philadelphia International Airport and to nearby cities such as New York and Washington, DC both by highway and by rail. More information about Villanova and its location is available on the Villanova website at https://www1.villanova.edu/university.html . Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teach mathematics courses at the introductory, upper, and graduate levels. Establish and maintain a research program in your area of expertise. Be an active member of the department, the Villanova community, and the profession. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. (completed before Fall 2027) in mathematics, applied mathematics, or a related field. Commitment to excellence in both teaching and research. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: All applications are to include: Cover letter. Curriculum vitae. Copies of academic transcripts (undergraduate and graduate). Three professional references (four maximum). At least one should be able to address the candidate’s disciplinary expertise, and at least one reference should have seen the candidate deliver or design classroom instruction. References will be contacted via email to submit confidential letters of recommendation when the application is submitted. Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests For finalists, an official graduate transcript and a statement of contribution to Villanova’s Mission and Enduring Commitments will be required. An email will be sent to your references with a secure web link asking that they submit confidential letters of recommendation. Review of applications begins upon receipt and continues until the position is filled. We invite you to apply by November 1, 2026, for full consideration. Posting Date: 09/25/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 4 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33424": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty – Classical Studies",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty – Classical Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty – Classical Studies To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications must include the contact information for 3 references who will be contacted for finalists only. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2021804F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty – Classical Studies Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/9-months Department: 133-Classical Studies Position Summary: Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Classical Studies for undergraduate and/or graduate (M.A.) courses. The specific courses involved may vary from semester to semester (e.g., Latin and/or ancient Greek language at all levels, Latin and/or ancient Greek literature, Greek and/or Roman history/culture). The applicant must be committed to excellence in teaching. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and related duties will vary with the specific course(s) being taught. Graduate (M.A.) courses will be taught either online or simulcast (campus and online). Minimum Qualifications: Candidates must have an M.A. in Classics and be working towards a Ph.D. in Classics or related field. Candidates must have teaching experience. Preferred Qualifications: Ph.D. in Classics. For graduate (M.A.) courses, experience teaching online. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Applications must include the contact information for 3 references who will be contacted for finalists only. Posting Date: 06/22/2021 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,160.00 – $2,230.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: N/A Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Summary of Teaching Evaluations Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
