    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34120": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Research Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Undergraduate Research Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Undergraduate Research Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20255450V Position Title: Undergraduate Research Assistant Posting Type Student Hours/week: up to 20 hrs/wk Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2025-2026 Academic Year Location Off-Campus Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 1-5 Department: 960-Center for Resilient Water Systems Contact Name: Linda DeAngelis Contact Phone/Extension: 6105194960 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Villanova Center for Resilient Water Systems is hiring student interns to assist with off campus stormwater monitoring, field testing, and laboratory testing and analysis. The position supports ongoing stormwater management research as part of PennDOT’s I-95 Girard Avenue Interchange Reconstruction Project. The student intern would complete lab and/or field work to support stormwater sampling and flow and soil measurements. Laboratory work includes soil classification testing, data management and analysis, maintaining a safe and clean lab, and preparing samples and equipment. Field work may include assisting graduate students with maintaining field sites, collecting samples, installing/maintaining equipment, and infiltration testing. Requirements: Attention to detail, able to follow directions: science or engineering major preferred. Previous lab experience a plus. Critical thinking skills in order to work safely in the lab and field. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Must be willing to complete repetitive tasks in the lab and/or field and stand for extended periods of time. Must be able to work in uncomfortable field conditions such as extreme temperatures, humidity, and/or rain. Must be able to lift at least 50 pounds. Wage Rate: $15/hr. Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35714": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant Professor Positions in Neuroscience",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Tenure Track Assistant Professor Positions in Neuroscience Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Tenure Track Assistant Professor Positions in Neuroscience To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications will be reviewed until the position is filled. However, to maximize the chances of success, all required elements of applications should be received by September 15, 2026. All applicants must submit the following required documents: • Cover letter/Letter of application • Curriculum vitae (CV) • Statement of research interests • Statement of teaching philosophy • Copy of graduate transcript • Copies of representative publications • Three letters of recommendation. Three letters of recommendation are required. Each recommender will receive an email invitation from the application system, prompting them to submit their letter directly to the system. Important to note that these emails will not be sent until after you have submitted your application, by uploading a cover letter and CV (under the category of “Required Documents”). Your statement of research interests, statement of teaching philosophy, copy of your graduate transcript (unofficial acceptable), and copies of representative publications are also required. However, they are listed below in the category of “Optional Documents”, which gives you the option to upload these documents after submission of the cover letter and CV. Of note, your application will not be reviewed until all required components have been submitted. Again, we recommend that all required elements be submitted by September 15. Other documents in support of your application (e.g., teaching evaluations, syllabi) are optional and must be submitted directly to the portal as “Optional Documents”. If you experience issues with the application portal, please contact the search committee at benjamin.sachs@villanova.edu. An official graduate transcript, a statement on anticipated contributions to the university’s mission and enduring commitments, and other materials will be required from finalists for the position. About the University: Founded in 1842, Villanova University has a total enrollment of about 10,500 students of whom approximately 7000 are full-time undergraduates in one of four colleges: Liberal Arts and Sciences, Engineering, Nursing, and Business. Most of the rest are enrolled in graduate programs in one of the above four colleges or in the School of Law. Location and Accessibility: Villanova University is located approximately 12 miles west of Philadelphia, PA, in the heart of Philadelphia’s suburban “Main Line” area. It is readily accessible by car and by public transportation. The campus is located about a quarter of a mile from the Villanova/St. Davids exit of I-476, a major component of the Philadelphia area expressway system. Villanova is connected to Philadelphia and to suburban communities to the west by a SEPTA (Southeastern Pennsylvania Transportation Authority) bus line and by the R5 regional rail line which has a station on campus. Another rail line, SEPTA’s Norristown High Speed Line, with two stations on campus, connects Villanova with suburban communities to the north and to the south. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260057F Position Title: Tenure Track Assistant Professor Positions in Neuroscience Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 143-Psychological and Brain Sciences Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . THE DEPARTMENT OF PSYCHOLOGICAL AND BRAIN SCIENCES at VILLANOVA UNIVERSITY invites applications for TWO TENURE TRACK POSITIONS ( ASSISTANT PROFESSOR ) in NEUROSCIENCE to begin in August 2027. Candidates must have a Ph.D. in Neuroscience, Psychology, or a closely related discipline and should have the ability to generate a high-quality research program using non-human model systems and a commitment to teaching in our undergraduate and graduate (M.S.) programs, including mentorship of Master’s theses in our rigorous, research-oriented program. We seek candidates whose research, teaching and service has prepared them to contribute to our commitment to excellence of our academic community. For more information about our department and programs, visit http://psychology.villanova.edu. Applications must be submitted at https://jobs.villanova.edu and must include a cover letter, curriculum vita, three letters of recommendation, and other supporting documents as detailed on the application website. An official graduate transcript, a statement on anticipated contributions to the University Mission and Enduring Commitments, and other materials will be required from finalists for the position. Review of applications will begin on September 15, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. The search committee may be contacted by email at benjamin.sachs@villanova.edu. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: • Establish and maintain a high-quality research program leading to publication in respected outlets. • Contribute to the department’s teaching efforts, establishing skillful classroom teaching and student mentoring. Teaching responsibilities likely will include Introductory Psychology, Biopsychology, and other assignments determined by faculty member interests and department/program needs. • Provide formal and informal academic advisement to students in accordance with department standards. • Be an active member of our department, college and university. Minimum Qualifications: Candidates must have earned, or be near completion of, a Ph.D. in Neuroscience, Psychology, or a closely related discipline, with proven achievement or clear aptitude for excellence in research and teaching. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Applications will be reviewed until the position is filled. However, to maximize the chances of success, all required elements of applications should be received by September 15, 2026. All applicants must submit the following required documents: • Cover letter/Letter of application • Curriculum vitae (CV) • Statement of research interests • Statement of teaching philosophy • Copy of graduate transcript • Copies of representative publications • Three letters of recommendation. Three letters of recommendation are required. Each recommender will receive an email invitation from the application system, prompting them to submit their letter directly to the system. Important to note that these emails will not be sent until after you have submitted your application, by uploading a cover letter and CV (under the category of “Required Documents”). Your statement of research interests, statement of teaching philosophy, copy of your graduate transcript (unofficial acceptable), and copies of representative publications are also required. However, they are listed below in the category of “Optional Documents”, which gives you the option to upload these documents after submission of the cover letter and CV. Of note, your application will not be reviewed until all required components have been submitted. Again, we recommend that all required elements be submitted by September 15. Other documents in support of your application (e.g., teaching evaluations, syllabi) are optional and must be submitted directly to the portal as “Optional Documents”. If you experience issues with the application portal, please contact the search committee at benjamin.sachs@villanova.edu. An official graduate transcript, a statement on anticipated contributions to the university’s mission and enduring commitments, and other materials will be required from finalists for the position. About the University: Founded in 1842, Villanova University has a total enrollment of about 10,500 students of whom approximately 7000 are full-time undergraduates in one of four colleges: Liberal Arts and Sciences, Engineering, Nursing, and Business. Most of the rest are enrolled in graduate programs in one of the above four colleges or in the School of Law. Location and Accessibility: Villanova University is located approximately 12 miles west of Philadelphia, PA, in the heart of Philadelphia’s suburban “Main Line” area. It is readily accessible by car and by public transportation. The campus is located about a quarter of a mile from the Villanova/St. Davids exit of I-476, a major component of the Philadelphia area expressway system. Villanova is connected to Philadelphia and to suburban communities to the west by a SEPTA (Southeastern Pennsylvania Transportation Authority) bus line and by the R5 regional rail line which has a station on campus. Another rail line, SEPTA’s Norristown High Speed Line, with two stations on campus, connects Villanova with suburban communities to the north and to the south. Posting Date: 07/16/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Statement of Teaching Philosophy Writing Sample/Publications Transcripts Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents Other Document Summary of Teaching Evaluations Other Document (2) Statement of Contribution to Mission © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
