    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36539": {
      "title": "Senior Project Manager",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Senior Project Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Senior Project Manager To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260456S Position Title: Senior Project Manager Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 806-Project Management Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Senior Project Manager proactively manages the planning, design, and construction efforts necessary to implement projects of varying size and complexity, including new construction, major renovations, and smaller capital and maintenance projects. The Senior Project Manager performs project management duties with a high degree of independence and limited oversight and manages multiple projects concurrently, including large, phased, or otherwise complex projects and work in occupied facilities. The Senior Project Manager is responsible for planning and implementing assigned projects, including preparing Requests for Proposals (RFPs), supporting contract execution, and coordinating the selection of design professionals, consultants, and contractors. These responsibilities include proactively managing scope, schedule, budget, quality, safety, risk, and communications; anticipating issues; developing and recommending solutions; and communicating decisions and project status clearly to University leadership and stakeholders. The Senior Project Manager also mentors less experienced project management staff and supports the development of departmental standards and procedures. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Project Planning, Design & Construction Management. Manages assigned capital and maintenance projects through planning, design, bidding, construction, closeout, and occupancy. Responsibilities include projects of varying size and complexity, from smaller renovation and maintenance projects to major renovations, infrastructure improvements, and new construction. Capital Planning, Budgeting & Project Initiation. Leads early planning for assigned projects and supports University departments in the development of annual capital budget requests. Develops preliminary project scopes, cost estimates, schedules, phasing plans, and feasibility assessments. Coordinates field investigations and conceptual studies and advises University leadership and stakeholders on project priorities, risks, options, and tradeoffs before design initiation. Design & Consultant Management. Manages the programming and design phases of assigned projects. Develops consultant procurement strategies and manages architects, engineers, legal counsel, and specialty consultants through Requests for Proposals, selection, contract execution, and design. Reviews drawings, specifications, estimates, and schedules for alignment with project objectives, applicable codes, permitting requirements, University standards, and available funding. Supports the AVP Planning, Design, & Construction and the Director of Capital Projects in preparing for presentations to authorities having jurisdiction, regulatory agencies, community groups, and other external stakeholders, including assembling documentation, coordinating consultant input, and preparing presentation materials. Bidding, Procurement & Contract Administration. Leads competitive bidding and procurement activities in coordination with Procurement and in accordance with University policies. Develops bid and contracting strategies; prepares and reviews bid packages, construction contracts, purchase requisitions, and related procurement documentation; and manages clarifications, negotiations, and recommendations for award. Evaluates contractors and vendors based on qualifications, cost, schedule, risk, and project requirements. Construction Management & Field Coordination Manages the construction phase of assigned projects, coordinating contractors, vendors, consultants, campus partners, and occupants to ensure timely and successful project delivery. Monitors construction progress, quality, safety, and schedule performance and proactively addresses issues affecting scope, cost, operations, or schedule. Provides on-site field oversight as required and leads coordination for phased work in occupied facilities. Financial Oversight, Change Management & Project Closeout Develops and monitors project budgets, forecasts, commitments, expenditures, and contingency use. Reviews and processes contractor and vendor invoices and evaluates and recommends approval or disapproval of change orders to the AVP Planning, Design, & Construction and the Director of Capital Projects. Maintains required project documentation and contract records and identifies emerging budget or schedule risks for timely resolution. Coordinates project closeout activities, including commissioning, occupancy, as-built documentation, training, warranties, and final financial reconciliation. Stakeholder Communication & Project Reporting Manages project communications and provides clear, timely, and accurate status updates to University stakeholders throughout the project lifecycle. Communicates project scope, schedule, budget, decisions, risks, and anticipated impacts. Ensures stakeholders understand upcoming activities, required decisions, and changes affecting project delivery or campus operations. Escalates significant issues to University leadership with appropriate background and a recommended course of action. Team Leadership & Departmental Support Mentors and supports less experienced project management staff and provides project-based guidance, technical review, and assistance with issue resolution. Supports consistent project management practices, document standards, reporting, and process improvement across the department. Assists the AVP Planning, Design, & Construction and the Director of Capital Projects with capital planning, special initiatives, and presentations to University leadership and governing bodies as assigned. Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelor’s degree in Civil, Electrical, or Mechanical Engineering, Architecture, Construction Management, or a closely related field is required. Equivalent technical training, knowledge, and at least 15 years of progressively responsible experience in design and construction may substitute for a technical degree. Professional licensure or project management certification is preferred. Specific Job Knowledge Advanced knowledge of construction materials and techniques and working knowledge of building envelope, structural, plumbing, electrical, HVAC , and life-safety systems. Demonstrated experience in construction contract administration and in managing complex, phased, and occupied-facility projects. Minimum Work Experience 10+ years of progressively responsible experience in the planning, design, budgeting, estimating, procurement, and construction of capital projects. Experience managing complex institutional or commercial projects with significant budget, schedule, stakeholder, or regulatory requirements is required. Higher education experience is preferred. This experience must include independent management of all phases of projects from programming and design through bidding, construction, commissioning, closeout, and occupancy. Must be well-versed in the design process, construction methodologies and procedures, codes, and project management principles; able to solicit, evaluate, and negotiate estimates, bids, and cost proposals; proficient in managing project budgets and schedules; and able to read and interpret design and construction contracts and contract documents, including drawings, specifications, payment applications, and change orders. Equipment Knowledge Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Microsoft Excel, Microsoft PowerPoint, Bluebeam, and project management and scheduling software is required. Familiarity with database programs, Autodesk AutoCAD, and Autodesk Revit is preferred. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Work outside with moderate exposure to weather, noise, dust and other conditions typical of construction projects. Walking, bending, reaching, climbing ladders, and ability to lift up to 50 lbs. Occasionally attend and/or support meetings or presentation outside of normal working hours. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 10/09/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 19 and the range is $135,000-150,000. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 19 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Do you posses a Bachelor's degree in Civil, Electrical, or Mechanical Engineering, Architecture, Construction Management, or a closely related field or Equivalent technical training, knowledge, and at least 15 years of progressively responsible experience in design and construction? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have 10+ years of progressively responsible experience in the planning, design, budgeting, estimating, procurement, and construction of capital projects? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have Proficiency in Microsoft Word, Microsoft Excel, Microsoft PowerPoint, Bluebeam, and project management and scheduling software is required. Familiarity with database programs, Autodesk AutoCAD, and Autodesk Revit is preferred? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
