    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35996": {
      "title": "Ticket Office Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Ticket Office Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Ticket Office Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260319V Position Title: Ticket Office Assistant Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Detailed Work Schedule Weeknight and weekend athletic events. Number of positions: 12 Department: 728-Athl - Ticket Office Contact Name: Eryn Schultz Contact Phone/Extension: eschul03@villanova.edu Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: In accordance with established policies and procedures, the Ticket Office Assistant provides exceptional customer service in person at the ticket office on game days for events hosted by Villanova Athletics. Answer customer inquiries and process ticket sales via walk-up orders. Responsible for daily reconciliation of ticket sales and payments. Other assignments may include but are not limited to the compliance pass entrance, will-call distribution and scanning operations. Perform other tasks as assigned by the Ticket Office staff. Requirements: Experience in an in-person customer service position. Familiarity with MS Office applications (Word/Excel). Applicants should be dependable, punctual and possess effective communication and problem solving skills, as well as strong attention to detail. Must have a customer-friendly personality and project a positive image of the University and the Athletics Department to fans, donors, staff, students, alumni, and other groups. Must be able to multi-task and work in a fast-paced environment. Must be able to work weeknights and weekends as needed for events, including working all home football games. Must have reliable transportation to and from athletic events. Additional Information: Athletic ticketed sports throughout the 2026- 2027 seasons include: Football, Volleyball, Women’s and Men’s Basketball, and Men’s and Women’s Lacrosse. 1-2 years customer service experience preferred but not required. Please attach a resume, cover letter and a copy of your VU Class Schedule. Physical Demands Summary: Some jobs require lifting, extensive walking and/or lengthy periods of standing along with exposure to both natural (i.e. weather) and event (i.e. music/crowd volume) related elements Wage Rate: $11.25 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * I understand that satisfactory attendance in all academic classes is required to maintain student employment at Villanova University. Yes No Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Other Document Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36415": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Research Assistant – Lung Transplant Research Study",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Undergraduate Research Assistant – Lung Transplant Research Study Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Undergraduate Research Assistant – Lung Transplant Research Study To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260398V Position Title: Undergraduate Research Assistant – Lung Transplant Research Study Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Driscoll Hall Detailed Work Schedule Flexible. Mostly remote. 10 hours per week. At least two semesters, prefer 12 months. Number of positions: 3 Department: 948-Nursing-Research & Innovation Contact Name: Koons, Brittany ( please add as job approver) Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-7127 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Research Assistant will work with Dr. Koons and the research team on an NIH -funded study focused on improving outcomes for lung transplant patients and their caregivers. This position offers undergraduate students hands-on experience with clinical research, including participant recruitment, longitudinal data collection, and research team collaboration Requirements: • Recruiting, screening, enrolling, and consenting caregiver participants • Taking a lead role in conducting study visits with patients and caregivers • Administering study measures and collecting research data in accordance with study protocols • Entering and maintaining study data in a database • Participating in weekly research team meetings • Assisting with other research activities as needed Research Assistants will receive training and mentorship in clinical research procedures and have opportunities to contribute to research presentations, abstracts, and publications. This position is particularly well suited for students interested in gaining experience in clinical and behavioral research, nursing, healthcare, psychology, public health, or related fields. Additional Information: o Undergraduate students in nursing, psychology, biology, or another health- or behavioral-science-related field o Strong communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills o Reliable, detail-oriented, and able to work independently and collaboratively o Comfortable interacting professionally with patients and caregivers o Ability to maintain confidentiality and follow research protocols o Commitment of approximately 10 hours/week for at least two semesters, preferably 12 months Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: 15.00 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
