    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33254": {
      "title": "Athletic Trainer Certified (ATC)",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Athletic Trainer Certified (ATC) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Athletic Trainer Certified (ATC) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20210326T Position Title: Athletic Trainer Certified (ATC) Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: temporary Approximate Number of Hours per Week 30-40 Department: 733-Athletics - Training Room Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Villanova University Athletics has immediate opening for an Athletic Trainer Certified ( ATC ). Under the license of our Team Physician, assist the Assistant Athletic Director for Sports Medicine in all activities related to the delivery of health-care to our varsity student-athletes (sports assigned by Assistant Athletic Director for Sports Medicine), which includes working cooperatively and in conjunction with the Strength & Conditioning Staff. Design, implement and supervise appropriate treatment and rehabilitation programs for student-athletes, by maximizing and individualizing integrated training programs to achieve desired outcomes. Perform all duties in compliance with all rules, regulations, and bylaws of the NCAA , associated Conferences, and University relating to the conduct and administration of the program. Duties and Responsibilities: * Responsible for the coordination and supervision of the delivery of health care to assigned programs. * Responsible for all phases of health care. * Design and implement treatment and rehab programs for time-loss and surgical rehab cases. * Assist with the implementation of the Athletics Department Drug Testing Program. * Serve as a liaison between Sports Medicine staff and Strength & Conditioning staff regarding rehabilitation programs. * Assist in the management of external accounts, including pharmacy and Physical therapy. Serving as liaison with the Health Center and outside medical practices associated with the care of varsity student athletes. * Responsible for the daily electronic medical documentation for all student-athletes. * Assist with the daily operation and maintenance of the athletic training facility. * Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned by the Director of Sports Medicine. Minimum Qualifications: * Bachelor’s Degree in sports medicine/athletic training or related field; current NATABOC certification; Pennsylvania Athletic Training Class A Certification required by start date. * Current CPR / AED Certification. * At least 1 year athletic training experience including preventive, evaluative, and rehabilitative skills. * Must have knowledge of health care insurance issues and drug testing protocols. * Must have extensive experience with post-surgical rehabilitation. Experienced with therapeutic modalities and rehabilitative equipment. * Ability to keep good records, including S.O.A.P. notes, daily rehab updates, and injury reports and proficiency with personal computer applications necessary. * Excellent communication skills. * Ability to demonstrate and instruct during rehab and functional training protocols. Preferred Qualifications: Experience working with field hockey, volleyball, tennis, swimming and/or rowing at collegiate level a plus. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Available to work flexible hours including nights, weekends, and possible travel. Special Message to Applicants: EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: 02/01/2021 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $40/hr Job Classification: exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as: • Any person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and • Such contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU. Examples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following: • Parents/Legal Guardians • Coaches (high school, college, club) • Personal/Skills Trainers • Relatives • Strength Coach • Advisors Consistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any: • Basketball (men’s or women’s) prospective student-athletes (grades 9-12) or their parents, relatives or coaches? Y N Yes No * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as: • Any person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and • Such contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU. Examples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following: • Parents/Legal Guardians • Coaches (high school, college, club) • Personal/Skills Trainers • Relatives • Strength Coach • Advisors Consistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any: • Current VU basketball (men’s or women’s) student-athletes? Y N Yes No Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36594": {
      "title": "Student Success Specialist",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Student Success Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Student Success Specialist To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260454S Position Title: Student Success Specialist Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 129-A&S Office for Undergraduate Students Position Summary: The Student Success Specialist serves as the primary operational and administrative liaison for the Ellis Center’s Office for Student Success. Reporting to the Director, this role oversees daily office operations, coordinates program logistics, and guides students, families, faculty, and staff through university policies, confidential processes, and support resources. Key Responsibilities Administrative & Process Management: Execute end-to-end documentation and compliance for Leaves of Absence (medical and non-medical), Attendance Verifications, Student Concerns, Faculty Feedback, Academic Standing, and Withdrawals. Draft and issue official correspondence, including Leave letters and tri-annual Academic Standing notifications under the Associate Dean’s direction. Data Analysis & Reporting: Collect, analyze, and present semesterly and annual data across all caseload areas to track trends, identify vulnerable student populations, and inform strategic planning and outreach. Student Success Coaching & Outreach: Provide follow-up coaching and multi-channel outreach to referred students, monitoring progress on action plans, re-engaging unresponsive students, and facilitating warm handoffs to campus resources. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Administrative Liaison & Communication Hub: Serve as the primary operational point of contact for the Office for Student Success, delivering high-level administrative support to faculty, advisors, students, families, and campus partners. Manage the CLAS Student Success shared email inbox by triaging high-volume, confidential inquiries, independently exercising judgment to prioritize responses, and escalating complex or urgent matters to the Director and Associate Dean. Student Concern & Faculty Feedback Triage: Oversee the Slate Student Success Concern and Faculty Feedback workflows. Log, document, and track faculty, staff, and family referrals, initiating timely outreach and intervention strategies for at-risk students. Attendance Verification Management: Review, evaluate, and approve excused absence documentation in accordance with university policy. Draft and issue confidential notifications to faculty and advisors while maintaining compliant, meticulous record-keeping. Support the Director in administering the confidential Medical and Non-medical Leave of Absence processes for CLAS students. Serve as the secondary point of contact for students requesting, returning from, or inquiring about a leave of absence coordinated by the Office for Student Success or the Dean of Students. Coordinate communications among university offices involved in the leave process, including the Registrar, Counseling Center, Dean of Students, Athletics, and other campus partners. Prepare and distribute confidential correspondence, facilitate student deactivation and reactivation processes, coordinate registration PIN distribution to advisors, and ensure faculty, advisors, and students receive timely communication throughout the leave process. Coordinate the Academic Standing process three times annually under the direction of the Ellis Center Leadership. Prepare committee materials in collaboration with the Ellis Center advising team, organize Academic Standing Committee meetings, prepare and distribute individualized academic standing notifications, coordinate the academic standing appeal process, and verify the accuracy and timely delivery of all communications. Due to strict university deadlines, this responsibility may require extended hours during peak periods. In collaboration with the Director and Assistant Director(s), coordinate and manage educational programming for students, faculty, and staff that promotes student success, academic resilience, and effective navigation of university resources and policies. Coordinate the University Withdrawal process by serving as the primary administrative contact for students considering withdrawal from the University. Meet with students to explain university procedures, discuss available resources and alternative pathways to degree completion when appropriate, prepare withdrawal documentation, and distribute official correspondence while maintaining confidentiality throughout the process. Provide administrative and operational support to the Director, including scheduling meetings, drafting correspondence, maintaining departmental records, responding to inquiries received through the office phone and general email account, providing reception desk coverage as needed, and training and supervising graduate assistants supporting data collection, office operations, and programming initiatives. In collaboration with the Ellis Center team, develop, maintain, and improve data collection processes across multiple platforms supporting retention, persistence, and student success initiatives. Perform other duties and assist with projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelor’s degree required. Work Experience Two to three years of progressively responsible administrative or student services experience in a confidential, fast-paced environment, preferably in higher education or a student-facing setting requiring independent judgment, complex coordination, and frequent interaction with diverse constituencies. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Exceptional written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills with the ability to communicate professionally, tactfully, and compassionately with students, families, faculty, staff, and university administrators. Demonstrated ability to build collaborative working relationships while maintaining the highest standards of confidentiality, professionalism, and customer service. Excellent organizational, time management, and project coordination skills with the ability to manage multiple competing priorities, respond effectively to changing demands, and consistently meet critical deadlines. Demonstrated ability to independently prioritize work, exercise sound judgment, recognize and escalate urgent or high-risk student concerns, and maintain accuracy while managing a high volume of confidential communications, shared inbox correspondence, and student records. Demonstrated ability to exercise discretion, sound judgment, and emotional intelligence when interacting with students experiencing academic, personal, financial, medical, or other life challenges. Ability to remain calm under pressure, assess the nature and urgency of student concerns, provide compassionate and solution-focused customer service, and connect students and families with appropriate university resources while maintaining confidentiality and professional boundaries. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities, adhere to strict administrative deadlines, interpret and communicate university policies, and exercise sound judgment when handling sensitive and confidential student information. Experience working in a higher education environment is preferred. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with exceptional attention to detail and accuracy in record keeping, data management, and document preparation. Ability to analyze information, identify trends, and support data-informed decision-making related to student success initiatives Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Strong working knowledge of Microsoft Office Suite, including Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Experience with or the ability to quickly learn student information and case management systems such as Banner, Slate, Maxient, Argos, Power BI, and other university data management platforms. Knowledge of student records management, FERPA , confidentiality standards, and administrative processes within a higher education setting is preferred. Equipment Knowledge Proficiency in operating personal computers and standard office equipment. Experience using Microsoft Office applications, Banner, Slate, Maxient, Argos, Power BI, and other student information and data management systems. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: n/a Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 10/07/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 10/22/2026 Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 13 and the range is $52,000-65,100. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 13 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Transcripts © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36580": {
      "title": "General Cook II",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | General Cook II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us General Cook II To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The schedule for this role varies. This is based on events of the Inn. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260149S Position Title: General Cook II Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 507-Inn at Villanova University Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The General Cook II performs a variety of task including, but not limited to food prep, grill cooking, cleaning and sanitation of kitchen area with minimal supervision. This person has in-depth knowledge of food safety and sanitation under guidelines set by The Inn at VU. This person works with chefs, managers and other staff to ensure the success of the Inn. All team members should improve our systems and overall operation. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Work assigned areas such as main kitchen, buffets, action stations, etc. Ability to identify needs for various stations, with minimal supervision. This includes small ware needs, equipment needs and settings, portion controls, and overall quality of ingredients. 2. Follow recipes and produce food items as assigned by Chefs. Maintain proper food temperatures and appearance of food. Record and maintain food production records. Be responsible for gathering ingredients, utensils, pots, pans and food from walk-ins and freezers for preparation of product. 3. Clean and sanitize equipment including but not limited to hoods, ovens, grills, floors, walls, hot trucks, kettles, prep tables, broilers, char broilers and other cleaning task as assigned by chefs/ managers. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES 4. Work special functions if requested. 5. Ability to lead the kitchen team without Manager presence. Additional duties as assigned by chefs/managers that may include utility and pantry duties. Minimum Qualifications: POSITION SPECIFICATIONS : Formal Education: (e.g., degree) High School Graduate or Formal GED Current Serve Safe Certification (a plus) Specific Job Knowledge: (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) In-depth knowledge of food service safety and sanitation procedures. Minimum Work Experience: (type and number of years) Must have at least three years of basic food service experience. Work Skills: (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Ability to read and interpret recipes and adjust scale to yield requirement Practices excellent personal hygiene habits; follows and adheres to uniform standards daily. Basic communication skills. Ability to work with minimal supervision. Ability to interact with people on a constant basis. Equipment Knowledge: In-depth knowledge of operating commercial kitchen equipment and their functions. Ability to set-up, operate, break down and clean. Ability to properly use knives, slicer, ovens and other equipment as directed by chef/managers. Working Conditions/Environment: (conditions, if known, which may impact the incumbent working in this position) Tools, machinery and equipment used: Knives, oven, grill, fryer, slicer, broiler, rational oven, dish machine, floor cleaning machines such as wrangler. Environmental conditions: (any unusual/adverse conditions such as exposure to chemicals, noise, illumination, air quality, weather exposure etc.) Ability to use chemicals daily as required. Will use proper protective equipment as called for by the specific chemical and task. Physical requirements: (items such as lifting, pushing, pulling, standing or sitting for extended periods of time, manual dexterity, walking etc.) Ability to lift up to 40 pounds independently, sit stand for extended periods, push/pull up to 40 pounds independently, use various chemicals Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The schedule for this role varies. This is based on events of the Inn. Posting Date: 10/05/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $18.98 per hour / shift differential added for qualifying shifts updated LS on 7/22 Salary Grade: 9 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a High School Diploma or equivilent? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have at least three years of basic food service experience? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have 3 years experience in catering? (Open Ended Question) * Are you able to work nights and weekends (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
