    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35752": {
      "title": "Information Technology Technician I - Learning Space Support",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Information Technology Technician I - Learning Space Support Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Information Technology Technician I - Learning Space Support To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260272V Position Title: Information Technology Technician I - Learning Space Support Posting Type Student Hours/week: 5 - 10 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Detailed Work Schedule Emphasis is placed on availability for the following shifts: M-F, 7:00 am – 10:00 am M-Th, 4:30 pm – 7:00 pm Sat, 8:30 am – 1:00 pm, as needed; Cabrini availability is highly valued. Transportation between campuses available based on Shuttle schedule. Other availability will be considered. Number of positions: 17 - 22 Department: 289-UTS - Classroom Technologies Contact Name: Evan Dorsey Contact Phone/Extension: x95219 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Learning Space Student Technicians are the main source of audiovisual assistance for professors and presenters in teaching and learning spaces. The main responsibilities of these technicians entail: Ensuring uninterrupted learning space operations by responding to hotline inquiries with immediate, high-priority phone and in-person support. Collaborating with full-time staff to deliver comprehensive technical support to faculty, staff, and the broader university community. Assessing, resolving, and documenting learning space service requests, incidents, and tasks within the ticketing system to ensure accurate records. Facilitating efficient setup and real-time support for learning space technology to keep academic schedules on track. Diagnosing and resolving hardware and software malfunctions during active instruction and between classes to minimize downtime. Ensuring long-term hardware reliability by maintaining accurate asset records and performing routine functional systems testing and preventive maintenance. Gaining hands-on experience with technical projects involving the deployment, maintenance, and optimization of specialized audiovisual software and hardware. Requirements: Preferred candidates will possess the following skills: Excellent written and oral communication skills, particularly in contexts of customer service; the ability to handle potentially challenging situations. Excellent interpersonal skills, specifically the ability to cultivate positive work relationships. Working knowledge of multimedia equipment operation and interfacing. Well-developed problem-solving skills. High degree of adaptability. Working knowledge of Windows, macOS, Zoom/Teams, and Microsoft 365. Knowledge of HTML5 highly valued. Training provided to ensure job success. Additional Information: The Learning Space Student Technician position comes with responsibilities and sometimes challenging situations, but it prepares students for life after college; it provides the skills, the professional training and the life lessons needed for internal advancement and future fulfilling employment. Exemplary student employees will be recognized and promoted within the team. In preparation for the opening of Cabrini Campus, ATS is increasing its student staff, presenting more opportunities for student employment. This position is technical but not exclusive; students of all majors are welcome to apply. ATS is currently interviewing primarily for Fall 2026 and Spring 2027 ATS focuses on fostering a welcoming work environment where student employees are treated with kindness, dignity, and respect. Physical Demands Summary: Should be able to efficiently walk the campus and carry a laptop. Exceptions and accommodations will be considered on a case by case basis for individuals with documented needs. Lifting, pushing, pulling, standing or sitting for extended periods of time, manual dexterity, etc. Wage Rate: $11.25 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * What is your availability (days, times)? (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
