      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Undergraduate Research Assistant - CHES Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Undergraduate Research Assistant - CHES To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260370V Position Title: Undergraduate Research Assistant - CHES Posting Type Student Hours/week: 20 hours p/week Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Drosdick Hall Detailed Work Schedule Able to work schedule given to student(s) by faculty and/or graduate researchers. Number of positions: 5 Department: 986-Center for Human-Environmental Systems Contact Name: Dr. Wenqing Xu Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-8549 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Center for Human Environmental Systems is seeking motivated undergraduate research assistants to support ongoing sponsored research projects in the areas of environmental engineering, transportation engineering, and materials engineering. Selected candidates will contribute to specific research tasks under the guidance of faculty and graduate researchers Requirements: Must be pursuing a major in science or engineering. Strong attention to detail and ability to follow instructions. Capable of working independently and managing time effectively. Prior laboratory experience is preferred (e.g., general chemistry labs or research projects). Must be 18 years of age or older. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $15/hr. Posting Detail Information Closing Date (1