    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36425": {
      "title": "Dining Supervisor- Cabrini Campus",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Dining Supervisor- Cabrini Campus Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Dining Supervisor- Cabrini Campus To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The start date for this position is on or after June 1, 2026. Schedule during normal operating hours: Tuesday - Friday 6am - 3pm Saturday 7am - 4pm Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260206S Position Title: Dining Supervisor- Cabrini Campus Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 837-Dining Services- Cabrini Campus Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Dining Supervisor directly supervises the daily operation and ensures that daily schedules of activity are established and quality standards are maintained. They will also assume all of the manager’s responsibilities and authority in manager’s absence. This person will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the value of the Villanova Mission Statement and the Dining Services Mission Statement. This person will focus on our Core Values: Safety, Sanitation, and Excellence. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Demonstrates complete understanding of departmental requirements. Monitors daily performance of staff, including the quality of products and service, sanitation, and food handling practices, and also ensures compliance with established standards. Accurately inventories the supplies daily and requisitions items needed to meet par levels. Depending on the unit, may have additional ordering responsibilities. Assists managers with daily schedules and work assignments. Shifts staff to complete essential duties when need arises. Coordinates work of staff to promote efficiency of operations. Trains staff, assists with orientation of new associates, recommends actions necessary for staff discipline, terminations, promotions, and provides input to annual performance. NONESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Responsible for register procedures, including operating the cash register, and running all reports. Monitors customer needs and responds to any concerns or questions in a friendly and courteous manner. Routinely inspects areas of assigned responsibility and reports all substandard safety and sanitation, security, or equipment conditions to the manager. Consistently monitors standards and makes recommendations for change to managers. Performs other duties as assigned (daily/weekly cleaning)-special projects. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: High School diploma required or GED equivalent. Work Experience: 3 years minimum experience in food and/or customer service; combination of post-secondary education/certifications and experience may also be considered. Specific Job Knowledge Background in food service industry including preparation and production and safety and sanitation Equipment Knowledge General knowledge of kitchen equipment such as: slicers, dish machines, ovens, fryers, mixers, knives, etc Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education: ServSafe Certified, preferred Work Experience: 5 years experience in food and/or customer service with at least 1 years in institutional food service, preferred Work Skills: Demonstrated organizational skills with excellent written and oral skills Ability to work with a diverse work force Ability to work in a group Must be self-motivated and able to work with general supervision Ability to teach and train Inventory and ordering skills preferred Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery, and equipment used: Any of the above-mentioned equipment as needed Environmental conditions: Exposure to extremes in temperature Cleaning chemicals Physical requirements: Must be able to lift 10 pounds, up to 30 pounds with assistance Standing and walking for extended periods of time Special Message to Applicants: The start date for this position is on or after June 1, 2026. Schedule during normal operating hours: Tuesday – Friday 6am – 3pm Saturday 7am – 4pm Posting Date: 09/23/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within hourly grade 12 and the range is $23.37 – $26.11/hr. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 12 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a High School Diploma or equivilent? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
