    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36355": {
      "title": "Catering Production and Events Manager - Cabrini Campus",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Catering Production and Events Manager - Cabrini Campus Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Catering Production and Events Manager - Cabrini Campus To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Schedule will vary weekly depending on event needs. Must be flexible. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260272S Position Title: Catering Production and Events Manager - Cabrini Campus Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 838-Cabrini Catering Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Reporting directly to the Director of Catering, the Catering Production & Events Manager is responsible for coordinating, selling, and executing catering and event services for Villanova University’s internal departments and external clients. This position is crucial to ensuring high-quality service standards, supporting campus events and conferences, and driving revenue growth through proactive sales and relationship management. The Catering Production & Events Manager will work closely with various teams to plan, organize, and execute events successfully while maintaining a high level of customer service and satisfaction. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Sales & Client Relations: Act as the contact for catering/event inquiries from internal departments, student organizations, faculty, staff, and external clients. Conduct sales calls, site tours, and client meetings to secure bookings for university event spaces and catering services. Prepare customized catering proposals, pricing estimates, and event contracts in accordance with university policies. Collaborate with clients to understand event objectives, dietary needs, timelines, and budget constraints. Administrative: Complete/Maintain Temporary wait staff and student waitstaff payroll timecards. Assist with entering contracts/BEO’s as needed. Operations/Event Planning & Execution: Work closely with culinary and production teams to create event pull sheets. Assist with bar pull sheets. Manage event logistics, and provide on-site support when needed. Work with customers for event timelines. Build and maintain strong relationships with university departments and external vendors. Promote university dining services at campus events, orientations, and outreach opportunities. Administrative & Financial Management: Complete/Maintain Temporary wait staff and student waitstaff payroll timecards. Assist with entering contracts/BEO’s as needed. Maintain accurate records of sales activities, contracts, payments, and invoices. Ensure all events are billed accurately and payments are collected in a timely manner. Assist with annual budgeting, forecasting, and event revenue tracking. Compliance & University Engagement: Ensure all events comply with campus policies, food safety regulations, and licensing requirements. Build and maintain strong relationships with university departments and external vendors. Promote university dining services at campus events, orientations, and outreach opportunities. Additional Duties: Assist with other tasks and responsibilities as assigned by the Director of Catering, including special projects, event support, and marketing. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: Bachelor’s degree in Hospitality Management, Business, Communications, or related field. Minimum of 3 years of experience in catering sales, event planning, or hospitality, preferably in an educational or institutional setting. Specific Job Knowledge: Strong knowledge of catering sales, event planning, and client management. Familiarity with event management software (e.g., CaterTrax, Tripleseat) and Microsoft Office Suite. Knowledge of food safety regulations and event compliance standards. Minimum Work Experience: Minimum of 3 years of experience in catering sales, event planning, or hospitality, preferably in an educational or institutional setting. Equipment Knowledge: Proficiency with event management software and standard office technology (Microsoft Office, email, etc) Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Ability to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends, based on event needs. Comfortable with walking, standing, and attending events in various indoor and outdoor settings. Special Message to Applicants: Schedule will vary weekly depending on event needs. Must be flexible. Posting Date: 08/07/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 13 and the range is $51,000-63,800. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 13 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
