    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34040": {
      "title": "The Wendy U. and Thomas C. Naratil Endowed Professorship in Oncology Nursing",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | The Wendy U. and Thomas C. Naratil Endowed Professorship in Oncology Nursing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us The Wendy U. and Thomas C. Naratil Endowed Professorship in Oncology Nursing To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications must include: cover letter resume/curriculum vitae statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions support the University’s mission (and enduring principles) and a statement on inclusive excellence are required at time of interview. Contact information for 3 individual references are required for all finalists. Required for appointment: • Official transcripts from undergraduate and graduate degrees. • Evidence of professional liability insurance. • Criminal background check clearance. • FBI fingerprints and PA Child Abuse Clearances. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260018F Position Title: The Wendy U. and Thomas C. Naratil Endowed Professorship in Oncology Nursing Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 232-Nursing Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The M. Louise Fitzpatrick College of Nursing at Villanova University invites applications for the inaugural Wendy U. and Thomas C. Naratil Family Endowed Professorships in Oncology Nursing, a distinguished tenured faculty appointment for a teacher-scholar dedicated to advancing excellence in cancer care through nursing scholarship, education, clinical practice, and leadership. We seek a visionary oncology nursing scholar, educator, and leader with a strong national and/or international reputation who will elevate the College’s impact in cancer research, interprofessional education, and clinical innovation. Supported by dedicated funding, the Endowed Professor will drive transformative research, cultivate interdisciplinary partnerships within the Philadelphia region’s renowned cancer ecosystem, mentor and educate the next generation of nurse leaders, and shape conversations that advance cancer care nationally and globally. The Endowed Professor will teach at the undergraduate and graduate levels within the Fitzpatrick College of Nursing. We also anticipate an affiliation with Fox Chase Cancer Center , an NCI -designated Comprehensive Cancer Center and ANCC -recognized Magnet® hospital based in Philadelphia, PA. Options related to this potential partnership will be discussed with candidates as part of the interview process. The opportunity for collaboration provides a robust clinical and research home to support sustained scholarly and practice excellence. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Lead a nationally and/or internationally recognized program of oncology nursing research. Secure external funding to support innovative research and programmatic initiatives. Publish in high-impact, peer-reviewed journals and present at leading academic and clinical conferences. Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in oncology nursing and related areas. Mentor faculty, postdoctoral fellows, and undergraduate and graduate students in research and professional development. Build and sustain regional and national collaborations that influence oncology practice, policy, and education. Design and launch a forward-looking Oncology Nursing certificate or graduate focus within the Fitzpatrick College of Nursing. Facilitate the development of an Oncology Nursing Consortium with peer Schools of Nursing. Serve in leadership roles within the College, University, and professional organizations. Demonstrate a strong commitment to inclusive excellence in research, teaching, and clincal practice. Establish a robust research program and/or clinical practice through a potential joint appointment at Fox Chase Cancer Center. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: PhD or equivalent terminal degree in Nursing or a related field. Specific Job Knowledge and Skills: Eligibility for RN licensure in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Established national reputation in oncology nursing, evidenced by sustained scholarly productivity, external funding, and professional leadership. A distinguished record of achievement that qualifies the candidate for an appointment at the rank of Professor. Demonstrated excellence in undergraduate and graduate teaching and mentorship. Experience mentoring DNP and PhD students. Strong alignment with the mission and values of the Fitzpatrick College of Nursing, including commitments to holistic health, social justice, and service. Embrace Villanova University’s teacher–scholar model. Preferred Qualifications: Oncology nursing certification (e.g., OCN®, AOCN®, or equivalent). Experience in interdisciplinary, translational, or community-engaged research. Proven record of impactful partnerships with clinical institutions or cancer centers. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Applications must include: cover letter resume/curriculum vitae statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions support the University’s mission (and enduring principles) and a statement on inclusive excellence are required at time of interview. Contact information for 3 individual references are required for all finalists. Required for appointment: • Official transcripts from undergraduate and graduate degrees. • Evidence of professional liability insurance. • Criminal background check clearance. • FBI fingerprints and PA Child Abuse Clearances. Posting Date: 03/09/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Other Document (2) Statement of Contribution to Mission © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35550": {
      "title": "Media Assistant - Undergraduate",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Media Assistant - Undergraduate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Media Assistant - Undergraduate To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260254V Position Title: Media Assistant - Undergraduate Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10-15 hours per week Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Drosdick Hall Detailed Work Schedule | Position begins in the Fall 2026 Semester, 8/24/26 Number of positions: 2 Department: 201-Dean-Engineering Contact Name: Therese Wosczyna Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-3948 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The College of Engineering is seeking two creative and motivated student leaders to collaborate with COE’s Communication & Marketing and Engineering Recruitment teams to develop engaging, year-round social media content. These students will play a key role in showcasing the Villanova Engineering experience through authentic storytelling, event coverage, and student-driven campaigns. Key Responsibilities Create social media content highlighting College of Engineering events, programs, and student experiences. Capture and produce short-form video content (e.g., Instagram Reels, TikTok-style videos, stories). Conduct and feature student interviews, day-in-the-life content, and event coverage. Lead and participate in social media takeovers to provide authentic student perspectives. Identify and develop student-centered content based on social media trends. Work closely with the Communications team to ensure branding consistency and strategic messaging. Attend select campus events and outreach programs to gather content. Qualifications Current Villanova University student. Strong interest in social media, marketing, storytelling, or communications. Experience with content creation tools (e.g., Instagram, TikTok, Canva, Adobe Suite) preferred. Excellent communication and organizational skills. Ability to work independently while collaborating with a team. Creative mindset with attention to detail and brand alignment. Time Commitment Approximately 10 hours per week (flexible based on schedule and event calendar). Benefits Gain hands-on experience in marketing, communications, and digital storytelling. Build a professional portfolio of social media and video content. Work closely with Communications and Engineering leadership. Play a key role in shaping the narrative of the Villanova Engineering student experience. Application must include: Cover letter CV/Resume Three samples of previous related work or what your vision of social media content would look like. Requirements: Undergraduate students at the sophomore level or above Additional Information: Student(s) will be working with Heather Gill Physical Demands Summary: Normal activities (possible lifting of ~20 lbs.) Wage Rate: $13.00/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Other Document Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36157": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, University Advancement Communication (UAC)",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Assistant Director, University Advancement Communication (UAC) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Assistant Director, University Advancement Communication (UAC) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260413S Position Title: Assistant Director, University Advancement Communication (UAC) Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 654 - University Communications and Marketing - Advancement Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people. As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . In close collaboration with the Director, University Advancement Communication, and as a member of the University Advancement Communication ( UAC )leadership team, the Assistant Director of University Advancement Communication is responsible for leading the execution of creative and integrated multi-channel advancement communications for the full spectrum of University fundraising, stewardship and engagement activities across a wide variety of constituencies and donor levels. This includes working with University Advancement staff across campus to oversee a portfolio of advancement communication projects in their assigned University Advancement (UA) areas, including Alumni Relations, Stewardship, Family Engagement and Philanthropy, and Corporate and Foundation Relations, among others. It also includes working closely with the Director to ensure the effective and efficient operation of the UAC department. The Assistant Director manages one Communication Associate, providing day-to-day project support and direction, as well as helping to ensure their projects meet the University’s advancement and strategic goals. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: In close collaboration with the Director, and as a member of the UAC leadership team, the Assistant Director, UAC , is responsible for leading the execution of creative and integrated multi-channel advancement communications for University Advancement. Plans, prioritizes and oversees a portfolio of advancement communication projects in their respective UA areas while building and strengthening relationships with advancement staff across campus, and serves as a leader to support overall advancement communication goals. Manages one Communication Associate in all aspects of project management for a wide range of advancement communication projects to ensure excellence and the successful implementation, coordination and completion of all deadlines, as well as ensuring that advancement and strategic goals are met. The Assistant Director, UAC , will supervise these daily activities, goal setting and overall performance, providing project assistance, guidance, feedback and support. The Assistant Director, UAC , also works closely with the Director to ensure the efficiency and effectiveness of departmental operations, including all project management and communication systems are running to deliver projects on deadline and on budget. Performs other duties and assists with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelor’s degree in marketing, communications or a related field required, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Work Experience Must have 5+ years of relevant communication and marketing experience within an academic, non-profit or business environment. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) This individual must be a team player with strong writing, research, interpersonal, management, organizational and planning skills. Must be a flexible self-starter who enjoys collaboration with a wide variety of constituencies. Must have excellent written and verbal communication, problem solving and decision making skills with the ability to build and maintain excellent internal and external relationships. Must have the ability to handle multiple projects, priorities and deadlines within a fast-paced, multifaceted environment with the ability to work evenings, weekends and possibly holidays as the demands of the job dictates. Must be able to handle confidential information with a high level of discretion. This individual must have a deep commitment to the well-being of the University, a commitment to the University’s Augustinian Catholic heritage, the advancement of its mission and to serving the needs of a diverse community. Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) This individual must have a broad working knowledge of communication and marketing with a proven record of developing, leading. executing and assessing strategic and tactical marketing and communications plans. Must be highly proficient in all standard computer applications, including Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Adobe Acrobat. Equipment Knowledge Personal computers, copiers and other standard office equipment. Preferred Qualifications: Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Experience with direct mail, and/or fundraising and alumni communication is strongly preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Must have the ability to work evenings, weekends and possibly holidays as the demands of the job dictates. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 08/26/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 16 and the range is $71,700-89,600. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 16 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/31033": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Honors",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Honors Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Honors To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Honors Program will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. All applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the following three pieces of information: a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2020711F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Honors Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/10-months Department: 139-Honors Position Summary: Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in the Honors Program for undergraduate courses only. The specific courses involved may vary from semester to semester. The applicant must be committed to excellence in the teaching of their discipline. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and related duties will vary with the specific course(s) being taught. Minimum Qualifications: Advanced degree is required and/or experience suitable for course instruction. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The Honors Program will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. All applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the following three pieces of information: a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: 03/27/2020 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 0 Maximum Number of References Needed 0 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Transcripts Other Document Statement of Teaching Philosophy Summary of Teaching Evaluations Writing Sample/Publications Statement of Research Interests Statement of Contribution to Mission © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
