    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36493": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant Hourly -- Communications and Marketing, Law School",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Graduate Assistant Hourly -- Communications and Marketing, Law School Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Graduate Assistant Hourly -- Communications and Marketing, Law School To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260411V Position Title: Graduate Assistant Hourly -- Communications and Marketing, Law School Posting Type Graduate Assistant Hours/week: up to 20 hours per week Eligibility: Graduate Assistant Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Widger Law School Building Detailed Work Schedule Availability M-F between the hours of 9 and 5, based on applicant’s schedule. Number of positions: 1 Department: 655 - University Communication and Marketing - College Communications Contact Name: Melissa Nyman Contact Phone/Extension: 9-5434 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Graduate Assistant supports the Communications and Marketing team with a variety of projects and responsibilities. Primary duties include gathering content to support web stories and other original content (this may include meeting with and interviewing subjects), managing the production of internal and external newsletters, supporting event communications (website, posters, and other materials), performing routine web edits, helping to manage the team’s inbox and triage requests, attending team meetings, scheduling social media posts, and capturing photos or videos primarily for social media. Requirements: Applicants should have strong project management skills, a commitment to accuracy and attention to detail, and the ability to manage multiple assignments and projects with many connected components. Must be a current full-time graduate student at Villanova. The individual must be highly proficient in all standard computer applications, including Microsoft Word, Excel, PowerPoint and Adobe Acrobat. Additional Information: Preferred but not required: Social media management experience and experience in Canva is a plus. Interest in or experience with writing and story production preferred (such as web profiles and/or social media copy). Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $18.00/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Writing Sample/Publications © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33428": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Accounting",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty, Accounting Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty, Accounting To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Accounting and Information Systems Department will accept applications until position is filled. All applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the the following three pieces of information: a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. 3. Statement of Teaching Philosophy. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, he or she may submit them on line in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2012021F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty, Accounting Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 217-Accountancy Position Summary: Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Accounting for undergraduate and MBA courses. The specific courses involved may vary from semester to semester. The applicant must be committed to excellence in the teaching of accounting. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching specific Accounting courses. Minimum Qualifications: The applicant must be committed to excellence in business education. A master’s degree within a relevant field is strongly preferred. Equivalent experience may be considered. Preferred Qualifications: PhD or terminal degree in a related field or similar professional experience in a related field. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The Accounting and Information Systems Department will accept applications until position is filled. All applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the the following three pieces of information: a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. 3. Statement of Teaching Philosophy. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, he or she may submit them on line in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: 11/19/2013 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,925.00 – $2,505.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed Maximum Number of References Needed Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Transcripts Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34617": {
      "title": "Student Equipment Manager",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Student Equipment Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Student Equipment Manager To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260140V Position Title: Student Equipment Manager Posting Type Student Hours/week: 9-20 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Jake Nevin Field House Detailed Work Schedule Students have the opportunity to choose shifts that fit their schedule. Once shifts are chosen, that schedule will be weekly for the remainder of the semester. We ask that each student choose 3 shifts minimum (9 hours weekly), and that all commit to at least one weekend shift (Friday, Saturday or Sunday) Weekday Shifts (M-F): 9am-12pm, 12pm-3pm, 3pm-6pm, 6pm-9pm Weekend Shifts: 9am-12pm, 12pm-3pm, 3pm-6pm, 6pm-9pm Rotating schedule for Friday and Saturday 6pm-9pm shifts Must be able to work at least one weekend shift, weekly Number of positions: 15 Department: 734-Sports - Equipment Contact Name: Nora Toney Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-5617 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Assist with the daily operations of the athletic equipment room, including receiving and organizing inventory, managing laundry, distributing gear, and maintaining a clean and organized workspace. Support student-athletes, coaches, and staff with equipment needs and help prepare for practices, competitions, and team travel. Requirements: Ability to work in a fast-paced, team-oriented environment Strong attention to detail and organizational skills Reliable, punctual, and able to commit to scheduled shifts Ability to lift/push/pull and move boxes/equipment (up to ~50 lbs) Willingness to perform physical tasks (laundry, stocking, cleaning) Strong communication skills and positive attitude Ability to follow directions and complete tasks independently Flexibility to work evenings and weekends as needed Respect for equipment policies, confidentiality, and team spaces Additional Information: This is a part-time, on-campus student position for the 2026–27 academic year , students must be enrolled in classes at Villanova to be eligible for this position Work schedules are flexible but may include mornings, evenings, weekends, and holidays based on team needs Students must follow all equipment room policies and procedures Training will be provided; no prior experience required Opportunity to work closely with varsity athletic programs and gain hands-on experience in collegiate athletics operations Professional conduct and a team-first attitude are expected at all times Physical Demands Summary: This position requires standing, walking, and moving for extended periods of time. Duties include lifting, carrying, pushing, and pulling equipment and boxes (up to ~50 lbs), as well as frequent bending, reaching, and repetitive motions (laundry, stocking, organizing). The role may involve working in varying temperatures and requires the ability to safely perform physical tasks throughout the duration of assigned shifts. Wage Rate: $10.00 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Do you currently work anywhere else on campus? If so, how many hours per week? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36436": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Research Position",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Undergraduate Research Position Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Undergraduate Research Position To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260408V Position Title: Undergraduate Research Position Posting Type Student Hours/week: up to 20 hrs/wk Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Drosdick Hall Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 1-5 Department: 960-Center for Resilient Water Systems Contact Name: Linda DeAngelis Contact Phone/Extension: 6105194960 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Villanova Center for Resilient Water Systems (also known as the Villanova Urban Stormwater Partnership) is hiring student interns to assist with a floodplain investigation. The position supports ongoing flood field and lab research as part of Dr. Smith’s research group. The student intern would complete field surveys and lab tests to support experiments to deepen the understanding of floodplain function. Requirements: Attention to detail, able to follow directions: science or engineering major preferred. Previous computational experience a plus. Critical thinking skills in order to work safely in the lab and field. Must have a computer and be willing to complete repetitive computational tasks. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $15/hr. Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33412": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Marketing &amp; Business Law - Professional Selling Course",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Marketing &amp; Business Law - Professional Selling Course Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Marketing & Business Law - Professional Selling Course To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Marketing Department will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. All applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the the following three pieces of information: (a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; (b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, he or she may submit them on line in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2017403F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Marketing & Business Law - Professional Selling Course Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: temporary Department: 222-Marketing Position Summary: The Department of Marketing & Business Law in the Villanova School of Business ( VSB ) at Villanova University is seeking applications for an adjunct position in marketing to start January 2018. The course is Professional Selling, and requires considerable business development experience and a passion for teaching Professional Selling to undergraduates. Further information about the department can be found at: https://www1.villanova.edu/villanova/business/departments/marketing_buslaw.html Professional Selling is a required class in the recently added Concentration in Business Development within the Marketing department in VSB . Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching one three credit Professional Selling course. Minimum Qualifications: An MBA or other business-related masters degree from an AACSB accredited institution is required. Preferred Qualifications: Teaching, sales and sales training experience. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The Marketing Department will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. All applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the the following three pieces of information: (a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; (b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, he or she may submit them on line in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: 08/18/2017 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,925.00 – $2,505.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: N/A Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Optional Documents Transcripts © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
