    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35930": {
      "title": "Philanthropy Associate",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Philanthropy Associate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Philanthropy Associate To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260292V Position Title: Philanthropy Associate Posting Type Student Hours/week: 6 hours (minimum) – 20 hours (maximum) per week Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Riley Hall Detailed Work Schedule Flexible scheduling available. Shifts to be completed between 2-7 p.m. Monday-Thursday and 1-3 p.m. on Friday. Number of positions: 5 Department: 608-Development Contact Name: Abby Loranca Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-7938 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Villanova University Advancement is searching for enthusiastic and motivated undergraduate students to join the Student Philanthropy program! Student Philanthropy Associates support the Villanova Annual Fund through both fundraising and stewardship efforts. As an integral member of the UA team, you will establish, develop, and maintain relationships with alumni, family, and friends to secure resources for Villanova’s top priorities across academics, scholarships, student life, and athletics. This opportunity is for students who wish to gain meaningful work experience, develop professional job skills, and gain valuable experience across communications, fundraising, sales, marketing, and customer service. You’ll directly impact the student experience, gain leadership skills, and serve as an ambassador through various programs across Villanova. Duties and Responsibilities: · Reach out to supporters to build personal rapport, update alumni records, and acquire donations for the University · Build a strong, compelling case in support of the Villanova Annual Fund through interactions with prospects via phone calls, emails, and text messages · Serve as an ambassador at events, including 1842 Day and Homecoming · Manage conversations with a high-level of professionalism and handle personal information with confidentiality · Meet performance goals established during each shift · Gain a greater understanding of the University’s mission, goals, academics, student programs, and its needs for philanthropic support Requirements: · Bachelor’s Degree in progress ·Commit to a minimum of six hours per week with variable scheduling available. Shifts to be completed between 2-7 p.m. Monday-Thursday and 1-3 p.m. on Friday. · Excellent relationship-building and interpersonal skills, with the ability to interact comfortably and effectively with internal and external stakeholders · Willing and able to consistently ask for philanthropic support via phone calls, email, and text · Enthusiasm for Villanova and our mission · Ability to record data accurately · Outstanding time management and organization skills · An eagerness to be coached and to learn every day · Persistent and positive attitude Additional Information: · Competitive Wages: Student Philanthropy Associates earn $13.00 per hour · Build your resume: Develop strong fundraising, communication, sales, marketing and customer service skills. · Network: Learn from and build relationships with alumni in various professions across the country · Incentives: Prizes earned for meeting team goals and end-of-semester celebrations. ·Flexibility: Choose your schedule to complete the six-hour weekly minimum. Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $ 13.00 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36360": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Researcher - College of Engineering",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Postdoctoral Researcher - College of Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Postdoctoral Researcher - College of Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Villanova is a Carnegie-classified doctoral university . From its founding in 1842 to its position today as a nationally recognized leading university, Villanova University has forged a path of academic excellence. The University is in the Philadelphia metropolitan area, home to a large concentration of universities, industries, and government labs. Please submit your application at: http://jobs.villanova.edu . Application packages must include: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Academic Transcripts Names and contact information of three references The review process will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260074F Position Title: Postdoctoral Researcher - College of Engineering Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Department: 959-Center for Energy - ES2 Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Center for Energy ES2 in the Mechanical Engineering Department at Villanova University has an opening for a full-time Postdoctoral Scholar position. The Post-Doctoral Researcher will be part of a research team working on advanced liquid cooling systems for high density data centers, with emphasis on two-phase cooling systems that involve flow boiling of refrigerants. Research topics span fundamental areas such as flow boiling in microchannels and complex porous media funded by the NSF ES2 Industry/University Cooperative Research Center, to applications in actual direct-to-chip cooling systems, from chip to rack, in collaboration with major data center industry partners. In addition to conducting individual research, the Post-Doctoral Researcher will be expected to be a research leader to Doctoral and MS researchers. The position will involve significant interaction and networking with industry partners from many major data center companies, providers, and vendors. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: (1.) Initiate research in new and emerging areas of heat transfer and thermal management applied to data center applications (2.) Design experimental apparatus, systems, and instrumentation for two-phase flow and heat transfer (3.) Supervise and participate in the construction and/or assembly of experimental apparatus, systems, and instrumentation (4.) Perform careful, systematic experimental investigations involving scales from microchannels to full rack systems (5.) Develop physics and AI-based models to elucidate physics, perform optimization, and create surrogate models for system level simulators (6.) Participate in weekly meetings and help to prepare reports and presentations for project sponsors. Minimum Qualifications: Requirements include a PhD in Engineering or a closely related field. Experience managing milestone-driven sponsored research projects and communicating effectively with stakeholders Training and experience with two-phase flow and heat transfer with refrigerants, theory and experiments, is mandatory. Experience with hardware development and instrumentation required. Experience with software tools such as ANSYS Fluent, MATLAB , EES , REFPROP , and LabView is required. Excellent organization, communication, and interpersonal skills are prerequisites. Highly motivated, able to work independently and communicate proactively. Preferred Qualifications: Previous or current experience in a relevant industry or a national lab is highly desirable. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Villanova is a Carnegie-classified doctoral university . From its founding in 1842 to its position today as a nationally recognized leading university, Villanova University has forged a path of academic excellence. The University is in the Philadelphia metropolitan area, home to a large concentration of universities, industries, and government labs. Please submit your application at: http://jobs.villanova.edu . Application packages must include: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Academic Transcripts Names and contact information of three references The review process will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Date: 09/15/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Statement of Contribution to Mission Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
