    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/31069": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Villanova Interdisciplinary Immigration Studies Training for Advocates",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Villanova Interdisciplinary Immigration Studies Training for Advocates Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Villanova Interdisciplinary Immigration Studies Training for Advocates To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. * The College of Professional Studies will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the position. * Official Transcripts will be required of all finalists for this position. * Applications must include contact information for 3 references who will be contacted via email to submit confidential letters of recommendation when the application is submitted. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2020693F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Villanova Interdisciplinary Immigration Studies Training for Advocates Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 576-Dean, Professional Studies Position Summary: The College of Professional Studies invites qualified individuals to apply for an Adjunct Faculty position to teach in the VIISTA Program (Villanova Interdisciplinary Immigration Studies Training for Advocates), a 100% online interdisciplinary educational program that trains students to become immigrant advocates ready to serve migrants and refugees. The Program is comprised of three modules. Module 1 focuses on how to successfully work with immigrants and is the foundation for the program. Modules 2 and 3 focus on immigration law and practice and are designed to train people to become Department of Justice ( DOJ ) partially accredited representatives (Module 2), or fully accredited representatives (Module 3). We are seeking instructors for all three modules. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: * Conducting in a professional manner all assigned classes per guidance and policies from the University and College of Professional Studies. * Preparing and submitting accurate and precise student grades and other assigned documents when due. * Regularly assessing formative and summative student work product, assignments, and activities including providing written feedback on Discussion Boards, audio, and video recordings. * Actively engaging in learning community so that the Instructor’s presence is regularly felt by the students. * Building a strong online learning community. * Answering student questions and providing guidance, where appropriate. * Attendance at college-wide meetings and events (virtual or in-person as appropriate). * Supporting and following college policies and procedures. Minimum Qualifications: * Law degree, including experience in immigration law practice. * Committed to excellence in teaching. Preferred Qualifications: * Specific knowledge of Blackboard, Canvas, and other Instructional Design Tools as well as Web Conferencing Tools. * Strong understanding of adult learning principles and theories. * Experience teaching online, particularly in a higher education setting is recommended. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: * The College of Professional Studies will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the position. * Official Transcripts will be required of all finalists for this position. * Applications must include contact information for 3 references who will be contacted via email to submit confidential letters of recommendation when the application is submitted. Posting Date: 02/28/2020 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Contribution to Mission Optional Documents Other Document Summary of Teaching Evaluations Transcripts Writing Sample/Publications Statement of Research Interests Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be