    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36501": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Assistant or Associate Professor in Astrophysics",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Tenure Track Assistant or Associate Professor in Astrophysics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Tenure Track Assistant or Associate Professor in Astrophysics To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu. All applications are to include: * Letter of interest. * Current and complete curriculum vitae. * Statements of research and teaching interests *Names and contact information of three references who will be contacted to submit confidential letters of reference. Finalists will be asked to submit a statement on their contributions to the University Mission and Enduring Commitments. The mission statement they should respond to is to be found here: https://www1.villanova.edu/university/president/about-university.html Inquiries may be directed to Dr. Kelly Hambleton Prsa at kelly.hambleton@villanova.edu. Review of applications will begin on November 15, 2026 with a final deadline of December 1, 2026. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260086F Position Title: Tenure Track Assistant or Associate Professor in Astrophysics Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 182-Astronomy and Planetary Science Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science at Villanova University invites applications for a full-time tenure track position at the rank of Assistant or Associate Professor. Rank will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s record and experience. The appointment will begin in the Fall of 2027. Villanova’s Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science is a standalone department offering undergraduate major and minor degrees in astronomy and astrophysics, with a long tradition of involving students directly in research. Research areas include stellar astrophysics and binary stars, exoplanets and planetary science, near-field cosmology, and time-domain astronomy and is supported by participation in TESS , Gaia, JWST , the Vera C. Rubin Observatory/ LSST and others. Faculty have access to the on-site Villanova Observatory, high-performance computing resources, and membership in external observing consortia. The successful candidate will join a community of scientists and educators who value a wide range of voices, backgrounds, and experiences. We welcome applicants with experience in inclusive teaching and mentoring practices and who will help make astronomy accessible to students from all backgrounds. We are open to candidates working in any subfield of astrophysics or planetary science, and we encourage applicants to articulate how their program would grow at a university of Villanova’s scale. The successful candidate will be expected to maintain an active, externally recognized research program that engages undergraduate students, and to contribute to the department’s academic mission at all levels. Experience with astronomical instrumentation, observatory operations, or planetarium and public-outreach programming would be especially welcome, but not required. Full consideration will be given to strong candidates in any area. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: In addition to maintaining an active research agenda leading to publication, our new colleague will teach undergraduate courses in astronomy, astrophysics, planetary science, physics or their area of expertise, as well as other departmental courses, in a way that fosters connections across the discipline and the Villanova community. Minimum Qualifications: We seek a colleague with a PhD in astronomy, astrophysics, planetary science, physics or closely related field in hand by June 1, 2025 , with at least 2 years of postdoctoral or equivalent experience, who can demonstrate excellence in undergraduate teaching and mentoring students in research. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Located twelve miles west of Philadelphia and an hour and a half by train from New York City, Villanova sits within one of the densest concentrations of research universities, liberal arts colleges and science-education institutions in the country, offering rich opportunities for collaboration and public engagement. Special Message to Applicants: Applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu. All applications are to include: * Letter of interest. * Current and complete curriculum vitae. * Statements of research and teaching interests *Names and contact information of three references who will be contacted to submit confidential letters of reference. Finalists will be asked to submit a statement on their contributions to the University Mission and Enduring Commitments. The mission statement they should respond to is to be found here: https://www1.villanova.edu/university/president/about-university.html Inquiries may be directed to Dr. Kelly Hambleton Prsa at kelly.hambleton@villanova.edu. Review of applications will begin on November 15, 2026 with a final deadline of December 1, 2026. Posting Date: 10/06/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents Other Document Summary of Teaching Evaluations Writing Sample/Publications Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Transcripts Statement of Contribution to Mission © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
