    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33430": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - School of Law",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - School of Law Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - School of Law To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applicants must apply online and include: a letter of interest (including the names and email address for at least 3 references), current curriculum vitae, a statement describing your teaching philosophy, including courses you are interested in teaching, academic transcripts; unofficial transcripts will be accepted to submit application; however, official transcripts are required if you are selected for an interview. Screening of submitted applications begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2021849F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - School of Law Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: temporary Department: 241-Law School Instruction Position Summary: Charles Widger School of Law seeks qualified individuals for its Adjunct Faculty Pool and welcomes applicants at any time. The School of Law offers programs leading to a JD degree. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching law school courses. Duties will vary with the specific courses being taught. Minimum Qualifications: JD degree; must be committed to excellence in law school education. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: All applicants must apply online and include: a letter of interest (including the names and email address for at least 3 references), current curriculum vitae, a statement describing your teaching philosophy, including courses you are interested in teaching, academic transcripts; unofficial transcripts will be accepted to submit application; however, official transcripts are required if you are selected for an interview. Screening of submitted applications begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Posting Date: 09/17/2021 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position has a salary of $1,500.00 per credit hour. This may be pro-rated in the case of team-teaching scenarios where effort is shared. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * What is your area of expertise (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
