    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33414": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Real Estate",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Real Estate Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Real Estate To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Department of Finance will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications. Please indicate your areas of teaching interest and expertise within the specified question in the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2015226F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Real Estate Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: temporary Department: 220-Finance and Real Estate Position Summary: The Department of Finance and the Daniel M. DiLella Center for Real Estate in the Villanova School of Business ( VSB ) invite applications for adjunct teaching positions in commercial real estate for undergraduate and MBA courses taught during the day and/or evening. Openings to teach these courses develop on a periodic basis, depending on department teaching needs. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching specific real estate courses, with a focus on commercial real estate topics Minimum Qualifications: The applicant must be committed to excellence in business education. A master’s degree within a relevant field is strongly preferred. Thorough knowledge of commercial real estate is required. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The Department of Finance will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications. Please indicate your areas of teaching interest and expertise within the specified question in the application. Posting Date: 03/20/2015 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,925.00 – $2,505.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * Briefly list your areas of teaching expertise. (Open Ended Question) * Briefly describe your previous teaching experience. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document Transcripts Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
