    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36263": {
      "title": "Student Manager - IDEA Lab",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Student Manager - IDEA Lab Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Student Manager - IDEA Lab To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260376V Position Title: Student Manager - IDEA Lab Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Falvey Memorial Library Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 6 Department: 100-Provost Contact Name: Kirsten Bronkovic Contact Phone/Extension: - Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Work at the Institute for Innovation & Entrepreneurship ( IIE ) where we serve the university to support, encourage, and accelerate innovative thinking and entrepreneurial endeavors. The IIE is looking for team members to support our events, programming, and resources at the IDEA Lab. 3D Printer Manager Maintain the 3D printer, take inventory of supplies and make ordering recommendations. Help fellow students, faculty and staff with the use of the 3D printers. Hold at least two (2) 3D Printer workshops per semester. Must also hold posted office hours for the Villanova community to book equipment time or time for personalized instruction. Maker Space Manager Maintain Glow Forge, take inventory of all supplies in the Maker Space and make ordering recommendations. Help fellow students, faculty and staff with the use of the Glow Forge or any other equipment, supplies or tools in the Maker Space. Make sure that all tools are operational and that there are enough supplies for Maker Space to operate at full capacity and efficiency. Hold at least two (2) Glow Forge workshops per semester. Must also hold posted office hours for the Villanova community to book equipment time or time for personalized instruction. Idea Lab Manager Maintain physical space of the Idea Lab, including but not limited to watering plants, stocking snacks, playing music, cleaning and straightening tables and chairs both inside and outside of the Lab, tracking and ordering supplies, making necessary catering orders for events. Events Manager Responsible for coordinating speaker logistics and for the Innovator’s Supper Club, IIE tabling events across campus, and serve as point person for Idea Challenge and Villanova Student Entrepreneurship Competition ( VSEC ). Plans team building events, including, but not limited to worker bonding day in the fall, graduation BBQ in the spring. In addition to planning, the Events Manager will actively work at these events. Manager of IIE Events & Programs Promote IIE events and programs ensuring brand-alignment and up to date information. Responsible for at least 1 post per week, mirrored across Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, LinkedIn, and Wildcat Newswire/Campus Currents, as well as populating Idea Lab screens and website with corresponding content. Manager of Entrepreneur Stories Promote IIE student entrepreneurs, their ventures, and alumni entrepreneurs. Responsible for at least 1 post per week, mirrored across Instagram, Facebook, TikTok, LinkedIn, and Wildcat Newswire/Campus Currents. Requirements: Skills in the desired role for which you are applying and an interest in innovation and/or entrepreneurship. Additional Information: TBD Physical Demands Summary: Ability to lift 10lbs Wage Rate: 15/HR Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/32409": {
      "title": "Research Technicians - Educational Development and Assessment",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Research Technicians - Educational Development and Assessment Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Research Technicians - Educational Development and Assessment To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. A unique and exciting opportunity for high school-level educators looking for summer work! This is a non-exempt position, with up to 10-12 hours per week available to the selected candidates. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20240539T Position Title: Research Technicians - Educational Development and Assessment Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: temporary Approximate Number of Hours per Week Department: 205-Mechanical Engineering Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . We are seeking experienced high school teachers to join our research team for an innovative educational development project. The selected candidates will play a crucial role in refining and completing subject-specific content for an immersive online educational program to teach integrated geography, mathematics, and geology through the lens of geologic and dinosaur paleontological work. The research project focuses on the interdisciplinary realm of geosciences, utilizing its unique characteristics to foster integrated learning. Through the creation of an immersive Virtual Field Trip ( VFT ), we aim to increase exposure to geosciences in high school and early college and enhance STEM education by seamlessly integrating subjects such as geography, math, biology, and physics within geoscience applications. The VFT , featuring a virtual paleontology expedition, will be hosted on the American Geosciences Institute’s digital platform, ensuring wide accessibility. Assessment tools, including validated instruments, will gauge the VFT’s impact on student engagement, academic gains, and attitudinal factors. The broader impacts encompass supporting early-career scientists, engaging undergraduate students in hands-on experiences, and disseminating outcomes widely to schools, museums, and beyond. Duties and Responsibilities: Duties and responsibilities include: Collaboration with Principal Investigators (PIs) on the development of specific set of modules for the online program. Refinement and complete subject-specific educational content for the VFT modules. Leveraging curricular expertise to optimize the adaptability of the VFT to existing high school curricula. Aligning learning objectives and educational content to closely meet state and national educational standards. Minimum Qualifications: Required qualifications include: Bachelor’s degree required and other state-mandated teaching certifications. Minimum of one year experience high school teaching in geography, geology, or mathematics. Strong curriculum development skills and familiarity with educational policies and standards. Ability to collaborate effectively with PIs and contribute to the ongoing development of educational modules. Commitment to working during the summer months. Preferred Qualifications: A knowledge of multimedia resources and the ability to incorporate them into online lessons preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: A unique and exciting opportunity for high school-level educators looking for summer work! This is a non-exempt position, with up to 10-12 hours per week available to the selected candidates. EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $26.10/hour Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36557": {
      "title": "Associate Full Stack Developer",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Associate Full Stack Developer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Associate Full Stack Developer To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260343S Position Title: Associate Full Stack Developer Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 723-UTS-Web Services and Technologies Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more The Associate Full Stack Developer supports the design, development, implementation, maintenance, and enhancement of web applications, digital experience platforms, and related web services that support Villanova University’s digital ecosystem. This role contributes across the software development lifecycle while building foundational capability in front-end and back-end development, integrations, cloud-based delivery, deployments, troubleshooting, release support, and platform operations. Under guidance, the Associate Full Stack Developer assists with implementing and supporting scalable, reliable, and maintainable solutions aligned with University standards. Work may include support for Adobe Experience Manager ( AEM ), including AEM as a Cloud Service and AEM Edge Delivery Services; the University website; the University mobile app built on Modo Labs; the University Web Portal built on OneCampus; APIs; analytics and tagging tools; and other related digital services. This position contributes to the reliable operation and continuous improvement of the University’s web and mobile services environment while developing technical depth and practical experience. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Development & Application Support Develop, test, debug, and enhance web application features, components, templates, and related functionality across front-end and back-end technologies. Maintain and update existing applications and digital platform functionality within established architectures, standards, and development patterns. Support assigned development tasks from requirements through implementation while building proficiency in coding standards, testing practices, and reusable approaches. Feature Integration & Technical Implementation Implement and support defined integrations, API connections, and data exchanges under established patterns and guidance from senior team members. Assist with validating, troubleshooting, and refining application behavior related to connected systems and platform features. Contribute to technical implementation tasks that support consistent functionality across applications, services, and digital platforms. Application Maintenance & Issue Resolution Support the maintenance, troubleshooting, and enhancement of applications and digital platform functionality in development, testing, and production environments. Investigate and resolve assigned defects, configuration issues, and user-reported problems with guidance from senior team members when needed. Apply established security, accessibility, performance, and quality practices while helping maintain stable and effective digital services. Team Collaboration & Delivery Support Work with developers, analysts, and stakeholders to support requirements clarification, implementation tasks, testing, and delivery of application enhancements. Collaborate across teams supporting web, mobile, and portal services to complete assigned work effectively and build technical depth through practical experience. Quality, Standards & Continuous Improvement Contribute to testing, documentation, validation, and knowledge sharing activities that support reliable delivery and maintainable applications. Follow established development standards, reusable approaches, and team practices while continuing to build proficiency with development tools, automation, and AI-assisted workflows. Perform other duties and assist with projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelor’s degree or relevant industry certifications (such as AEM and Java) plus relevant years of experience may be considered in lieu of a degree. Work Experience 0-2 years of relavant work experience. Internships, academic projects, personal projects, or technical training that demonstrate foundational web development capability are helpful. Exposure to developing, testing, debugging, or maintaining web applications, websites, or digital platform functionality is beneficial. Exposure to front-end and back-end development in a collaborative software delivery environment is beneficial. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Strong interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills, with the ability to work effectively with both technical and non-technical audiences. Strong organizational, planning, analytical, and problem-solving skills, with attention to detail and the ability to manage assigned work effectively. Ability to work independently on defined tasks while collaborating effectively with team members and stakeholders. Adaptability and willingness to learn new tools, technologies, and development practices in an evolving technical environment. Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Foundational familiarity with web development concepts, browser testing and debugging, and responsive web behavior. Foundational familiarity with front-end technologies such as JavaScript, HTML , and CSS , with exposure to back-end development concepts and modern development tools. Ability to learn how to translate defined requirements into components, pages, features, or functional application updates. Awareness of accessibility, usability, maintainability, SEO , web performance optimization, and general content management system concepts. General awareness of APIs, version control, cloud-based web delivery, and common integration patterns. Other: Commitment to Villanova University’s mission and values, including fostering an inclusive and service-oriented culture. Commitment to continuous improvement, learning, and adoption of new platform capabilities and best practices. Willingness to work outside standard business hours to support critical maintenance or system events. Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education Master’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Information Systems, or a related discipline. Relevant industry certifications such as AEM and Java. Work Experience Experience working within higher education. Hands-on experience in web development, enterprise website support, content management systems, or digital platform implementation is preferred. Experience with Adobe Experience Manager ( AEM ), especially AEM as a Cloud Service, including components, templates, content fragments, and content publishing practices, is preferred. Experience with AEM Edge Delivery Services ( EDS ), React, or other modern front-end development tools and component-based development patterns is preferred. Experience developing, supporting, or configuring mobile app or portal platforms such as Modo Labs or OneCampus is preferred. Experience with APIs, analytics or tagging tools, technical documentation, and accessibility best practices in web development is preferred. Work Skills (e.g., written, and verbal communication skills) Preferred ability to use AI coding assistants and related development tools effectively and responsibly to improve productivity while maintaining code quality, testing rigor, and secure development practices. Interest in or exposure to emerging AI technologies, including AI agent development, workflow integrations, and related tooling. Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Preferred knowledge of SEO , web performance, maintainable web development practices, and analytics or tagging concepts. Familiarity with Google Analytics, Google Tag Manager, and related analytics or tagging tools is preferred. Understanding of Agile methodology, SDLC practices, information security, and WCAG /digital accessibility requirements as they relate to web development. Preferred familiarity with AEM Cloud environments, Edge Delivery Services, modern content delivery concepts, and component-based development approaches. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery and equipment used: Standard office technology, including computer, monitor, keyboard, telephone, and other common business software and collaboration tools. Environmental conditions: ( any unusual/adverse conditions such as exposure to chemicals, noise, illumination, air quality, weather exposure etc.). Work is typically performed in a standard office or hybrid work environment with no unusual exposure to adverse conditions. Physical requirements: (items such as lifting, pushing, pulling, standing or sitting for extended periods of time, manual dexterity, walking etc.) Requires extended periods of sitting and computer use, with occasional standing, walking, and manual dexterity sufficient to operate standard office equipment. May occasionally need to lift computing/office equipment. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 10/13/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 16 and the range is $71,700-89,600. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 16 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * This is a hybrid position that requires on-campus presence. Do you currently live within a commutable distance to Villanova University