    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35562": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor and Director of the Intellectual Property Clinic",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Assistant/Associate/Full Professor and Director of the Intellectual Property Clinic Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Assistant/Associate/Full Professor and Director of the Intellectual Property Clinic To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applications must be submitted online and should include: Application cover letter, Current and complete curriculum vitae, Statement of teaching philosophy, List of 3 references (we will contact the references for finalists only), Unofficial academic transcripts are required to submit the application. Official transcripts will be required from finalist only. Finalists will be required to submit a statement on their contributions to the University Mission and Enduring Commitments. Mission Statement | Villanova University Review of applications begins upon receipt and continues until the position is filled. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260052F Position Title: Assistant/Associate/Full Professor and Director of the Intellectual Property Clinic Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Department: 241-Law School Instruction Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Villanova University Charles Widger School of Law seeks an outstanding lawyer-educator to direct and teach its Intellectual Property (“IP”) Law Clinic. The IP Clinic provides direct representation to entrepreneurs, businesses, and social ventures consistent with the mission of the clinical program, serving client needs in a wide range of intellectual property acquisition, retention, and licensing. Areas of practice may include patent, trademark, copyright and trade secrets, and may include supervision of U.S. P.T.O. certified students engaged in patent and trademark prosecution. Non-patent bar eligible Directors may be asked to work with an adjunct to supervise patent matters. The Director will be a full-time, 12-month continuing non-tenure track (governed by ABA Standard 405©). We anticipate a start date of June 1, 2027. The mission of the Villanova Clinical Program is to teach law students to become competent, reflective, ethical, and creative lawyers committed to seeking justice. Through our teaching and advocacy, we pursue social justice with our clients and surrounding communities by challenging systemic racism, combating inequality, and fostering social change. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teach clinic seminar focused on lawyering skills, professional development, and ethical practice, employing clinical teaching methods. Supervise all aspects of student practice while utilizing clinical teaching pedagogy and serve as the attorney of record in Clinic cases when required by the rules of the relevant jurisdiction. Supervision of student practice may include supervision of U.S. P.T.O. certified students engaged in patent and/or trademark prosecution. Oversee all aspects of administration of the IP Clinic, including but not limited to conducting outreach to clients, selecting matters, reporting to funding sources, and maintaining files. Minimum Qualifications: A Juris Doctor degree is required. Pennsylvania bar membership (or an ability to waive into the Pennsylvania bar) is required. Relevant legal practice experience is required. An understanding of, and commitment to, clinical teaching methodology, including an ability to work both collaboratively and independently, is required. A demonstrated interest and/or aptitude for student supervision and teaching is required. Expertise in substantive areas of law relevant to representing and advising clients in a variety of intellectual property acquisition, retention, and licensing needs is required. Excellent oral and written communication skills are required. Preferred Qualifications: Patent Bar membership is preferred. Prior clinical teaching experience or experience supervising law students is preferred. Five years of legal experience is strongly preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: All applications must be submitted online and should include: Application cover letter, Current and complete curriculum vitae, Statement of teaching philosophy, List of 3 references (we will contact the references for finalists only), Unofficial academic transcripts are required to submit the application. Official transcripts will be required from finalist only. Finalists will be required to submit a statement on their contributions to the University Mission and Enduring Commitments. Mission Statement | Villanova University Review of applications begins upon receipt and continues until the position is filled. Posting Date: 07/06/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Summary of Teaching Evaluations Writing Sample/Publications Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Statement of Contribution to Mission Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36175": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant II",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Administrative Assistant II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Administrative Assistant II To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260084S Position Title: Administrative Assistant II Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/10-months Avg Hours Week 25 Department: 985-French and Francophone studies Position Summary: The Administrative Assistant II will assist the Program Directors of French & Francophone Studies and Italian Studies with overseeing the two undergraduate Programs, including maintaining undergraduate records, overseeing correspondence, and maintaining accurate degree audits, student graduation lists, and assisting with logistical aspects of course registration and advising. Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: French and Francophone Studies and Italian Studies tasks: Assist the two Program Directors with all aspects of the program from application through graduation, including certifying students for graduation; managing accurate degree audits, helping coordinate registration and advising, course overrides; acting as a liaison with the Ellis Center and the Registrar, and other offices as needed. Provide administrative support to faculty, students and student clubs, including helping with grant applications, gathering program statistics and general recordkeeping; helping schedule and plan events; ordering office supplies; keeping the office and utility room orderly; and serving as back-up to communicate with building manager about necessary maintenance. Handle inquiries via phone, email, and office contact throughout the day. Participate in program meetings, including taking the minutes. Oversee the programs’ websites, making necessary adjustments on a regular basis as well as assisting with more significant updates as required by the implementation of new policies or program requirements. Serve as a liaison with other academic programs across the University. Manage social media networks to assure an active presence on all platforms used by the programs to communicate. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education High school diploma or equivalent required. Minimum Work Experience The individual must understand the importance of inclusive education with a desire to work with students, faculty, and staff of varying backgrounds and social identities. General familiarity with Microsoft Office Applications (including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, Teams, and Adobe Acrobat) and software such as Concur. Proficiency in tech applications for helping design and update websites and creating networking feeds on social media. Minimum of 2-3 years related work or internship experience required. Specific Job Knowlege Expertise in MS Office suite required Excellent writing and communication skills; ability to plan, and manage projects and public-facing events; Strong interpersonal and organizational skills; Ability to work effectively with faculty, staff, and students; ability to work collaboratively as a team member; ability to meet deadlines, handle multiple tasks simultaneously and work independently in a visible, fast-paced office environment with numerous interruptions. Experience operating and troubleshooting standard office equipment. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree preferred. Event planning experience preferred; graphic design and social media proficiency preferred but not required. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 08/26/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within hourly grade 11 and the range is $25.05-26.48/hr. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 11 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
