    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/32418": {
      "title": "VIEW: Residential Program Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | VIEW: Residential Program Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us VIEW: Residential Program Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The summer program runs June 16- 29, 2024. This position needs to be available on June 13, 14 & 15 for training and preparation for the summer program. This position will also act as the social media administrator. The person needs to be comfortable navigating social media. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20240534T Position Title: VIEW: Residential Program Assistant Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: temporary Approximate Number of Hours per Week Residential, June 1- June 29, 2024 Department: 702 - Center for Access Success and Achievement Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Villanova Initiative for Engaging Women ( VIEW ), a 10-month college-prep program that consist of a summer residential component, is seeking Residential Counselors for the summer program. The Residential Program Assistant will serve as the second point of contact for all staff and students. Applicants will reside on campus for the duration of the program. Duties and Responsibilities: The Program Assistant will report directly to the Program Director and assist the Program Director with the flow of the program; to include scheduling, organizing events and facilitating workshops. The Program Assistant will assist as needed to support students in English and/or math, travel with students to and from class, meals, residence halls and chaperone trips. Minimum Qualifications: Rising college junior, recent graduate or graduate student Organization skills required. Ability to work with minimum supervision. Experience working with high school students. Preferred Qualifications: Previous experience working in a camp (day or overnight) or summer program setting. Skills or trained in programming and administrative experience. Previous experience as a Residential Advisor on college campus. Created/developed programs for college or was a member of an executive board of an organization. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: May require walking in various weather conditions. Special Message to Applicants: The summer program runs June 16- 29, 2024. This position needs to be available on June 13, 14 & 15 for training and preparation for the summer program. This position will also act as the social media administrator. The person needs to be comfortable navigating social media. EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: 02/16/2024 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 03/27/2024 Salary Posting Information: $15.00/hr Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36560": {
      "title": "O’Toole Family Endowed Assistant Director of Scholarship Coordination",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | O’Toole Family Endowed Assistant Director of Scholarship Coordination Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us O’Toole Family Endowed Assistant Director of Scholarship Coordination To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260435S Position Title: O’Toole Family Endowed Assistant Director of Scholarship Coordination Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 291-Dean - Enrollment Management Position Summary: The O’Toole Family Endowed Assistant Director of Scholarship Coordination plays a central role in advancing Villanova University’s commitment to identifying, supporting, and engaging exceptional scholars through signature scholarship programs. Reporting to the Assistant Dean of Enrollment, this position serves as a connective bridge between the Offices of Enrollment, University Admission, and Financial Assistance. The Assistant Director also has a strong working relationship with Villanova’s Center for Access, Success, and Achievement ( CASA ) to ensure that scholarship recipients have access to the myriad support services available at Villanova, and will receive and direct programmatic insights from CASA and other partners to the appropriate next steps. Finally, the position works closely with donors, families, and external partners to ensure a personalized and mission-aligned experience for each scholar across multiple programs. The Assistant Director leads the coordination and engagement efforts for several major scholarship programs, including the O’Toole Scholars and Posse programs, while also supporting the onboarding and ongoing success of Evans Scholars and Cooperman Scholars along with other smaller endowed scholarship programs. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: O’Toole Scholars Program Manage the annual O’Toole Scholars selection and engagement process. Plan and execute annual recruitment travel to the Archdiocese of Newark, building strong partnerships with high schools and community leaders. Partner with the Office of University Admission to shape the finalist pool. Coordinate finalist travel to Villanova and manage the on-campus interview day experience for students and guardians. Enhance scholar engagement during the senior year of high school and throughout their transition to Villanova. Maintain and expand a consistent meeting cadence and engagement strategy with O’Toole Scholars once matriculated. Work closely with CASA partners to ensure an enhanced student experience Posse Scholarship Program Manage planning and logistics for 6–7 annual campus visits and off-campus selection events in partnership with the Posse Foundation. Coordinate finalist preparation, mentor selection, UNITAS weekend travel, and retreat logistics. Serve as the primary university liaison to donor families and other Posse supporters and stakeholders, enhancing scholar engagement and stewardship. Support programming, retention, and celebration of Posse Scholars across their Villanova experience. Evans Scholarship Program Oversee administrative and programmatic responsibilities related to Villanova’s onboarding as a new Evans Scholar institution. Support the student scholars’ experience, from onboarding through graduation, in collaboration with Financial Assistance and Student Life partners. Other Endowed and Named Scholarships Manage administrative processes for additional endowed scholarships such as the Maguire Scholars, Howley Scholars, and Cooperman Scholars. Oversee annual data collection and reporting to select partnerships, including the Cristo Rey Network, IDEA Prep, and Chicago Scholars. Manage the admissions and administrative tasks of several Philadelphia-based partnerships Coordinate the Augustinian High School Scholarship process and any related events Support donor engagement, reporting, and student stewardship as needed. Collaborate on emerging scholarship initiatives and special projects related to Enrollment Management priorities. Contribute to broader office initiatives in support of student access, retention, and success. Perform other duties and assist with projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelor’s degree Work Experience Minimum three years of relevant experience in higher education, scholarship administration, student success, or related fields. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Strong project management and event coordination skills. Demonstrated ability to build relationships with diverse constituencies including students,families, donors, and institutional partners. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Meticulous attention to detail across multiple agreements and channels. Exceptional organizational skills, cultural competency, and a collaborative spirit to sustain high-impact relationships across internal and external stakeholders. Ability to work evening and weekend hours may be required to support operational needs Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education · Master’s degree Work Experience · Experience working with scholarship or donor-funded programs in higher education. · Demonstrated success in fostering inclusive and engaging student communities. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) · Familiarity with the Posse Foundation, Evans Scholars Foundation, or similar access-based scholarship initiatives. · Understanding of financial aid, admissions, or student success processes. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Ability to work evening and weekend hours may be required to support operational needs Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 10/13/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 13 and the range is $51,000-63,800. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 13 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33452": {
      "title": "Adjunct Professor - Electrical and Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Professor - Electrical and Computer Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Professor - Electrical and Computer Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering Department will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. All applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the the following three pieces of information: (a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; (b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, he or she may submit them on line in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2018489F Position Title: Adjunct Professor - Electrical and Computer Engineering Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/9-months Department: 204-Electrical and Computer Engineering Position Summary: The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering at Villanova University is seeking applications for adjunct faculty positions. The department offers a wide variety of courses in analog and digital electronics, computer architecture, cybersecurity, microwaves, energy systems and signals and communications. Further information about the department can be found at http://www1.villanova.edu/villanova/engineering/departments/ece.html. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and related duties will vary with the specific course(s) being taught. Minimum Qualifications: The minimum qualification is a Master’s degree in electrical or computer engineering or a related field. Commitment to teaching excellence is expected. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Undergraduate courses are offered during the day; most graduate courses run during the evening. Special Message to Applicants: The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering Department will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. All applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the the following three pieces of information: (a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; (b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, he or she may submit them on line in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: 05/11/2018 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,650.00 – $2,600.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: N/A Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Transcripts Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
