    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34138": {
      "title": "Villanova Sports Network Production Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Villanova Sports Network Production Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Villanova Sports Network Production Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20245232V Position Title: Villanova Sports Network Production Assistant Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10-15 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2025-2026 Academic Year Location Villanova Stadium Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 5-10 Department: 732-Athletics - Promotion + Marketing Contact Name: Jacob Whitten Contact Phone/Extension: 9-7684 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Villanova Athletics is seeking student production assistants to help with video content creation, live streaming, photography, graphic design or photography. ESPN+ Live streaming: Responsibilities include (but are not limited to): producer, director, operate video switcher, camera operator, provide production support, video engineer and other duties as assigned by supervisor. Live streaming events take place at Villanova Stadium, Higgins Soccer Complex, Finneran Pavilion, Jake Nevin Field House, Villanova Softball Complex, Proving Grounds in Conshohocken & Villanova Baseballl Park at Plymouth Meeting. If interested – serve as on-air talent for live streaming events. New for the 2025-26, Villanova Athletics will be streaming Olympic Sporting events to ESPN+. Video content creation: Assist in developing unique and exciting videos (hype videos, postgame reports, press conference recaps, previews, other non-live content) for various outlets, including but not limited to Villanova.com, Villanova Athletics Youtube, Villanova Athletics social media channels (Facebook, Twitter, Instagram, etc.), Villanova Athletics videoboards and Villanova Sports Network. Graphic Design / Photography: Assisting in developing digital media graphics and photography content for various outlets listed above. Requirements: Training available, but experience is preferred. Evening and weekend hours are constant throughout the year and are a major requirement for employment. Efficient / ability to learn in Adobe Premiere Pro, or Final Cut X Experience in Live Sport Productions Social Media savvy Background/experience in Post Production Passion for college athletics Willingness to work a flexible schedule including nights and weekends Knowledge of JVC Pro Cameras, and Filming Live Events Ability to meet tight deadlines and work well under pressure Efficient / ability to learn Adobe Photoshop, Lightroom & Illustrator Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Production assistants will be on each game or shoot (as their class schedule permits) to help transport gear, set up, assist during production, tear down, and load gear back to the office. Wage Rate: $15 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document Writing Sample/Publications © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
