    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35967": {
      "title": "Event and Guest Relations Intern",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Event and Guest Relations Intern Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Event and Guest Relations Intern To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20255537V Position Title: Event and Guest Relations Intern Posting Type Student Hours/week: 5-10 Eligibility: Work Study ONLY Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Garey Hall Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 5 Department: 323-Career Services Contact Name: Patti Schuler Contact Phone/Extension: 97191 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Students in the University Career Center will have the opportunity to develop their interpersonal and professional development skills while contributing to the UCC’s mission. Interns will gain valuable experience as they assist with the coordination and execution of UCC events and have direct exposure to employers recruiting at Villanova. Events are normally in person but occasionally could be virtual. Responsibilities: Assist in event management of any kind including, but not limited to: Set up event according to Career Center guidelines (this may involve picking materials up from Career Center and helping guests set up in room technology) Greet employers, presenters, guests of the UCC Check-in employer and student attendees Occasional introduction of employers/guests at the start of the event Collect the contact details of the presenters and deliver back to the Career Center Remain for the duration of the event to troubleshoot and facilitate Q&A (as needed) Clean up after the event (this may involve returning materials to the Career Center and helping dispose of leftover catering) Schedule time to meet with Career Center office staff prior to an event to discuss details Requirements: Solid interpersonal, verbal and written communication skills Attention to detail Flexibility and the ability to troubleshoot Must work at least 5 events per semester Events more often evenings with occasional morning and afternoon hours as needed (student can sign up based on their availability) Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: This job requires lifting or carrying general equipment or supplies (up to 25 pounds) to and from events. Wage Rate: $10.00/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
