    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36386": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Intern - Career Mentor",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Undergraduate Intern - Career Mentor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Undergraduate Intern - Career Mentor To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260245V Position Title: Undergraduate Intern - Career Mentor Posting Type Student Hours/week: 20 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Vasey Hall Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 1-5 Department: 261-Continuing Studies Administration Contact Name: Deborah Harris Contact Phone/Extension: 9-8035 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The VUnited Scholars Program is a residential certificate program offered through the College of Professional Studies ( CPS ) for students with intellectual and developmental disabilities. The Student Internship & Career Mentor (Job Coach) is a student worker position that supports VUnited Scholars in their vocational experiences, with a primary focus on internship success and career development. This role provides individualized, strengths-based support to students in campus and community-based internship settings, promoting independence, skill development, and meaningful engagement in the workplace. Student mentors serve as peer role models and job coaches, actively supporting job task completion, professional skill development, and workplace integration. Mentors maintain an engaged on-site presence and help foster a positive, respectful, and inclusive work environment while collaborating closely with VUnited staff and internship supervisors to ensure a successful and supportive experience. 95%: Student Internship & Career Support In partnership with Assistant Director and Program Director, meet with students for site placement and to assist in career support as needed. In partnership with Assistant Director and Program Director, communicate with supervisors to ensure the best internship experience and support student on-site employment. In partnership with the Assistant Director, assist with the VUnited Inclusive Professionals “VIP” Network by means of educating and expanding partnerships of employers committed to inclusivity. Provide direct, on-site job coaching support to VUnited Scholars during internship experiences Assist students in learning and completing job tasks using modeling, prompting, and coaching strategies Promote independence by gradually fading support and encouraging self-direction Support development of professional workplace skills, including communication, time management, organization, and task completion Maintain an active and engaged presence at internship sites to ensure consistent and effective support Support the development of positive working relationships between students and colleagues Assist with problem-solving and navigating workplace challenges in a respectful and supportive manner Support transitions to and from internship sites, including transportation routines as needed Communicate updates, concerns, and successes in a timely and professional manner with VUnited staff and supervisors Maintain accurate and timely documentation of student progress, support strategies, workplace observations, and communication with supervisors and VUnited staff Model professionalism at all times, including punctuality, communication, and workplace behavior 5%: Serve in additional roles as needed Requirements: Formal Education : Current undergraduate or graduate student at Villanova University Work Experience: Experience working with individuals with diverse learning styles and support needs preferred but not required Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills): Strong skills in verbal communication, writing, and editing. Excellent people skills, discretion and judgment, attention to detail, problem solver and timely follow through. Ability to work independently and as a cross-functional team member. Proactive, creative, and efficient in offering most effective student support. Experience working with diverse populations. Strong interpersonal and communication skills Professionalism, reliability, and punctuality Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area): Interest in career development, coaching, education, or human services Willingness to learn and apply strengths-based job coaching strategies Ability to balance support with promoting independence Demonstrated ability to contribute to a respectful, inclusive, and supportive environment for individuals with diverse learning styles and support needs Appreciation for the mission and values of the VUnited Scholars Program and Catholic Higher Education Equipment Knowledge: Computer literacy in MS Office Programs Valid driver’s license is required Must be eligible to become Villanova University van certified and comfortable transporting students to and from internship placements and program-related activities as needed Working Conditions/Environment: (conditions, if known, which may impact the incumbent working in this position): Combination of campus-based and community-based internship sites Requires movement between locations and active engagement in workplace settings Role involves standing, walking, and supporting students in real-time work environments Schedule primarily aligned with internship hours (Wednesdays), with some flexibility as needed Additional Information: Continuation is dependent upon continued funding through gifts and/or entrepreneurial tuition revenues. Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $15/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33401": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Theology",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Theology Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Theology To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Availability of positions is variable and dependent upon numbers of students and courses required. Screening of submitted applications begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Candidates selected for interviews for the Adjunct Faculty Pool will be contacted by telephone or e-mail. In accordance with University policy, finalists for this position will be subject to a criminal background check. Unofficial transcripts will be accepted to submit application; however, official transcripts are required if you are selected for an interview. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2015227F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Theology Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: temporary Department: 147-Theology/Religious Studies Position Summary: The Department of Theology & Religious Studies seeks qualified individuals for its Adjunct Faculty Pool and welcomes applicants at any time to submit a letter of interest (with names and the contact information of three references), a current resume and unofficial copies of college/university transcripts at https://jobs.villanova.edu. Availability of positions is variable and dependent upon numbers of students and courses required. Screening of submitted applications begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Candidates selected for interviews for the Adjunct Faculty Pool will be contacted by telephone or e-mail. In accordance with University policy, finalists for this position will be subject to a criminal background check. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Faculty members teach undergraduate or graduate courses in Theology. Minimum Qualifications: Undergraduate courses: Must hold a master’s degree in theology (or related discipline) from an accredited institution of higher education. Previous teaching experience preferred. Graduate Courses: Must hold a doctoral degree in theology (or related discipline) from an accredited institution of higher education. Previous teaching experience preferred. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Availability of positions is variable and dependent upon numbers of students and courses required. Screening of submitted applications begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Candidates selected for interviews for the Adjunct Faculty Pool will be contacted by telephone or e-mail. In accordance with University policy, finalists for this position will be subject to a criminal background check. Unofficial transcripts will be accepted to submit application; however, official transcripts are required if you are selected for an interview. Posting Date: 03/20/2015 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,160.00 – $2,230.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 0 Maximum Number of References Needed 0 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * Do you currently hold a Ph.D. or are you A.B.D? No Response Yes No * Briefly list your areas of teaching expertise. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
