    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36465": {
      "title": "Enrollment Counselor",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Enrollment Counselor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Enrollment Counselor To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260436S Position Title: Enrollment Counselor Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 576-Dean, Professional Studies Position Summary: The Enrollment Counselor is the primary point of contact for all inquiries and applications for all Associate, Bachelor’s, credit-bearing certificates and select non-credit professional education courses and programs in CPS . General responsibilities include proactively recruiting new students for CPS programs by conducting outreach via phone, email, and text messaging, as well as responding to telephone, e-mail, live chat & texting inquiries, application monitoring, and conducting telephone/zoom follow-up and outreach recruitment activities. While providing top-notch customer service, this individual guides applicants through the process of admission and/or enrollment, the collection of all application materials, and reviews applicants’ files, assesses qualifications for admission, and makes admission recommendations, with consultation from the Associate Director, Admissions and Senior Director, Admissions as needed. The Enrollment Counselor assists with developing and implementing strategies for recruiting and yielding diverse prospective students. S/he also assists with the application process for visiting students, as well as High School and Pre-College programming. Other responsibilities include: assisting in the planning and implementation of open houses, information sessions, student visits, and other recruitment activities; conducting preliminary transcript evaluations; representing the admissions and enrollment teams at various events; assisting with updating the Admissions section of the website; and performing other duties and special projects as assigned by the Associate Director, Admissions. The Enrollment Counselor also oversees the transition of newly admitted students to the academic programs and advising teams to ensure a seamless handoff for initial registration. Titles of Positions Supervised: None Duties and Responsibilities: Utilizes our Slate CRM to proactively recruit and select high-quality students into CPS degree and certificate programs to reach and/or exceed enrollment targets. Builds relationships with prospective students and applicants by understanding their personal and professional goals, helping them determine whether courses and programs in the portfolio are the right fit, answering questions, making connections, and providing superior service that showcases the Villanova difference and drives enrollment growth; monitors the daily progress of prospective students within the recruitment “funnel” in relation to enrollment goals. Conducts proper follow-up necessary to reach enrollment goals, ensuring follow-up is timely and personal. Communicates effectively and professionally with prospective students via phone, email, online chat, texting, and in person about the application process and program offerings. Facilitates information sessions (virtual/in-person) for various programs within the CPS portfolio. Participates in recruiting events to promote the entire CPS portfolio. Once an application is completed, reviews applicants’ files and assesses qualifications for admission to make admission recommendations. Records and tracks admissions application activity; monitors the CPS Admissions Reply form completion process and admission decisions within the CRM system. Collects and helps evaluate preliminary transcript reviews. Represents the College and/or Admissions team at various social, networking, and other internal events. Assists with updating the Admissions section of the website and ensuring publications are up to date. Assists with planning and executing open houses, information sessions, student visits, and other recruitment activities. Follows up with admitted students to answer questions, discuss CPS program differentiators, and encourage enrollment at CPS ; assists with other activities that support student yield as appropriate. Follows up with enrolling students to obtain final transcripts before classes begin. Maintains familiarity with the University catalog, CPS academic programs, and all CPS policies. Participates in service and social functions hosted by CPS and Villanova. Assists in answering phone calls and walk-ins, and guiding students to the appropriate staff. Partners with the Associate Director to deploy ad-hoc Slate mailings, both SMS and email, when needed to drive enrollments and/or engagement with prospects and/or applicants. Performs additional duties and assists with special projects as assigned. Participates in events with CPS on occasional nights and weekends. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: Bachelor’s degree required Minimum Work Experience: Minimum of 2 years of relevant and applicable work experience in a professional environment related to admissions and enrollment. Specific Job Knowledge: Demonstrated successful experience in recruitment for the adult population, or relevant sales experience achieving goal metrics. Strong understanding of CPS programs and an exceptional customer service orientation. Ability to build relationships with professionals of all backgrounds. Demonstrated success in recruiting initiatives with a track record of quantifying results. Experience recruiting for campus and online programs. Strong communication skills and a strong brand ambassador. Experience managing projects, deadlines, and priorities. Ability to make decisions in a fast-paced environment and handle multiple priorities across the College’s programs. Work Skills: Strong organizational, time management, and relationship management skills, with demonstrated ability to work as a team player. Results-oriented, able to anticipate and identify problems and opportunities and take decisive action to proactively address them. Excellent oral and written communication, problem-solving, and decision-making skills. Ability to establish and maintain long-term relationships and to communicate professionally and efficiently within a fast-paced environment. Proficient in all standard computer applications, including Microsoft Office, with extensive proficiency in Word and Excel; general knowledge of office principles and procedures; proficiency in a Customer Relationship Management ( CRM ) database (Slate preferred). Equipment Knowledge: Computers and all related programs used by the University. Other: Deep commitment to the College of Professional Studies, to the University’s Catholic/Augustinian heritage and the advancement of its mission, and to serving the needs of a diverse community. Preferred Qualifications: Experience recruiting for non-credit programs. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Participates in events with CPS on occasional nights and weekends. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 09/30/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 13 and the range is $52,000-65,100. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 13 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33420": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Marketing",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty, Marketing Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty, Marketing To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Department of Marketing and Business Law will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications. Please indicate your areas of teaching interest and expertise within the specified question in the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2012075F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty, Marketing Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 222-Marketing Position Summary: The Department of Marketing and Business Law in the Villanova School of Business ( VSB ) invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Marketing for undergraduate and/or MBA courses taught during the day and/or evening. Openings to teach these courses develop on a periodic basis, depending on department teaching needs. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching specific Marketing courses. Minimum Qualifications: The applicant must be committed to excellence in business education. A master’s degree within a relevant field is strongly preferred. Equivalent experience may be considered. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree preferred, teaching experience a plus. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The Department of Marketing and Business Law will accept applications throughout the year. If a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications. Please indicate your areas of teaching interest and expertise within the specified question in the application. Posting Date: 09/27/2012 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,925.00 – $2,505.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: N/A Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed Maximum Number of References Needed Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Briefly list your areas of teaching expertise. (Open Ended Question) * Briefly describe your previous teaching experience. (Open Ended Question) * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
