    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33248": {
      "title": "Camera Operator (Athletics Control Room)",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Camera Operator (Athletics Control Room) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Camera Operator (Athletics Control Room) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20210370T Position Title: Camera Operator (Athletics Control Room) Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: temporary Approximate Number of Hours per Week Department: 732-Athletics - Promotion + Marketing Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Villanova University Athletics is now hiring highly motivated, skilled, and passionate Camera Operator freelancers to join our Athletics Game Production team. The Camera Operator is responsible for the set-up, operation, and breakdown of all camera equipment associated with a game production script at the direction of the Villanova Athletics Marketing/Operations staff and Athletics Building Engineer. All duties are to be performed in accordance with the department and venue policies and procedures. Duties and Responsibilities: Work closely with Game Director and Building Engineer to test and manage all camera elements and shots associated with the game script select, assemble and position equipment (cameras, stands) throughout venue. Shoot scenes according to requirements within the game script at the direction of the Game Director. Capture quality footage from a fixed or moving position, travel to different locations depending on assignments. Maintain, clean and test all equipment and cameras to ensure every tool is in good working order each day before event starts. Participate in pre-event coordination planning meeting. Familiar with the language of event production and have a working knowledge of all current technology. Ensure the safety of equipment at all times. Respect standards and regulations regarding the safety of audio equipment, and apply safe work methods. Provide support and assistance to other venue areas as needed. Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: 1-2 years of related camera operations experience in live game production and live sports. Proficient using the following studio production cameras: Hitachi Hd6000, JVC HM 600. Excellent interpersonal & communication skills required. Must be a collaborative team player who works well with others in a fast paced and dynamic environment. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Available to work flexible hours including nights, weekends, and holidays Special Message to Applicants: EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: 08/12/2021 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $175 per event (5hr crew call) Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as: • Any person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and • Such contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU. Examples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following: • Parents/Legal Guardians • Coaches (high school, college, club) • Personal/Skills Trainers • Relatives • Strength Coach • Advisors Consistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any: • Basketball (men’s or women’s) prospective student-athletes (grades 9-12) or their parents, relatives or coaches? Y N Yes No * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as: • Any person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and • Such contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU. Examples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following: • Parents/Legal Guardians • Coaches (high school, college, club) • Personal/Skills Trainers • Relatives • Strength Coach • Advisors Consistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any: • Current VU basketball (men’s or women’s) student-athletes? Y N Yes No Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36566": {
      "title": "Boiler Operator",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Boiler Operator Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Boiler Operator To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Subject to changing shift throughout work week to cover boiler operator vacancies. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260449S Position Title: Boiler Operator Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 793-FS - Steam Plant Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. We believe that an inclusive community fosters an understanding and appreciation for diversity among our students, faculty, staff and administrators. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people. As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Under moderate supervision from the Chief Engineer or Lead Engineer, is capable of implementing the operation, maintenance and service of boilers and all auxiliary equipment associated with the generation and supply of high-pressure steam in accordance with all applicable standards of the trade and regulatory agencies. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Conducts burner firing operation plus auxiliary systems for all boilers. Checks water softeners for correct operation and needed services. Required to maintain salt level for brine tank. Maintains steam plant in clean condition as to oil spillage and general cleaning and appearance. Maintains proper records for all logs and reports required. Operates, maintains, troubleshoots, and repairs, as required, high pressure stream systems and all auxiliary equipment consistent with manufacturer’s guidelines, operating design parameters, and accepted practices to optimize energy use. Under moderate supervision troubleshoots and repairs steam devices including electronic, electrical, and mechanical components and connections. Operates and keeps in good working order a variety of equipment including hand tools, mobile electronic devices, measuring/diagnostic/testing meters and instruments. Reads and interprets basic blueprints, sketches, schematics, and wiring diagrams. Under moderate supervision performs soldering, pipefitting, as required. Coordinates repairs with other trades affected by the steam operations. Performs other duties as assigned within the normal scope of the department’s responsibilities and the individual’s capabilities. Responsible for monitoring, controlling, and maintaining boiler operations though SCADA system to insure the efficient and safe operation of boilers by leveraging SCADA technology to track system parameters, detect faults, and implement corrective actions. Required to perform and assist with all chemical treatment including Testing, Mixing, and loading of chemicals. Minimum Qualifications: HS diploma or equivalent and current documentation indicating successful passing of formal training classes or programs in high pressure steam systems and be able to exhibit acceptable life experience in high pressure steam systems operations. Requires at least two years’ work experience in a high-pressure steam plant operation. Must have the ability to follow both verbal and written directions in English; the ability to interact with students, faculty, administration, and staff in a professional and positive manner, as well as the ability to read and understand OSHA guidelines such as Material Safety Data Sheets, equipment safety data plates, fuel/chemical flash points, etc. Must have the physical ability to climb ladders, to bend, reach, crawl, and lift up to 60 lbs.; the ability to work in enclosed spaces as per OSHA guidelines. Must have the ability to read and interpret basic blueprints, drawings/sketches, schematics and diagrams. Must have and maintain a valid driver’s license. Must have experience in preventative maintenance procedures; in meter reading and lead testing; in the repair and shutoff of gas, water, electrical, life safety systems (i.e. fire alarm, sprinkler, etc.) and steam supplies. Basic Microsoft Windows and Microsoft Outlook skills. Must not have any disciplinary actions on file within the previous twelve months of applying for this position. Must have the ability to erect and work on scaffolding as per OSHA standards. Must have an excellent safety record Preferred Qualifications: City of Philadelphia Stationary Engineers License Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Must have the physical ability to climb ladders, to bend, reach, crawl, and lift up to 60 lbs. The ability to work in enclosed spaces as per OSHA guidelines. Special Message to Applicants: Subject to changing shift throughout work week to cover boiler operator vacancies. Posting Date: 10/02/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 12/01/2026 Salary Posting Information: $34.85 an hour Salary Grade: UNION Job Classification: union References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
