    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36399": {
      "title": "Professional Tutor, Writing Center",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Professional Tutor, Writing Center Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Professional Tutor, Writing Center To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260433S Position Title: Professional Tutor, Writing Center Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/9-months Avg Hours Week 20 Department: 100-Provost Position Summary: The Writing Center aids students in a collaborative effort of creating their ideal texts and producing their best quality work. The Writing Center encourages multiple, independent visits for all types of students, in all stages of their writing, and seeks to produce better writers, not better texts. This position is a year-to-year, nine-month appointment depending on need. It requires 20 hrs/week working for the Writing Center and reports to the Director of the Writing Center. This professional tutor will be assigned to work primarily with Villanova undergraduate students, but may also work with graduate students or faculty members. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Provide one-to-one consultations with Villanova students, staff, and faculty. Engage in a collaborative effort to help writers create their best quality work and improve writing skills. Complete online reports after each session. Attend brief team meetings (concerning workshops, discussing professional development opportunities, etc.) Support outreach efforts and secondary projects (running workshops, providing in-class presentations, etc.) Perform other duties and assist with projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree required 3 years previous face-to-face tutoring experience; knowledge of excellent writing skills, rhetorical models, and effective one-to-one tutoring methods; Excellent written and verbal communications skills. Microsoft Office applications. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Basic file handling Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 09/18/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within hourly grade 12 and the range is $22.36-30.00/hr. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 12 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
