    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34110": {
      "title": "Graduate Research Assistant - STEM Curriculum Developer",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Graduate Research Assistant - STEM Curriculum Developer Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Graduate Research Assistant - STEM Curriculum Developer To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20255609V Position Title: Graduate Research Assistant - STEM Curriculum Developer Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10-25 hours per week Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester Location Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 2-3 Department: 205-Mechanical Engineering Contact Name: Deeksha Seth Contact Phone/Extension: 9-4992 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: We are seeking part-time STEM Curriculum Developers to support the creation of virtual learning materials for high school and early college students. The position involves developing single-subject and interdisciplinary lesson plans in STEM fields – such as math, biology, physics, and engineering. Some lessons will be inspired by themes in geology and paleontology. This work is part of a broader effort to create engaging, standard-aligned Virtual Field Trips (VFTs) and STEM learning experiences for national distribution. This is a remote, temporary position beginning in Summer 2025. The role offers flexible hours and the opportunity to work with a collaborative and interdisciplinary team of educators and researchers. Requirements: Bachelor’s Degree or higher Strong written communication, organizational, and collaboration skills K–12 educators with curriculum development experience or graduate students pursuing degrees in STEM fields (e.g., Math, Biology, Physics, Engineering, Education) are encouraged to apply Additional Information: Develop lesson plans, instructional content, and assessments in STEM subjects Create both single-discipline and interdisciplinary modules based on project needs Align curriculum with NGSS and state/national standards Upload and organize content on an online learning platform Design interactive exercises and student activities that foster engagement and understanding Collaborate with faculty, graduate students, and external partners to ensure content accuracy and quality Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: 18/hr Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 08/05/2025 Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35649": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Analytical Chemistry",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Assistant Professor of Analytical Chemistry Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Assistant Professor of Analytical Chemistry To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. To apply, please visit Villanova’s job portal (https://jobs.villanova.edu/). Review of applications will begin September 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. The starting date is expected to be August 2027. Applications must be submitted online and include: • Cover letter • Complete curriculum vitae • Teaching statement (methods, outcomes, goals, and development activities, if applicable). • Proposed research statement that demonstrates potential for high-quality scholarship while involving undergraduate and master’s students. Should include any necessary instrumentation to be purchased with startup funding; a list of current departmental instrumentation is on the departmental website. • Candidates will be expected to provide a statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions may support the University’s mission (and enduring principles) . Please refer to the departmental website and the Villanova University Mission Statement. • Undergraduate and graduate transcripts (unofficial acceptable for application). Transcripts can be uploaded as a scan/PDF as an “Other Document” to the HR site. • Must include contact information for 3 references who can be contacted via email to submit confidential letters of recommendation when the application is submitted. • Other supporting documents may be submitted online in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260056F Position Title: Assistant Professor of Analytical Chemistry Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 184-Chemistry Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Department of Chemistry and Biochemistry at Villanova University invites applicants for a Tenure-Track Assistant Professor position in Analytical Chemistry to teach in our department, which offers ACS -certified B.S. degrees in chemistry, ASBMB -accredited B.S. degrees in biochemistry, M.S. degrees in chemistry and does not have a Ph.D. program. The successful candidate will receive a start-up package and a pre-tenure sabbatical. Please visit our webpage for information about the department, as well as our research and scholarship facilities page . Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will contribute to the vibrant curriculum of the department at both the undergraduate and graduate levels, teaching up to 15 contact hours per year (12 in the first year), with courses in instrumentation, quantitative analysis, and in additional area(s) of specialty. The candidate will establish and maintain an active and productive research program, integrate undergraduate and master’s students into research, actively seek extramural funding, and effectively participate in departmental/university professional service. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in chemistry or related fields with a demonstrated specialization involving quantitative chemical measurement. Applicants should show potential for success in teaching and research in a predominantly undergraduate liberal arts setting. Preferred Qualifications: Post-doctoral research experience that broadens the candidate’s expertise. Experience teaching and mentoring undergraduates in both classroom and laboratory settings. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Most graduate classes are taught in the evenings. Special Message to Applicants: To apply, please visit Villanova’s job portal (https://jobs.villanova.edu/). Review of applications will begin September 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. The starting date is expected to be August 2027. Applications must be submitted online and include: • Cover letter • Complete curriculum vitae • Teaching statement (methods, outcomes, goals, and development activities, if applicable). • Proposed research statement that demonstrates potential for high-quality scholarship while involving undergraduate and master’s students. Should include any necessary instrumentation to be purchased with startup funding; a list of current departmental instrumentation is on the departmental website. • Candidates will be expected to provide a statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions may support the University’s mission (and enduring principles) . Please refer to the departmental website and the Villanova University Mission Statement. • Undergraduate and graduate transcripts (unofficial acceptable for application). Transcripts can be uploaded as a scan/ PDF as an “Other Document” to the HR site. • Must include contact information for 3 references who can be contacted via email to submit confidential letters of recommendation when the application is submitted. • Other supporting documents may be submitted online in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: 07/13/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Statement of Research Interests Statement of Contribution to Mission Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
