    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36476": {
      "title": "Assistant Director for Data and Assessment",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Assistant Director for Data and Assessment Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Assistant Director for Data and Assessment To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. In addition to your resume and cover letter, please submit a written Statement of Contribution to Mission. You may find more information on our website about the University’s Mission and Enduring Commitments . Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260450S Position Title: Assistant Director for Data and Assessment Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 005-Office of Mission and Ministry Position Summary: The Assistant Director for Data and Assessment is responsible for the administration, analysis, and strategic use of programmatic data across the Office for Mission and Ministry ( OMM ). This position oversees registration and participant data management systems for the division, including utilizing the University’s event management platform and the Villanova Service Hub, ensuring the collection of accurate, reliable, and actionable information that supports program operations, assessment efforts, and decision-making. The Assistant Director serves as a key resource for reporting, evaluation, and data governance while identifying opportunities to improve processes, integrate systems, and strengthen OMM’s data culture. In collaboration with Mission and Ministry staff, the Office of Strategic Planning and Institutional Effectiveness, Advancement, and University Technology Services, this position designs and implements assessment strategies that measure program effectiveness and student learning outcomes. The Assistant Director for Data and Assessment develops reports, dashboards, presentations, and data-informed narratives that communicate impact and support strategic planning. The position also supports alumni engagement and donor stewardship initiatives by maintaining participation data systems that enable long-term constituent outreach, recognition, and engagement, advancing the mission and goals of the Office for Mission and Ministry. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The Office for Mission and Ministry ( OMM ) promotes and supports the Augustinian Catholic mission of the University with particular attention to the Augustinian charism and spirituality. A concern for building community and fostering an atmosphere that demonstrates care for our common home are core values integral to OMM’s stewardship of the University’s mission. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: 35% Program Data Management Oversee program registration and application processes for Mission and Ministry programs utilizing the University’s event management platform ( STOVA ), Microsoft Forms, and other approved technology platforms. Collaborate with program staff to develop consistent data collection standards and ensure the accuracy, completeness, and integrity of participant information. Serve as a representative of the Office for Mission and Ministry on the STOVA Working Group and assist with implementation of platform enhancements and best practices. Maintain program databases and reporting systems that support operational effectiveness, strategic planning, and organizational decision-making. Identify opportunities to streamline data collection and reporting processes and provide training and support for departmental staff. Generate routine and ad hoc reports to support program assessment, participation tracking, and leadership reporting. Identify opportunities to resolve challenges with technology. 25% Villanova Service Hub Management In collaboration with the Associate Director for Service Integration, manage all aspects of the Villanova Service Hub platform through GivePulse, including service opportunity postings, volunteer management, user support, and system administration. Coordinate the collection, maintenance, and integration of service-related data that exists outside of GivePulse and ensure accurate reconciliation with platform records. Develop and maintain reports on student engagement, volunteer participation, community partner activity, and other key performance indicators related to service and community engagement programs. Analyze trends and participation data to inform strategic planning and program development. Maintain the community partner database and ensure records are accurate, current, and aligned with University standards. Serve as the primary departmental resource for GivePulse administration, training, and troubleshooting. 25% Assessment and Evaluation Partner with the Office of Strategic Planning and Institutional Effectiveness to develop and implement assessment strategies for programs, initiatives, and events across Mission and Ministry. Design surveys, rubrics, questionnaires, and other assessment tools aligned with University learning outcomes, the Office for Mission and Ministry Strategic Plan, and department goals. Collect, organize, and analyze quantitative and qualitative data from multiple sources to measure program effectiveness and student outcomes. Prepare reports, dashboards, presentations, and executive summaries that communicate findings to stakeholders and support evidence-based decision making. Translate assessment results into compelling narratives that demonstrate impact through data-informed storytelling. Recommend improvements to programs, processes, and assessment methodologies based on findings and best practices. Identify unintegrated practices that create silos of information and recommend solutions. 10% Alumni Engagement and Stewardship Collaborate with Advancement, University Technology Services, and Mission and Ministry staff to develop and maintain systems that identify and tag student records based on program participation. Support long-term alumni engagement efforts by ensuring accurate participation data is available for future communication, outreach, and donor stewardship initiatives. Manage processes and data related to donor acknowledgement activities for Mission and Ministry funds, ensuring timely and accurate recognition of gifts. Produce reports and analyses related to alumni engagement, constituent participation, and donor stewardship efforts. Assist in the development of strategies that leverage program participation data to strengthen lifelong engagement with Mission and Ministry and Villanova University. Ensure compliance with University policies and best practices related to data governance, confidentiality, and record management. 5% Other Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: Bachelor’s degree in Data Analytics, Information Systems, Business Analytics, Higher Education Administration, Sociology, Statistics, Public Administration, Communications, or a related field required. Specific Job Knowledge: (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Knowledge of data collection, database management, reporting, and assessment methodologies. Understanding of survey design, and program evaluation. Experience with event management systems, CRM platforms, volunteer management systems, or similar databases. Knowledge of higher education assessment practices, student learning outcomes, and institutional effectiveness processes. Familiarity with data visualization, dashboard design, and data storytelling techniques. Understanding of data governance, confidentiality, records management, and applicable privacy regulations. Proficiency with Microsoft 365 applications, including Excel, Forms, Power BI, SharePoint, and related reporting tools. Knowledge of constituent engagement, alumni relations, volunteer tracking, or donor stewardship practices is preferred. Work Experience: Three to five years of experience in data management, assessment, institutional research, analytics, program evaluation, higher education administration, or a related field. Experience managing datasets, generating reports, conducting data analysis, and supporting organizational decision-making required. Work Skills: (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including the ability to present data through accessible reports, presentations, and executive summaries for diverse audiences. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with demonstrated ability to interpret complex data and communicate findings effectively. Ability to build partnerships inside the Villanova community and out to further the University Mission. Proficiency with software and technology across platforms and devices as well as an ability and willingness to learn more. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple projects, deadlines, and competing priorities simultaneously. High attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy, integrity, and confidentiality. Commitment to supporting the mission and values of Villanova University and the Office for Mission and Ministry. Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education: Master’s degree in Higher Education, Data Analytics, Assessment, Organizational Leadership, or a related discipline preferred. Work Experience: Experience in a higher education, nonprofit, faith-based, or mission-driven environment preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: In addition to your resume and cover letter, please submit a written Statement of Contribution to Mission. You may find more information on our website about the University’s Mission and Enduring Commitments . Posting Date: 10/01/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 14 and the range is $58,300-72,900. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 14 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * The Office for Mission and Ministry uses data from multiple programs, platforms, and stakeholders to evaluate impact, improve operations, and support strategic decision-making. Describe a project or initiative in which you collected, analyzed, and communicated data to inform decisions or improve outcomes. Please limit your response to 500 words or fewer. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Contribution to Mission Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
