    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35701": {
      "title": "Catering Delivery Assistant - Cabrini Campus",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Catering Delivery Assistant - Cabrini Campus Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Catering Delivery Assistant - Cabrini Campus To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Schedule will vary weekly depending on event needs. Must be flexible. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260251S Position Title: Catering Delivery Assistant - Cabrini Campus Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 838-Cabrini Catering Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Catering Delivery Assistant is responsible for the daily operation of catering delivery contracts and ensures that our quality standards are maintained. This includes the driving and operating of the department’s vans. This position is also responsible for the food delivery services in the building and for remote set ups . This person will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the value of the Villanova Mission Statement and the Dining Services Mission Statement. This person will focus on our Core Values: Safety and Sanitation, Friendly Courteous Service, and Excellence. All our associates should improve our systems and overall operation. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Deliver catering orders to various campus locations, including academic buildings, residence halls, administrative offices, and event venues. Load, transport, unload, and organize food, beverages, supplies, and catering equipment. Set up buffet lines, beverage stations, meeting refreshments, and event displays according to catering specifications. Verify the accuracy and completeness of orders before delivery and upon setup. Maintain food quality, temperature control, and safe handling practices during transportation and service. Provide courteous and professional customer service to faculty, staff, students, alumni, and guests. Assist with event breakdown, equipment retrieval, and cleanup following catered events. Operate carts, vans, or other approved campus delivery vehicles safely and responsibly. Maintain cleanliness and organization of catering storage areas, vehicles, and equipment. Communicate delivery schedules, special requests, and service issues to supervisors and catering staff. Follow university policies, health and safety regulations, and food service standards. Support other Dining Services operations as assigned Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: High School Diploma/equivalent or 2+ years of food service experience required. Specific Job Knowledge: Serv Safe certification preferred. Basic knowledge of food service overall. Valid PA Driver License required with a good driving record and no traffic violations. Must be able to meet and maintain VU driving privileges as outlined by Villanova’s Risk Management’s Motor Vehicle Record Policy for Driver’s of University Vehicles. Qualifications: Strong customer service and communication skills. Ability to work independently and as part of a team. Reliable attendance and punctuality. Ability to work flexible hours, including evenings, weekends, and special events Work Skills: Attention to detail and commitment to accuracy. Ability to follow written and verbal instructions. Ability to work in a fast-paced environment and meet deadlines. Professional demeanor when interacting with the campus community and visitors Equipment Knowledge: General kitchen and food service equipment knowledge. How to operate the department vans. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery and equipment used: Kitchen Equipment Vans Environmental Conditions: Chemicals associated with the food service industry. Physical Requirements: Ability to lift up to 30 pounds independently Ability to sit stand for extended periods Ability to push/pull up to 30 pounds independently Ability to use various chemicals Special Message to Applicants: Schedule will vary weekly depending on event needs. Must be flexible. Posting Date: 07/15/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $18.25 per hour. Shift differential for qualifying shifts. Salary Grade: 8 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
