    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36485": {
      "title": "Graduate Information Technology Technician",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Graduate Information Technology Technician Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Graduate Information Technology Technician To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260399V Position Title: Graduate Information Technology Technician Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10-20 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Kennedy Hall Detailed Work Schedule 10-20 hours a week Number of positions: 5 Department: 715-UTS - Technology Support Services Contact Name: Kimberly Walter Contact Phone/Extension: 6105194899 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Senior Information Technology Technician is a graduate student position. They provide advanced technical support to the Villanova University community through phone, chat, and in-person customer service channels. This role requires strong technical expertise, analytical thinking, customer service skills, and the ability to work independently. While serving as a mentor, technical resource, and point of escalation for other student employees. Record support requests using our TeamDynamix ( TDX ) ticketing system. Requirements: Provide excellent customer support through phone, chat, and face-to-face interactions. Monitor the Service Desk ticketing queue and proactively respond to incoming tickets, emails, chats, and support requests to ensure timely resolution. A minimum of one year of previous experience in information technology support, customer service, technical troubleshooting, or a related field is preferred. Diagnose, troubleshoot, and resolve complex hardware, software, network, and account-related issues. Utilize advanced technical knowledge and problem-solving skills to identify and resolve technology concerns efficiently. Exercise responsible use of elevated system access to support University technology resources and services. Assist with account administration and operational support for enterprise systems and services. Work independently with minimal supervision while demonstrating sound judgment and accountability. Adhere to all University security, privacy, compliance, and data protection standards. Serve as a technical resource for fellow student technicians by sharing knowledge, assisting with troubleshooting, and helping mentor newer team members. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Additional Information: Summer, Fall, and Spring position. * Technology Support Services will provide ALL training. Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: 15.00 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
