    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34395": {
      "title": "NovaEdge Resident Assistant 2026",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | NovaEdge Resident Assistant 2026 Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us NovaEdge Resident Assistant 2026 To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260107V Position Title: NovaEdge Resident Assistant 2026 Posting Type Student Hours/week: 35 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026 Summer Location Sullivan Hall Detailed Work Schedule Students will work 7 hours each day. Some will work during the day and some will work an evening shift. The responsibility to work will be shared evenly by all students. The program is for one week. Number of positions: 8 Department: 201-Dean-Engineering Contact Name: Stephen Jones Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-5439 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The NovaEdge program is seeking to hire Resident Assistants to provide assistance with the residence hall and activities with the NovaEdge High School students. The NovaEdge Resident Assistant will provide guidance and monitor high school students who participate in the program. They will meet with the students and involve them in on campus activities. They will also accompany the students on trips to companies that are in the area. The NovaEdge Program curriculum includes lectures by industry and university professionals, article reviews, and varying learning experiences. The students will have some day and evening hours. The NovaEdge program will be held on the Villanova campus, with housing in Sullivan Hall which allows students immediate access to engineering laboratories and state-of-the-art technological equipment. The program will be held for one week during July, including one weekend from 7/10/26 to 7/18/26. Student run activities will follow mostly an afternoon and evening schedule. The students will be served breakfast, lunch, and dinner. Requirements: Villanova Students must be rising sophomores, juniors, and seniors referred by your self, faculty or staff and must be in good standing with Villanova University. Additional Information: Compliance background checks are required of all applicants in order to work with minors on campus. Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $13 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 04/30/2025 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35902": {
      "title": "Storeroom Keeper",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Storeroom Keeper Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Storeroom Keeper To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260144V Position Title: Storeroom Keeper Posting Type Student Hours/week: Up to 20 hrs/week with courses, up to 40 hrs/week without Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Mendel Science Center Detailed Work Schedule Summer 26 Storeroom Hours: Monday – Thursday 9:00am – 5:00pm Fall 26 Storeroom Hours: Monday – Wednesday 7:30am – 9:30pm Thursday – Friday 7:30am – 6:00pm subject to change Spring 27 Storeroom Hours: Monday – Wednesday 7:30am – 9:30pm Thursday – Friday 7:30am – 6:00pm subject to change Number of positions: up to 25 Department: 184-Chemistry Contact Name: Joseph Kasopsky Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-5278 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Clean and set up labs, issue and receive equipment, file, deliver items to other departments, and other office duties as required. Students enter data in order to track and maintain storeroom chemicals while overseeing storeroom security. Supervise and assist with chemical check-out process. Prepare small and safe reagents and supply them for labs (1103, 1108, i.e. Zinc & Cooper strips). Prepare disposable pipettes for experiments. The Storeroom Keeper is the first visible contact that is trained on safety procedures and has the proper contact info and location for the on-duty safety officer. Requirements: Additional Information: Please indicate which semester you are applying to work: Summer, Fall, or Spring. Please include only your workable schedule not class schedule in the application, as well as your minimum and maximum hours preferred per week. In addition to applying online, please indicate a convenient time for Joseph Kasopksy to call you for a brief phone interview. Training will be provided. Only apply after you know your workable schedule in order to look at your open time slots. Physical Demands Summary: Some lifting required. Wage Rate: $11.25 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 04/25/2027 Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents Other Document Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
