    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35741": {
      "title": "Lab Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Lab Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Lab Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Only for ECE students Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260262V Position Title: Lab Assistant Posting Type Student Hours/week: 20 Eligibility: Work Study ONLY Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Drosdick Hall Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 1 Department: 204-Electrical and Computer Engineering Contact Name: Tom Xaviour Contact Phone/Extension: 6105194976 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The ECE Lab Assistant helps maintain and support the Electrical and Computer Engineering instructional labs. This role involves organizing lab spaces, preparing course materials and kits, checking parts and inventory, testing equipment, and assisting with lab setup and maintenance. The position is ideal for students interested in hands-on technical work, electronics, computer systems, and supporting a safe and effective lab environment. Requirements: Must be enrolled as a student in the ECE Department. Maintain and organize lab spaces, parts, tools, and supplies. Track inventory and help prepare lab kits for courses and projects. Set up lab stations, equipment, and instructional materials. Test, calibrate, and check lab instruments and hardware. Assist with PC software installation, updates, and troubleshooting. Support Linux OS imaging, patching, and maintenance. Move equipment and supplies as needed for lab operations. Report damaged, missing, or malfunctioning equipment. Support faculty, teaching assistants, and lab staff with other lab-related tasks as assigned. Additional Information: The timesheets get approved by Tom Xaviour ECE Lab Manager Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: 13 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 08/07/2026 Open Until Filled No Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
