    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36241": {
      "title": "Undergraduate Research Assistant - geotech",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Undergraduate Research Assistant - geotech Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Undergraduate Research Assistant - geotech To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Assist faculty, lab director, and graduate students in on going research activities. Tasks may include: tension testing of steel coupons, open web steel joist testing, construction of a new test set up for new research, etc. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260369V Position Title: Undergraduate Research Assistant - geotech Posting Type Student Hours/week: 5 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Drosdick Hall Detailed Work Schedule Number of positions: 5 Department: 202-Civil and Environmental Engineering Contact Name: Linda DeAngelis Contact Phone/Extension: 4960 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Student will aid in performing laboratory testing and evaluation of geomaterials. Requirements: Civil Engineering Major in the geotechnical area – Rising Junior or Senior. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $15/hr. Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus befo