    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/31115": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Villanova University is committed to fostering an inclusive academic environment and strongly encourages individuals from historically underrepresented groups in STEM to apply. Applications will be reviewed starting March 1, 2025 , but will be accepted until the position is filled. Required Application Materials: A cover letter expressing interest in the position. A current and complete CV. A research statement (2-page maximum). A teaching statement (2-page maximum). A statement on your contribution to University's mission reflecting on how your teaching, research and service contributes to the University’s value orientation as discussed in the University’s mission (and enduring principles). Two letters of recommendation (the system will request these directly from referees). Optional Supporting Documents: Applicants may submit additional documents relevant to their application, such as examples of outreach activities, teaching evaluations, or publications. Why Villanova University? Villanova University fosters an inclusive academic environment where scholars from all backgrounds can thrive. The Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science is part of a vibrant academic and regional community dedicated to fostering belonging, supporting underrepresented groups in STEM, and advancing cutting-edge research. In addition to becoming a member of the Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science, the successful applicant will become part of the newly established Villanova One Sky Center for Astrophysics, an interdisciplinary center devoted to advancing equity in astrophysics. We further provide mentoring and professional development opportunities through university-wide initiatives including VISIBLE: Villanova Initiative to Support Inclusiveness and Build Leaders. About the Fellowship: The Mendel Postdoctoral Fellowship offers competitive salary with travel funds and benefits, access to professional development workshops, and opportunities to collaborate within a supportive academic community. Fellows will have access to resources that enhance research and teaching excellence, preparing them for the next stage of their academic careers. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20251202F Position Title: Postdoctoral Fellowship in Stellar Astrophysics Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Department: 182-Astronomy and Planetary Science Position Summary: Villanova University’s Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science invites applications for the Mendel Postdoctoral Research Fellowship. The Mendel Fellowship is a flagship postdoctoral opportunity for candidates seeking to advance their academic careers. The fellowship provides comprehensive training and development in research, teaching, and service. The successful applicant will join Dr. Kelly Hambleton’s research group and work on cutting-edge projects in binary systems and asteroseismology. Current topics of interest include solar-like oscillators in binary systems, tidally excited pulsations, and RR Lyrae stars. Our research extensively utilizes data from Kepler, TESS , and Gaia, and we are actively involved in the Rubin LSST’s Transiting and Variable Science Collaboration. Alongside research, the fellow will teach undergraduate core science courses/labs for non- STEM majors, focusing on integrating problem-solving, laboratory experience, technology, quantitative tools, and interdisciplinary understanding. The fellow will also actively engage in departmental activities, contributing to research and education initiatives that shape the department’s future. The Mendel Postdoctoral Fellowship is a 2-year appointment with the possibility of extension for an additional year. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: The successful applicant will: Uphold and contribute to the department’s culture of diversity, equity, and inclusion, demonstrating respect for all students, staff, and faculty. Conduct state-of-the-art research in computational stellar astrophysics. Teach two sections of Mendel core science courses or labs per semester (current courses include “How Old is the Universe?”, “Life in the Universe”, “Planetary Skies and Landscapes”, “Birth and Death of Stars”, “Earth: Our Habitable World”, and “Earth: A Cosmic Connection”). Mentor undergraduate students, including those from underrepresented backgrounds in STEM . Participate in departmental affairs such as meetings, colloquia, public events, and outreach initiatives, contributing to the department’s reputation locally, nationally, and internationally. Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Physics, Astrophysics, Data Science, or a closely related discipline is required. Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated ability to work effectively with individuals from diverse backgrounds and contribute to inclusive environments in research, teaching, or outreach. Experience advocating for diversity, equity, and inclusion within academic or professional settings. Prior experience teaching STEM courses to non- STEM majors. Strong background in physics, astrophysics, statistics, and programming. Experience mentoring students or junior researchers, particularly from underrepresented groups. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Villanova University is committed to fostering an inclusive academic environment and strongly encourages individuals from historically underrepresented groups in STEM to apply. Applications will be reviewed starting March 1, 2025 , but will be accepted until the position is filled. Required Application Materials: A cover letter expressing interest in the position. A current and complete CV. A research statement (2-page maximum). A teaching statement (2-page maximum). A statement on your contribution to University’s mission reflecting on how your teaching, research and service contributes to the University’s value orientation as discussed in the University’s mission (and enduring principles). Two letters of recommendation (the system will request these directly from referees). Optional Supporting Documents: Applicants may submit additional documents relevant to their application, such as examples of outreach activities, teaching evaluations, or publications. Why Villanova University? Villanova University fosters an inclusive academic environment where scholars from all backgrounds can thrive. The Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science is part of a vibrant academic and regional community dedicated to fostering belonging, supporting underrepresented groups in STEM , and advancing cutting-edge research. In addition to becoming a member of the Department of Astrophysics and Planetary Science, the successful applicant will become part of the newly established Villanova One Sky Center for Astrophysics, an interdisciplinary center devoted to advancing equity in astrophysics. We further provide mentoring and professional development opportunities through university-wide initiatives including VISIBLE : Villanova Initiative to Support Inclusiveness and Build Leaders. About the Fellowship: The Mendel Postdoctoral Fellowship offers competitive salary with travel funds and benefits, access to professional development workshops, and opportunities to collaborate within a supportive academic community. Fellows will have access to resources that enhance research and teaching excellence, preparing them for the next stage of their academic careers. Posting Date: 01/31/2025 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 03/15/2025 Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 2 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36540": {
      "title": "Event Chef - Catering (On Call)",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Event Chef - Catering (On Call) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Event Chef - Catering (On Call) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. On call status - schedule will be determined based on needs of the department and various catering functions. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260029T Position Title: Event Chef - Catering (On Call) Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: casual/seasonal Approximate Number of Hours per Week Department: 423-Catering Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. The Event Chef will support and execute catered events per instructions from the Executive Chef on an as needed basis. Acts as lead culinarian for events by supervising the work of the Event Cooks who are on staff during large events. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : This position will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the values of the Villanova Mission and the Dining Services Mission Statement. This position will focus on our Core Values: Sanitation, Friendly Courteous Service, Quality, Meticulous Attention to Detail, and Safety. Prepare and execute menus for catering events, ensuring consistency and high-quality presentation. Collaborate with event planners to accommodate dietary preferences and special requests. Set up and break down cooking stations at event venues, ensuring compliance with food safety and sanitation standards. Manage food inventory, prep work, and ensure timely service during events. Assist with menu planning and suggest creative dishes that align with seasonal ingredients and event themes. Monitor portion control and minimize food waste. Supervise kitchen staff and support team members in a dynamic environment. Maintain a clean, organized, and efficient workspace during events. Adhere to all health and safety regulations while handling food and kitchen equipment. NONESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Assist in day time prep for events Minimum Qualifications: Work Experience: Kitchen experience Work Skills: Strong verbal and written communication skills Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education: Culinary degree, preferred Work Experience: Experience in high end and high volume restaurants or catering, preferred Specific Job Knowledge: Proven experience as a chef in catering, banquets, or event-based cooking. Strong knowledge of various cooking techniques, cuisines, and food presentation. Ability to work well under pressure and adapt to different event settings. Excellent time management and organizational skills. Food Handler’s Certification (or willingness to obtain). Ability to lift up to 50 lbs. and stand for extended periods. Flexible schedule, including availability on weekends, evenings, and holidays as needed. Reliable transportation to various event locations. Equipment Knowledge: Knowledge of modern cooking equipment and practices Other: Team player with a willingness to listen to direction and get the job done Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery, and equipment used: Must have a comprehensive understanding of knife work, time and temperature regulating systems, and ability to work with hot equipment. Environmental conditions: Must be able to work in a loud, hot, noisy environment. Physical requirements: Must be able to work on feet for an extended period of time. Must be able to lift 40 lbs. Special Message to Applicants: On call status – schedule will be determined based on needs of the department and various catering functions. EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: 10/09/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Up to $30.00/hour Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33444": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Humanitarian Engineering",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Humanitarian Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Humanitarian Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. We will be accepting applications throughout the year and will only fill teaching needs as they arise. Applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications are to include a letter of interest (including the name and contact information for at least 3 references), current and complete curriculum vitae, transcripts and a statement describing your teaching philosophy including courses you are interested in teaching. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2021835F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Humanitarian Engineering Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 201-Dean-Engineering Position Summary: Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Humanitarian Engineering for graduate courses taught in the evening and/or undergraduate courses taught during the day. The Center for Humanitarian Engineering and International Development offers programs leading to a minor in Humanitarian Engineering and offers a series of courses within the graduate program in Sustainable Engineering that includes topics related to international development. It supports research and curriculum development related to sustainable development which is integrated with M.S. degrees and participates in the College of Engineering Ph.D. degree program. The Center for Humanitarian Engineering and International Development was established in 2020 as an outgrowth from the Villanova Engineering Service Learning Program. The Center partners with non-profit organizations globally for the purposes of creating unique experiential learning opportunities for students and faculty wherein outreach efforts are integrated with research and curriculum in support of poverty alleviation and global challenges related to sustainable development. The Center is rooted in ethical engagement with global partners and genuinely believes that partnership, empowerment and humility are key elements of addressing global issues. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and related duties will vary based on the specific course(s) being taught. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree required. Applicants must be committed to excellence in engineering education. Preferred Qualifications: A doctorate in Engineering or closely allied discipline is strongly preferred. Previous teaching experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: We will be accepting applications throughout the year and will only fill teaching needs as they arise. Applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications are to include a letter of interest (including the name and contact information for at least 3 references), current and complete curriculum vitae, transcripts and a statement describing your teaching philosophy including courses you are interested in teaching. Posting Date: 08/19/2021 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,650.00 – $2,600.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: N/A Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35108": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Environmental Engineering (Microbiology)",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Environmental Engineering (Microbiology) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Environmental Engineering (Microbiology) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications are to include: A letter of interest (including the name and contact information for at least 3 references) Current and complete curriculum vitae Statement describing your teaching philosophy including courses you are interested in teaching. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260036F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Environmental Engineering (Microbiology) Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/9-months Department: 202-Civil and Environmental Engineering Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people. Even as a part-time employee, you will receive access to certain benefits, including tuition assistance and more . Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Civil and Environmental Engineering for graduate courses taught in the evening and/or undergraduate courses taught during the day. The Civil and Environmental Engineering Department offers programs leading to the B.S. and M.S. degrees and participates in the College of Engineering Ph.D. degree program. For this position, we are specifically looking for an adjunct faculty member to teach the graduate level course CEE 7511 Microbiology Environmental Engineering. The course description is as follows: Introduction to microbiology and biochemistry; bacteria, fungi, algae, protozoa, and viruses; structure, function, synthesis, and degradation of lipids, proteins, nucleic acids, and carbohydrates; nutritional requirements for microbial growth; waterborne disease; indicator organisms; microbial ecology; and microbiology of the nitrifiers, methanogens, and sulfur bacteria. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and other duties which vary with specific courses. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree required. The applicant must be committed to excellence in engineering education. Preferred Qualifications: An earned doctorate in Civil Engineering or closely allied discipline is strongly preferred. Previous teaching experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Undergraduate courses are offered during the day; graduate courses during the evening. Graduate courses include a synchronous component. Special Message to Applicants: Applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications are to include: A letter of interest (including the name and contact information for at least 3 references) Current and complete curriculum vitae Statement describing your teaching philosophy including courses you are interested in teaching. Posting Date: 05/21/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,650.00 – $2,600.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
