    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36424": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty, Management Information Systems",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Tenure Track Faculty, Management Information Systems Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Tenure Track Faculty, Management Information Systems To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu/. Review of applications begins immediately and continues until position is filled. All initial applications are to include : • Application letter • Curriculum vitae • Unofficial Graduate Transcripts • Sample of working papers • Names of three references who will be contacted via email to submit confidential letters of recommendation when the application is submitted. • Finalists will be expected to provide a statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions may support the University mission (and enduring principles) . Please refer to the departmental website and the Villanova University Mission Statement. Other information may be required if the candidate makes it into the interview round. For technical assistance, please contact us at 610-519-7900, 610-519-7616, or jobshelp@villanova.edu. Application related questions may be sent to Dr. Wenhong Luo, Search Committee Chair, (wenhong.luo@villanova.edu). Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260076F Position Title: Tenure Track Faculty, Management Information Systems Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 217-Accountancy Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Department of Accounting and Information Systems at the Villanova School of Business is seeking applications for a tenure-track position in Management Information Systems ( MIS ) to begin in Fall 2027 at the rank of Assistant Professor or Associate Professor. This faculty member will report to the Chair of the Accounting and Information Systems Department and is expected to (1) teach both undergraduate and graduate courses in Artificial Intelligence as well as other MIS areas, (2) publish in top MIS journals, (3) perform service, and (4) contribute to a collegial academic environment. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teach MIS courses in both the undergraduate and graduate programs. Competitive teaching loads are offered based on research output. Publish in any area of MIS primarily targeting top peer-reviewed academic journals listed on the Villanova School of Business journal list. Perform service commensurate with faculty rank. Minimum Qualifications: Ph.D. in IS or MIS or a closely related field Potential to publish in top peer-reviewed academic MIS journals For candidates seeking appointment at the Associate Professor level : Have an established record of peer-reviewed publications in top MIS journals Evidence of multi-year teaching with strong evaluations Preferred Qualifications: Demonstrated track record of high-quality teaching Evidence of high-quality scholarly research Demonstrated ability to collaborate with colleagues Dissertation on an aspect of Artificial Intelligence Potential to teach courses in Artificial Intelligence For candidates seeking appointment at the Associate Professor level : Evidence of high-quality teaching at both undergraduate and graduate levels Evidence of teaching experience in AI-related courses An editorial role or a service/leadership role within the profession Industry experience Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu/. Review of applications begins immediately and continues until position is filled. All initial applications are to include : • Application letter • Curriculum vitae • Unofficial Graduate Transcripts • Sample of working papers • Names of three references who will be contacted via email to submit confidential letters of recommendation when the application is submitted. • Finalists will be expected to provide a statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions may support the University mission (and enduring principles) . Please refer to the departmental website and the Villanova University Mission Statement. Other information may be required if the candidate makes it into the interview round. For technical assistance, please contact us at 610-519-7900, 610-519-7616, or jobshelp@villanova.edu. Application related questions may be sent to Dr. Wenhong Luo, Search Committee Chair, (wenhong.luo@villanova.edu). Posting Date: 09/22/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Writing Sample/Publications Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) Statement of Contribution to Mission © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
