    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35908": {
      "title": "Tenure Track Faculty, Accounting and Information Systems",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Tenure Track Faculty, Accounting and Information Systems Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Tenure Track Faculty, Accounting and Information Systems To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu/. Review of applications begins immediately and continues until position is filled. All initial applications are to include: • Application letter • Curriculum vitae • Unofficial Graduate Transcripts • Sample of working papers • Names of three references • Finalists will be expected to provide a statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions may support the University mission (and enduring principles) . Please refer to the departmental website and the Villanova University Mission Statement. Please ensure that materials evidence qualifications and address duties and responsibilities. Other information will be required if the candidate makes it into the interview round. For technical assistance, please contact us at 610-519-7900, 610-519-7616, or jobshelp@villanova.edu. Application related questions may be sent to Dr. Denise Hanes Downey, Associate Chair and KPMG Endowed Professor in Accounting (denise.downey@villanova.edu). Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260060F Position Title: Tenure Track Faculty, Accounting and Information Systems Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 217-Accountancy Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Department of Accounting and Information Systems in the Villanova School of Business is seeking applications for a Tenure Track position beginning Fall 2027. This person will report to the Chair of the Accounting and Information Systems Department. Our primary recruiting focus is at the rank of Assistant Professor; both recent graduates and experienced Assistant Professors are encouraged to apply. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: This person will primarily teach courses at the undergraduate level, and is expected to incorporate AI and other discipline-related emerging technologies into related coursework. The faculty member is expected to publish high quality research in any area of accounting, targeting top peer-reviewed academic journals. Service expectations are commensurate with hiring level and candidate’s prior experience, and will include participating in curriculum development activities and engagement with students, alumni and the broader accounting community. Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. with some relevant teaching experience, potential to publish in high quality journals, and a willingness to work in a collegial environment. Preferred Qualifications: A Ph.D. with a demonstrated track record of high-quality teaching across courses in the financial and managerial accounting series as well as evidence of excellence in working with students. An ability to innovate within the curriculum. Professional experience with a CPA license is also preferred. Demonstrated willingness to work with other faculty and contribute to a collegial environment. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu/. Review of applications begins immediately and continues until position is filled. All initial applications are to include: • Application letter • Curriculum vitae • Unofficial Graduate Transcripts • Sample of working papers • Names of three references • Finalists will be expected to provide a statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions may support the University mission (and enduring principles) . Please refer to the departmental website and the Villanova University Mission Statement. Please ensure that materials evidence qualifications and address duties and responsibilities. Other information will be required if the candidate makes it into the interview round. For technical assistance, please contact us at 610-519-7900, 610-519-7616, or jobshelp@villanova.edu. Application related questions may be sent to Dr. Denise Hanes Downey, Associate Chair and KPMG Endowed Professor in Accounting (denise.downey@villanova.edu). Posting Date: 08/03/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). 