    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36353": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Major Giving, Southeast",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Assistant Director of Major Giving, Southeast Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Assistant Director of Major Giving, Southeast To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260431S Position Title: Assistant Director of Major Giving, Southeast Position Type: Staff Location: Palm Beach, FL Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 604 - University Advancement Position Summary: Ignite Your Career at Villanova University! Whether undergraduate or graduate, faculty or staff, each community member brings with them a wealth of experiences that enrich our University and shift our perspectives. As a part of this community, your work will improve lives and ignite change! Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. · Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. · Villanova’s most precious asset is our people. As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Villanova University has embarked on a 10-year strategic plan, Rooted. Restless., with the goal of enhancing the Augustinian Catholic living and learning experience for all members of our community. University Advancement is seeking exceptional talent to join our mission-driven team working together toward our shared vision for Villanova, fueled by the generosity of the University’s philanthropic supporters as we “keep moving” in the spirit of St. Augustine in the public phase of Villanova’s comprehensive capital campaign: Espiritus Nova. Reporting to the Sr. Director of Major Giving for the Mid-Atlantic and Southeast, the Assistant Director of Major Giving, Southeast serves a frontline fundraiser in Villanova’s key Southeast markets. This position is responsible for establishing and managing effective relationships with varied prospects and existing donors. As a member of the regional major giving team, this individual will play a critical role in advancing the University’s strategic priorities and fundraising goals. The Assistant Director of Major Giving, Southeast will identify, qualify, cultivate, solicit and steward major gift prospects and donors, developing individualized engagement strategies that inspire philanthropic support. As a remotely based member of the regional development team, the Assistant Director must be highly organized, self-motivated, and comfortable working independently while remaining closely connected to colleagues across University Advancement. Success in this role requires strong initiative, accountability, effective time-management, and the ability to proactively develop and advance a major gift portfolio with minimal day-to-day supervision. The Assistant Director, Southeast is expected to conduct 10-12 meaningful prospect visits per month and manage a portfolio of 125 prospects with philanthropic capacity of $100,000 or greater and take ownership of advancing relationships throughout the donor lifecycle. The portfolio will be primarily based in Florida with expected travel to other regions within the Southeast region, including Georgia, New Orleans and Tennessee. In partnership with the Senior Director, the Assistant Director will help strengthen and expand Villanova’s fundraising presence throughout the Southeast. The individual will work closely with colleagues across Advancement, including Stewardship, Alumni Relations, and University leadership to grow and enhance the successful fundraising program in the Southeast within the context of Villanova University’s overall fundraising efforts. The incumbent will also support prospect engagement and involvement efforts related to cultivation and fundraising events in the Southeast region. This position is based remotely in Florida, with strong preference for candidates residing in Naples or Palm Beach and requires regular travel throughout the Southeast region, and quarterly trips to campus (Philadelphia). Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Identify and manage a portfolio of at least 125 prospects which includes alumni and parents. Working from pipelines will be expected with support to review zip code and other data as needed. Establish and manage effective relationships with portfolio prospects and donors; conduct a minimum of 10-12 prospect visits monthly and assume stewardship responsibilities for assigned prospects. This will be measured by weekly metrics including quantity and type of outreach. Plan and implement prospect cultivation and solicitation strategies developing work and stewardship plans; identify and evaluate potential donors from available research, peer screenings, and event participation. Report results to Sr. Director of Major Giving and develop outreach plan. Support prospect engagement and involvement efforts for University-wide events and programs taking place in the Southeast. Be a point of contact for Florida-based constituents to engage in the life of the University; encourage participation in activities and evaluate potential for development involvement. In conjunction with the Sr. Director of Major Giving, Mid-Atlantic and Southeast, provide support to the Southeast campaign committee. In conjunction with the Sr. Director of Major Giving, Mid-Atlantic and Southeast assist in coordinating development activities. Perform additional duties and assist with special projects and events as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required. Three to five years of experience as a frontline fundraiser in higher education or non-profit sector. Proven successful experience in individual fundraising or related sales/business development experience required. Experience dealing with major gift prospects required, preferably in the field of higher education and/or within the Florida non-profit philanthropic community. Commitment to the principles behind higher education and a strong desire to associate with Villanova University and champion its mission expected. Understanding of the University culture and ability to work within a multi-layered management system required. Ability and willingness to travel required. Excellent communication, interpersonal and analytical skills required. Must be well organized and detail oriented. The incumbent must be comfortable working in a team-oriented environment, as well as a disciplined self-starter who is results-oriented. Knowledge of general office equipment, including use of laptop computers, printers required. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree preferred. A minimum of two years working with major and/or principle gifts preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Regular travel to the Philadelphia-area expected. Occasional evening and weekend work and travel required. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 09/11/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 18 and the range is $118,400-131,500. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 18 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33258": {
      "title": "Finneran Pavilion Guest Services Supervisor",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Finneran Pavilion Guest Services Supervisor Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Finneran Pavilion Guest Services Supervisor To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20250632T Position Title: Finneran Pavilion Guest Services Supervisor Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: temporary Approximate Number of Hours per Week Department: 730-Athl - The Pavilion Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . As a member of the Villanova University Athletics staff, the Guest Services Staff Supervisor plays a vital role in maximizing the game day experience for Villanova Wildcat basketball fans. This role serves as both a supervisor of Guest Services Event Staff and an active team member, assisting fans and ensuring smooth event operations. The Guest Services Staff Supervisor supports fans in premium clubs, provides game day information, and fosters a welcoming environment. This is a seasonal part-time role that provides support during basketball, football, and select other events. All duties must be completed in compliance with University and NCAA rules and regulations. Duties and Responsibilities: Exceed customer service expectations of all Wildcat community members. Understand and practice policies and procedures set by Villanova University Athletics. Attend customer service team member training and maintain comprehensive knowledge of game day information, rules, and regulations. Go above and beyond to enhance game day experience Minimum Qualifications: 3+ years of experience 18 years of age or older Must be available nights, weekends, and holidays Ability to stand, walk, and climb stairs throughout the duration of the event Required to occasionally lift 10 pounds, unaided. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to work well with others and provide leadership to a team. Problem-solving skills with the ability to think quickly and remain calm in high-pressure situations. Positive attitude toward taking on additional job responsibilities. Good judgment and decision-making skills. Authorization to work in the United States of America Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Ability to stand, walk, and climb stairs throughout the duration of the event Required to occasionally lift 10 pounds, unaided. Special Message to Applicants: EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: 06/21/2023 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $19.50 per hour Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as: • Any person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and • Such contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU. Examples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following: • Parents/Legal Guardians • Coaches (high school, college, club) • Personal/Skills Trainers • Relatives • Strength Coach • Advisors Consistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any: • Basketball (men’s or women’s) prospective student-athletes (grades 9-12) or their parents, relatives or coaches? Y N Yes No * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as: • Any person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and • Such contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU. Examples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following: • Parents/Legal Guardians • Coaches (high school, college, club) • Personal/Skills Trainers • Relatives • Strength Coach • Advisors Consistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any: • Current VU basketball (men’s or women’s) student-athletes? Y N Yes No Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
