    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36148": {
      "title": "Lawson Family Business Fellow in Fashion",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Lawson Family Business Fellow in Fashion Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Lawson Family Business Fellow in Fashion To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications will be reviewed as they are submitted with the goal of having some appointed as the Lawson Family Business Fellow in the Fall 2026 for academic year 2026-2027 (Fall 2026 and Spring 2027) with the potential for renewal for future academic years. This part-time faculty position is intended to be 20 hours a week with an on-campus presence needed to support the responsibilities associated with the role. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260070F Position Title: Lawson Family Business Fellow in Fashion Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 257-Clay Center Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people. Even as a part-time employee, you will receive access to certain benefits, including tuition assistance and more . The Lawson Fellow will collaborate with key campus partners to shape and execute the future of Villanova’s Business of Fashion Society (BoFS), while building a university-wide network to engage students interested in business-focused fashion careers. Serving as advisor to the BoFS, the Lawson Fellow will set annual goals in collaboration with the student leaders and VSB’s O’Donnell Center for Professional Development. The Lawson Fellow will oversee business of fashion and beauty industry-related career education opportunities and guide signature initiatives such as the annual Business of Fashion Symposium and client-based Immersion Projects. The role includes partnering with career education leaders to strengthen VSB’s student business society culture, expanding industry-focused programming and resources, and engaging alumni and employers to create experiential learning, professional development, and career opportunities. Additionally, the Lawson Fellow will provide individual and group career coaching for students and may teach a special topics course focused on fashion and beauty industry trends and dynamics. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Collaborate with VSB O’Donnell Center for Professional Development Assistant Dean and team, VU Career Center, and College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Ellis Center for Professional Development to vision the future of the business of fashion/beauty initiatives and develop execution plan. Develop university-wide network for engaging all Villanova students interested in the fashion/beauty industry initiatives. Serve as Advisor for the Business of Fashion Society (BoFS) and related activities; regularly conduct update meetings and communicate with the executive board to establish annual goals, plan for academic year activities, monitor on-going activities, etc. Guide BoFS in planning the annual Business of Fashion Symposium, including helping secure speakers and developing agenda. Assist with developing and expanding BoFS client-based Immersion Project initiative; help to source clients and provide guidance to Project Teams. Work in partnership with O’Donnell Center Director of Career Education & Student Initiatives to contribute to advancement of VSB’s student business society culture and identify opportunities to assist with other groups. Engage Villanova alumni and other employers in fashion/beauty industries to create opportunities for TREKs (employer site visits), professional development, and career opportunities. Expand programming and compile relevant resources for students interested in fashion/beauty industries. Host 1:1 coaching appointments and group sessions with students to provide industry-related career and professional development guidance. Potential to teach special topics course based on fashion/beauty industry dynamics and emerging trends. Produce an annual report to the Lawson Family on the activities of the Lawson Fellow and Business of Fashion Society. On-campus presence throughout the semester for meetings and programs. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree. Professional experience working in fashion, beauty, luxury, and/or related industries and current network of contacts in those industries. Experience with and/or understanding of the importance of an intentional approach to college student career and professional development. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: On-campus presence required throughout the semester for meetings and programs. Special Message to Applicants: Applications will be reviewed as they are submitted with the goal of having some appointed as the Lawson Family Business Fellow in the Fall 2026 for academic year 2026-2027 (Fall 2026 and Spring 2027) with the potential for renewal for future academic years. This part-time faculty position is intended to be 20 hours a week with an on-campus presence needed to support the responsibilities associated with the role. Posting Date: 08/25/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents Other Document Statement of Contribution to Mission © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/30948": {
      "title": "Continuing Non Tenure-Track Faculty in Mechanics and Materials in the Department of Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Continuing Non Tenure-Track Faculty in Mechanics and Materials in the Department of Mechanical Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Continuing Non Tenure-Track Faculty in Mechanics and Materials in the Department of Mechanical Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Villanova is a Carnegie-classified doctoral university and the Mechanical Engineering faculty are internationally recognized for their research and teaching. The department has 23 full-time faculty members, approximately 300 undergraduate students, and 150 graduate students. We are committed to providing a rigorous educational experience in the discipline of mechanical engineering, graduating well-rounded leaders and life-long learners, who aspire to achieving professional excellence. We are equally committed to the discovery, dissemination, advancement, and application of cutting-edge research. Inspired by the Augustinian-Catholic tradition, we value an inclusive and diverse community in which we prepare our students to demonstrate the highest ethical conduct and contribute to the well-being of humankind. The Department of Mechanical Engineering and the College of Engineering are deeply committed to work-life balance and family-friendly programs for our faculty. This commitment is realized in strong collaborative relationships between our department and faculty with the Office of Diversity, Equity and Inclusion, the McNulty Institute for Women’s Leadership, and the VISIBLE (Villanova Initiative to Support Inclusiveness and Build Leaders) Office. The University is located 12 miles from Philadelphia along the historic Main Line. From its founding in 1842 to its position today as a nationally recognized leading university, Villanova University has forged a path of academic excellence. Please submit your applications at: http://jobs.villanova.edu. Application materials should include a cover letter, CV, transcript, teaching philosophy and the names of three references. The review process will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2022895F Position Title: Continuing Non Tenure-Track Faculty in Mechanics and Materials in the Department of Mechanical Engineering Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 205-Mechanical Engineering Position Summary: The Department of Mechanical Engineering at Villanova University has an opening for a full-time, continuing non tenure-track assistant professor position in the area of mechanics and materials. This is an academic year appointment, renewable subject to enrollment needs, availability of funding, and performance. The position starts in August 2022. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: The candidate will be expected to teach undergraduate core and laboratory courses in mechanical engineering, especially in the area of mechanics and materials. Other responsibilities include coordinating and maintaining course related laboratory equipment, mentoring undergraduate students, K-12 outreach, and developing new pedagogical methods. Minimum Qualifications: Requirements include a Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering or a closely related field and a demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence and innovation. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Villanova is a Carnegie-classified doctoral university and the Mechanical Engineering faculty are internationally recognized for their research and teaching. The department has 23 full-time faculty members, approximately 300 undergraduate students, and 150 graduate students. We are committed to providing a rigorous educational experience in the discipline of mechanical engineering, graduating well-rounded leaders and life-long learners, who aspire to achieving professional excellence. We are equally committed to the discovery, dissemination, advancement, and application of cutting-edge research. Inspired by the Augustinian-Catholic tradition, we value an inclusive and diverse community in which we prepare our students to demonstrate the highest ethical conduct and contribute to the well-being of humankind. The Department of Mechanical Engineering and the College of Engineering are deeply committed to work-life balance and family-friendly programs for our faculty. This commitment is realized in strong collaborative relationships between our department and faculty with the Office of Diversity, Equity and Inclusion, the McNulty Institute for Women’s Leadership, and the VISIBLE (Villanova Initiative to Support Inclusiveness and Build Leaders) Office. The University is located 12 miles from Philadelphia along the historic Main Line. From its founding in 1842 to its position today as a nationally recognized leading university, Villanova University has forged a path of academic excellence. Please submit your applications at: http://jobs.villanova.edu. Application materials should include a cover letter, CV, transcript, teaching philosophy and the names of three references. The review process will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Date: 01/31/2022 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive. Salary Band: N/A Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
