    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36488": {
      "title": "Recreation Center Attendant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Recreation Center Attendant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Recreation Center Attendant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260067V Position Title: Recreation Center Attendant Posting Type Student Hours/week: 1.5 - 20 hours/week Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Cabrini Detailed Work Schedule This position has various shifts between 6 AM and 11 PM. Number of positions: Until all are filled Department: 775-Athl - Intramurals Contact Name: Michael Hay Contact Phone/Extension: 6105196573 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Recreation Center Attendants will work under the direction and supervision of the Recreation Center Operations Coordinator and student Recreation Center Supervisors to carry out the overall, day-to-day operations in The Dixon Center and surrounding outdoor recreational facilities. Recreation Center Attendants will largely be responsible for enforcing recreation center policies and procedures, providing a positive customer-service experience for the community, and acting as a first responder in the event of an emergency. Requirements: Monitor recreational facilities and enforce recreation center policies and procedures, ensuring a safe environment for recreational activities. Stay current on fitness and recreation programs and operational procedures to provide exceptional customer service to Villanova community members. Create a welcoming and positive experience for users. Check, clean, and assist in the maintenance of fitness and recreation equipment. Provide basic instruction on the proper operation of cardiovascular and weight training equipment. Notify appropriate staff members of custodial issues, maintenance needs, and safety concerns. Assist with facility set-up and breakdown for a variety of events. Assist with the reservation, distribution, and collection of fitness and recreation equipment. Launder gym towels. Enact and/or assist in emergency response. Attend ongoing employee training sessions. Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: May be asked to carry/move fitness and recreation equipment. Must be able to lift 45 lbs. May be asked to perform duties at outdoor recreational facilities, in various seasons with the possibility of inclement weather. Wage Rate: $10.00/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Other Document Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33427": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Ethics",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Ethics Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Ethics To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Ethics Program will accept applications through April 2022. All applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The cover letter should address the candidate's competency to teach ETH 2050 and should include the names and the contact information of three references. 3. A statement of teaching philosophy. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2022923F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Ethics Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/9-months Department: 171-Ethics Position Summary: Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in the Ethics Program for undergraduate courses only. The applicant must be committed to excellence in the teaching of a core curriculum course, ETH 2050. This interdisciplinary course is the last of five foundational core courses that most Villanova undergraduates take. The Good Life: Ethics and Contemporary Moral Problems provides the students an opportunity to explore the rich philosophical and theological resources available for the ongoing exploration of what constitutes a good life. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teach 1-3 sections of ETH 2050, hold regular weekly office hours. Minimum Qualifications: Advanced degree in philosophy or theology, AOS Ethics Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience preferred, Ph.D. in hand preferred Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The Ethics Program will accept applications through April 2022. All applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The cover letter should address the candidate’s competency to teach ETH 2050 and should include the names and the contact information of three references. 3. A statement of teaching philosophy. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: 04/01/2022 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,160.00 – $2,230.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 2 Maximum Number of References Needed 2 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Transcripts Summary of Teaching Evaluations © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
