    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36434": {
      "title": "Emergency Manager",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Emergency Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Emergency Manager To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260401S Position Title: Emergency Manager Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 808-Environmental Safety Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more The Emergency Manager provides leadership, coordination, and administration of Villanova University’s comprehensive all-hazards emergency management program. Reporting to the Director of Environmental Health and Safety, this position is responsible for developing, implementing, and continuously improving emergency preparedness, mitigation, response, recovery, continuity, and resilience programs across the University’s campuses and operations. The Emergency Manager works collaboratively with University leadership, Public Safety, Facilities Management, Student Life, University Communications, the Office of the Provost, University Information Technology, Athletics, Research Administration, and external partners to ensure institutional readiness for emergencies and disruptive events. The position serves as the University’s primary coordinator for emergency management planning, preparedness training, exercises, incident support, continuity planning, and emergency management program development. The Emergency Manager develops and maintains emergency operations plans, annexes, procedures, and preparedness initiatives that support the University’s ability to protect life, maintain critical functions, sustain academic and business operations, and recover efficiently from emergencies. The position coordinates institutional emergency preparedness efforts across multiple campuses and supports major events, special events, and other activities requiring emergency planning and coordination. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Emergency Management Program Leadership Serves as the University’s primary coordinator for emergency management activities, including preparedness, mitigation, response, recovery, continuity, and resilience initiatives. Develops, implements, and evaluates emergency management policies, procedures, standards, and programs. Coordinates institutional emergency preparedness initiatives across University departments, campuses, and operational areas. Provides guidance and consultation to University leadership regarding emergency preparedness and emergency management best practices. Maintains awareness of emerging threats, regulatory requirements, and industry best practices applicable to higher education emergency management. Planning, Preparedness, and Continuity Develops, maintains, and updates the University’s Emergency Operations Plan and supporting annexes, procedures, and event-specific plans. Coordinates continuity planning initiatives to support the continuation and recovery of critical University functions, services, research activities, and academic operations. Conducts hazard vulnerability analyses, preparedness assessments, and program evaluations to identify risks and continuous improvement opportunities. Supports development of mitigation strategies and preparedness initiatives to strengthen institutional resilience. Maintains emergency management records, planning documentation, and compliance-related materials. Emergency Response, Recovery, and Incident Support Supports University response and recovery activities during emergencies, incidents, planned events, and disruptive situations. Coordinates Emergency Operations Center activation, readiness, staffing, documentation, and support activities with internal partners. Maintains situational awareness, incident documentation, resource tracking, and status reporting during emergency events. Coordinates post-incident reviews (hot washes), after-action reports, corrective action planning, and improvement initiatives. Facilitates coordination with external emergency management agencies, public safety organizations, government entities, and community partners during incidents and recovery efforts. Training, Exercises, and Community Outreach Develops and delivers emergency preparedness training and educational programs for students, faculty, staff, and University stakeholders. Plans, facilitates, and evaluates tabletop, functional, and full-scale exercises designed to test University plans and capabilities. Coordinates emergency preparedness awareness campaigns and outreach activities. Manages corrective action processes arising from exercises, drills, and emergency events. Supports compliance with emergency drill, exercise, and preparedness requirements. Campus Partnerships and External Coordination Develops and maintains collaborative relationships with University departments and external agencies that support emergency preparedness and response activities. Serves as a liaison with local, county, state, federal, and regional emergency management organizations. Supports emergency planning and preparedness activities associated with major events, athletic events, commencement/ceremonial exercises, conferences, and other special activities. Participates in committees, working groups, and planning teams related to emergency preparedness and institutional resilience. Program Administration Coordinates program metrics, documentation, records management, budgeting support, equipment readiness, and other administrative functions necessary to support emergency management operations. Other duties as assigned Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Emergency Management, Homeland Security, Public Administration, Public Safety Administration, Environmental Health and Safety, Business Continuity, Criminal Justice, or a closely related field. Comprehensive knowledge of emergency management principles and practices, including preparedness, mitigation, response, recovery, continuity, and resilience. National Incident Management System ( NIMS ) Incident Command System ( ICS ) Emergency Operations Center operations Higher education emergency management principles Emergency exercise design and evaluation Business continuity and continuity of operations planning Hazard vulnerability assessment methodologies Emergency communications and notification systems Clery Act emergency response and evacuation requirements Relevant federal, state, and local emergency management guidance and regulations Required FEMA IS-100 FEMA IS-200 FEMA IS-700 FEMA IS-800 Five (5) years of progressively responsible experience in emergency management, emergency preparedness, business continuity, disaster recovery, public safety, homeland security, military emergency management, public health preparedness, or a closely related field. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in Emergency Management, Public Administration, Homeland Security, Public Health, Business Continuity, Risk Management, or a related discipline. Experience in higher education emergency management. Experience developing and implementing emergency management plans. Experience coordinating Emergency Operations Center activities. Experience developing and facilitating emergency exercises and drills. Experience supporting continuity planning and recovery operations. Experience working within complex organizations and multidisciplinary environments. ICS -300 ICS -400 G-191 Emergency Operations Center Management E/L 962: All-Hazards Position Specific Planning Section Chief IAEM – Associate Emergency Manager ( AEM ) IAEM – Certified Emergency Manager ( CEM ) Certified Business Continuity Professional ( CBCP ) Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Work is performed in both office and field environments. The position may be required to respond to emergencies outside normal business hours, including evenings, weekends, holidays, and during adverse weather conditions. Periodic travel between University campuses and off-site locations may be required. The position requires the ability to sit, stand, walk, communicate effectively, and operate computers, mobile devices, communications equipment, and other office technology for extended periods. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 09/25/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 17 and the range is $84,000-105,100. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 17 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35928": {
      "title": "Front of House Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Front of House Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Front of House Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20234737V Position Title: Front of House Assistant Posting Type Student Hours/week: 15-20 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2025-2026 Academic Year Location Mullen Center Detailed Work Schedule Working Evenings, Weekend Afternoon, Weekend Evenings Number of positions: 15 Department: 824 - Performing Arts Center Contact Name: Tina Sheing Contact Phone/Extension: 6105195006 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Provide Front of House ( FOH ) assistance (e.g. concessionaires, ushers) for MULLEN CENTER performances and events. Maintain knowledge of and positive relationship with University and patrons Assist patron complaints or inquiries. Requirements: Must be an excellent communicator within an academic environment with an ability to instruct, supervise, and clearly explain ticketing and front of house information and procedures to diverse audiences (e.g., creative personnel, undergrad/graduate students, production staff, other University departments, academic departments, and external clients). Excellent customer service skills and proven ability to develop and sustain productive relationships Additional Information: Physical Demands Summary: Standing for periods of time, some light lifting Wage Rate: $10.00-$13.00 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 07/02/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
