    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/34063": {
      "title": "CRF Student Ambassador",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | CRF Student Ambassador Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us CRF Student Ambassador To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260056V Position Title: CRF Student Ambassador Posting Type Student Hours/week: 10 Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Garey Hall Detailed Work Schedule CRF is open 9:00 AM- 5:00 PM Monday through Friday. Students work a minimum of 10 hours per week, typically in 2-4 hour shifts. Number of positions: 1 Department: 165- Office of U/G Research & Fellowships Contact Name: Kate Vicente Contact Phone/Extension: (610) 519-6138 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Summary : The Center for Research and Fellowships ( CRF ) administers three key areas of programming at Villanova University: student research, nationally competitive scholarships and fellowships, and the Presidential Scholars Program ( PSP ). CRF seeks an undergraduate student worker to support general office functions starting in Fall 2026. Student workers will have numerous opportunities to develop professional skills through writing, editing, outreach, and events. This position reports to CRF’s Senior Administrative Assistant. Responsibilities : Front Desk & Operations: Greeting all guests to the CRF -Office of Education Abroad ( OEA ) office suite; checking in appointments; answering in-person and phone inquiries; editorial projects; data projects; supporting CRF staff on programmatic needs. Events: Provide support with events, including the autumn Student Research Symposium, February Presidential Scholars Interview Program. Creating and editing promotional materials. Outreach: Assist in outreach and recruitment of candidates for external scholarships and fellowships, such as the Fulbright U.S. Student Program and other awards. Promote CRF through on-campus tabling and orientation events (occasionally on weekends/evenings). Other duties and projects as assigned. Requirements: Requirements : Students from any major or program on campus are welcome to apply for this position. We are looking for someone with: Strong interpersonal/customer service skills. This role involves frequent interaction with students, staff, and external stakeholders like Villanova applicants, parents, and high school guidance counselors including in person and on the phone An interest in writing, proofreading, and editorial work Willingness to take initiative Reliability, time management, and organizational skills This position requires the ability to discreetly manage sensitive information in accordance with University and FERPA confidentiality guidelines Additional Information: CRF is open 9:00 AM- 5:00 PM Monday through Friday. Students work a minimum of 10 hours per week, typically in 2-4 hour shifts. Physical Demands Summary: The job is physically comfortable and mostly requires a typical desk sitting position. Wage Rate: $13.00 per hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 07/09/2026 Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/35552": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Mechanical Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Mechanical Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Note : Screening of submitted applications begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Please submit your application at: https://jobs.villanova.edu/ and complete a faculty profile. Application packages must include: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Copies of Unofficial Academic Transcripts Statement Describing Your Teaching Philosophy (including courses you are interested in teaching) Names and contact information of three references Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260051F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Mechanical Engineering Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/12-months Department: 205-Mechanical Engineering Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. The Department of Mechanical Engineering seeks qualified individuals for its Adjunct Faculty Pool and welcomes applicants at any time. The Mechanical Engineering Department offers programs leading to BS and MS degrees and participates in the College of Engineering’s Ph.D. degree program. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching undergraduate and/or graduate level courses. Duties will vary with the specific courses being taught. Minimum Qualifications: Master’s degree required. The applicant must be committed to excellence in engineering education. Preferred Qualifications: An earned doctorate in Mechanical Engineering or a closely allied discipline is strongly preferred Previous teaching experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Note : Screening of submitted applications begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Please submit your application at: https://jobs.villanova.edu/ and complete a faculty profile. Application packages must include: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Copies of Unofficial Academic Transcripts Statement Describing Your Teaching Philosophy (including courses you are interested in teaching) Names and contact information of three references Posting Date: 07/02/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
