    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36500": {
      "title": "Research Analyst, Survey Research",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Research Analyst, Survey Research Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Research Analyst, Survey Research To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260451S Position Title: Research Analyst, Survey Research Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 704-Office of Strategic Planning and Institutional Effectiveness Position Summary: Under the general supervision of the Director for Survey Research and Evaluation, the Research Analyst will independently manage and conduct strategic surveys for the University. The Research Analyst will analyze data and create interactive data visualizations to support strategic decision-making. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Work on the development, administration, and reporting of strategic surveys that are part of the University’s Systematic Survey Cycle. Work on the development, administration, and reporting of surveys commissioned by university entities. Analyze and synthesize survey data into actionable insights that inform strategic decision-making, planning, policy development, assessment, and programming. Analyze qualitative comments generated from survey research projects, including editing, coding, thematic analysis, and summarization of findings for reports and presentations. Collaborate with University stakeholders to communicate survey findings and support evidence-based decision-making. Assist in the administration of Villanova’s sitewide Qualtrics license, including user/permission management, technical use inquiries, and encouraging best practices for data security and governance. Steward survey data and develop databases that support longitudinal reporting and trend analysis. Maintain current knowledge of survey methodology, assessment practices, data collection technologies, and emerging trends in survey research. Perform other duties and assist with projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelor’s degree in a research- or analytics-related field such as social sciences, educational research, statistics, psychology, sociology, public administration, data analytics, or a closely related discipline. Work Experience Three years of experience in survey research, institutional research, assessment, market research, program evaluation, data analytics, or a related field. Work Skills Demonstrated ability to work effectively and respectfully with individuals from a wide range of backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives, and to contribute positively to a collaborative working and learning environment. Ability to work independently and collaboratively in a team environment. Strong organizational skills and the ability to manage multiple concurrent projects and deadlines. Strong written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to communicate technical findings to non-technical audiences. Ability to create and edit professional reports, presentations, and summaries. Ability to maintain confidentiality when working with sensitive information. Specific Job Knowledge Experience with survey research methods and data collection practices. Experience analyzing and interpreting quantitative and qualitative data. Ability to synthesize findings into actionable insights and recommendations. Experience using survey platforms such as Qualtrics or comparable survey software. Proficiency with Microsoft 365 applications, particularly Excel, Word, and PowerPoint. Experience with one or more statistical, analytical, or data visualization tools. General understanding of higher education, institutional research, assessment, or organizational decision-making environments. Equipment Knowledge PC, working in varied server environments Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education Master’s degree in higher education, educational research, statistics, social sciences, public administration, data analytics, or a related field. Work Experience Five or more years of experience in higher education, institutional research, assessment, program evaluation, or a comparable professional environment, including independent management of survey research projects. Experience designing, administering, analyzing, and reporting survey research projects. Experience presenting research findings and recommendations to faculty, staff, administrators, or other stakeholder groups. Experience providing consultation and methodological guidance to faculty, staff, administrators, or external stakeholders regarding survey design, data collection, and reporting. Experience serving in an administrative, support, trainer, or advanced-user role for Qualtrics or a comparable enterprise survey platform. Specific Job Knowledge Current Qualtrics certification (e.g., CoreXM Certification, XM for Strategy & Research Expert Certification, or equivalent) and/or demonstrated advanced proficiency in Qualtrics survey design, administration, and reporting. Experience analyzing survey data using SPSS , R, or similar statistical software. Experience conducting qualitative analysis of open-ended survey responses, including coding, thematic analysis, and reporting of findings. Knowledge of IRB protocols, research ethics, and data confidentiality practices. Familiarity with higher education survey research, assessment, institutional effectiveness, or accreditation-related activities. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 10/06/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 14 and the range is $58,300-73,800. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 14 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Please describe any current Qualtrics certifications you hold (e.g., CoreXM Certification, XM for Strategy & Research Expert Certification, or equivalent) and/or your advanced experience using Qualtrics for survey design, administration, distribution, data collection, reporting, and analysis. (Open Ended Question) Describe your experience in prioritizing tasks and providing assistance while under pressure. What is your strategy for completing a variety of tasks in a fast paced environment? (Open Ended Question) Please describe in detail how your background and experience would be applicable for this position. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
