    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36437": {
      "title": "Center Administrator, Center for Irish Studies",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Center Administrator, Center for Irish Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Center Administrator, Center for Irish Studies To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Applications must include contact information for 3 references. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260434S Position Title: Center Administrator, Center for Irish Studies Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week 35 hours Department: 166-Irish Studies Program Position Summary: The Center Administrator works closely with the Center Director to manage the operations of the Center for Irish Studies, providing support in the coordination and development of all Center programs and initiatives. Key responsibilities include: managing Center operations; fiscal reporting, planning, and budget management; supervising the Center’s student fellows and interns; event planning, community outreach, promotion and management; public relations and communications. Limited travel and occasional attendance at evening events is anticipated. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Manage the operations of the Center, including budget, fiscal reporting, and payments; the Center shared files and folders; and Center materials for students. Work with the Irish Studies administrative assistant in payments, calendar, and newsletter. Assist Director in coordinating visits by Irish Fulbrights, visiting Heimbold Chair, and other residencies. Assign tasks to Administrative Assitant staff. Supervise student fellows. Collaborate with the Director to plan, develop, promote and execute Center programs and events; plan and execute annual meetings with community groups. Work with Advancement to coordinate fund-raising efforts and publications. Assist the Director on the annual report and donor reports. Develop and update communication materials associated with Center initiatives, including the Center website, newsletters, and social media; maintain communications with internal and external stakeholders, including students, faculty, staff and other centers at Villanova; donors; external partners, including the Irish Government (Consulate General of Ireland; Culture Ireland, Office of the Irish Ambassador; Fulbright IIE , NiCCONA), and local residents and community organizations including the Irish Diaspora Center and the Irish American Business Chamber and Network. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in Liberal Arts and Sciences or related discipline required; Master’s degree in related discipline desirable. Strong program, event and budget management skills; experience with communications, marketing, and public relations, including website management and social media. Excellent oral and written communication skills; strong organizational, problem-solving and interpersonal skills required. Ability to work independently, manage multiple projects and events, and to work with and gain the respect of multiple constituencies, including faculty, staff, alumni, students, professionals and the general public. Knowledge of Ireland, the Irish diaspora, and interest in Irish culture. Other requirements include Minimum of 3 years experience in a relevant and applicable work environment required. Equivalent of work experience or years of education will be considered. Proficiency in all standard computer applications, including Microsoft office products, particularly Microsoft Word and Excel. General knowledge of office principles and procedures is required. Knowledge of Banner and Sharepoint preferred. Preferred Qualifications: Master’s degree in related discipline desirable. Knowledge of Banner, Salesforce preferred. Work in a not-for-profit organization with a public-facing and/or student involvement. Some experience traveling to or living in Ireland. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: none Special Message to Applicants: Applications must include contact information for 3 references. Posting Date: 09/25/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 13 and the range is $52,000-65,100. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 13 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33413": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Spanish",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Spanish Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Spanish To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The Romance Languages and Literatures Department will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. All applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the following three pieces of information: a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2020709F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Spanish Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/9-months Department: 140- Romance Languages & Literature Position Summary: Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Spanish for undergraduate courses only. The specific courses involved may vary from semester to semester. The applicant must have an M.A. and be committed to excellence in the teaching of Spanish at all levels. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and related duties will vary with the specific course(s) being taught. Minimum Qualifications: A master’s degree in Spanish, native or near native knowledge of Spanish and English required. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The Romance Languages and Literatures Department will accept applications throughout the year. When a teaching vacancy arises, we will consider the submitted applications in an effort to staff the course. All applicants must apply online at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications must include: 1. A current and complete resume/curriculum vitae. 2. A cover letter or letter of interest. The letter should include the following three pieces of information: a) the type of courses the applicant is interested in teaching; b) the time period during which the applicant expects to be available; c) the names and the contact information of three references. If the applicant wishes to submit any other supporting documents, they may submit them online in conjunction with the application. Posting Date: 03/24/2020 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: 2020709F Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website 