    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36260": {
      "title": "Events &amp; External Relations Specialist",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Events &amp; External Relations Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Events & External Relations Specialist To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until position is filled. All applications must include the following: Resume Cover Letter Names of three (3) references During the application process, you will also be answer to respond to the following prompt: Please briefly describe your experience with graphic design and marketing software. What programs or tools have you used (Canva, Adobe Creative Suite, PowerPoint, etc.), and how comfortable are you using them to create promotional or event-related materials? Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260419S Position Title: Events & External Relations Specialist Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/10-months Avg Hours Week Department: 216-Dean - Villanova School of Business Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Events & External Relations Specialist within the Villanova School of Business provides event logistics, promotion, consulting, management, and external relations and graphic design support for VSB . This Specialist within the Dean’s Office supports the development and execution of events, event marketing, event promotion, and social media content to ensure successful programs, events, and stakeholder engagement. This role also generates and develops content to ensure brand consistency and alignment with the University and VSB’s key messages and strategic objectives. The Specialist is responsible for providing project support for External Relations and Donor Engagement programming, including partnering with internal and external vendors, and partners. The Events & External Relations Specialist works to ensure high-quality service to students, faculty, alumni, program participants, and other stakeholders in support of VSB mission and objectives. The Events & External Relations Specialist also supports financial and administrative processes. This is a 10‑month staff position aligned with the academic year. The role does not require work during summer months, and compensation is structured to reflect the 10‑month schedule. The timing of the 2 unpaid summer months is informed by the University academic calendar, major School events, and the business needs of VSB and is established in partnership with the selected candidate. More information about the schedule and position will be shared during the interview process. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Event Management: Partners with the Associate Director and Assistant Dean to develop and execute a strategic event portfolio that advances VSB’s priorities, goals, and stakeholder engagement objectives. Leads the planning, coordination, and execution of Dean’s Office signature programs and events, including academic excellence ceremonies, executive speaker programs, and other high-profile initiatives. Serves as the primary liaison for internal and external stakeholders, ensuring alignment of event objectives, communications, logistics, and participant experience. Manages all phases of event planning and execution, including project planning, venue selection, budgeting, registration, vendor management, catering, audiovisual requirements, marketing coordination, risk mitigation, on-site event management, and post-event evaluation. Oversees event-related budgets and financial administration, including expense management and vendor procurement, as appropriate. Collaborates with VSB Communications and Marketing partners to develop and implement event promotion and engagement strategies across print, digital, web, and social media channels. Supports external relations initiatives, including coordination of guest speakers, VIP guests, and strategic partnerships that enhance the visibility and impact of VSB programs. Develops and maintains relationships with vendors, venues, service providers, and university partners to support operational excellence and event success. Oversees event registration platforms, attendance tracking, reporting, and data management to support operational effectiveness and informed decision-making. Establishes and analyzes event metrics, participant feedback, and operational data to assess outcomes, drive continuous improvement, and implement event management best practices. Serves as a subject matter expert and representative of VSB on university committees and collaborative initiatives related to major events and programs. Provides guidance, coordination, and oversight to student ambassadors, volunteers, and assigned staff supporting event operations. External Relations Support: Provides high-level program and event promotion support for stakeholder and DAC engagement initiatives, ad hoc corporate visits and/or other money-generating events (e.g., CPE credits, trainings, etc.) Tracks Business School ranking opportunities, participation, methodology, and timeliness. Event Promotion: Supports the development and execution of all event promotion, graphics, and marketing for VSB programs and events, such as the academic excellence ceremonies, the Dean’s signature events, and other Executive Speaker Series Events. Also supports event promotion for external conferences and industry events in partnership with the VSB Marketing and Communications office. Sponsorship and Branding Management: Manages photography, print, online and digital assets. Supports sponsorship, branding, and external speaking opportunities for VSB ; collaborates with VSB Marketing and Communication and Dean’s Office staff to assure alignment and efficiency; supports trade shows, conferences, and key relationships, etc. Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in communications, journalism, English, marketing, public relations, or related discipline is required. Minimum 2 years of high-level project experience, including communication and marketing experience. Strong proficiency in planning and supporting functions including business correspondence, scheduling, budget and financial processes, and project management, social media, analytics, and client service. Proficiency in all standard computer applications (Microsoft Office) and social media platforms (such as Instagram, Facebook, LinkedIn, Twitter, YouTube). Ability to solve problems proactively and independently. Creative thinker with attention to detail. Knowledge of event functions and ability to manage multifaceted projects. Expertise to communicate with a variety of audiences across different mediums. Must convey a highly professional demeanor, be a team player, and have exceptional organizational and communication skills. Ability to provide high-level service to diverse groups of constituents. Ability to handle a fast-paced environment and manage multiple projects/tasks with varied deadlines. Must be poised with strong customer-service skills and be able to work independently under limited supervision Experience operating and troubleshooting standard office equipment. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Occasional evening and weekend work required to serve the needs of the Villanova School of Business. Special Message to Applicants: Review of applications will begin immediately and will continue until position is filled. All applications must include the following: Resume Cover Letter Names of three (3) references During the application process, you will also be answer to respond to the following prompt: Please briefly describe your experience with graphic design and marketing software. What programs or tools have you used (Canva, Adobe Creative Suite, PowerPoint, etc.), and how comfortable are you using them to create promotional or event-related materials? Posting Date: 09/02/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 13 and the range is $of $47,500-49,800. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 13 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Please briefly describe your experience with graphic design and marketing software. What programs or tools have you used (Canva, Adobe Creative Suite, PowerPoint, etc.), and how comfortable are you using them to create promotional or event-related materials? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/32404": {
      "title": "Standardized Patient",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Standardized Patient Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Standardized Patient To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. This is a pooled position. Applications will be reviewed as the need arises for Standardized Patients. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20240577T Position Title: Standardized Patient Position Type: Temp/Intern Location: Villanova, PA Work Schedule: Varies Approximate Number of Hours per Week Varies Department: 937-FCN Simluation & LRC Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Standardized patients (SP) are individuals trained to simulate medical and mental health conditions accurately and in a standardized way, to document performance and rate interpersonal communication. Duties and Responsibilities: Following a period of training, SP will have the following general responsibilities: Portray medical / mental health patients in an accurate, standardized way. Observe and accurately document student performance on skills checklists and rating scales. Provide debriefing and / or direct teaching to students regarding interpersonal communication and physical examination skills. Participate in training for roles to be portrayed. Training can be on site and/or via computer. All SP’s will receive training as appropriate for their roles. SP’s are required to dress as patients (i.e. in hospital gowns, etc.) as appropriate to their role. SP’s are required to undergo physical examinations by Nurse Practitioner students as part of the students’ training. All SP sessions are video recorded and SP must give permission for such recording as well as their use in educational and research projects. All SP’s will undergo continuous quality assurance through video review. Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: High school graduate or equivalent Ability to read and write in English. Must have e-mail access and ability to use a PC and internet. Preferred Qualifications: At least one year of experience as an SP is preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: This is a pooled position. Applications will be reviewed as the need arises for Standardized Patients. EEO Statement Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian order. Diversity and inclusion have been and will continue to be an integral component of Villanova University’s mission. The University is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Posting Date: 10/21/2024 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $22/hr. Job Classification: non-exempt Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36551": {
      "title": "Dining Services Hospitality Associate -Villanova or Radnor, PA",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Dining Services Hospitality Associate -Villanova or Radnor, PA Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Dining Services Hospitality Associate -Villanova or Radnor, PA To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Schedules available include: Full Time, 12 months (works year round): 1.) Sunday - Thursday 4:30 pm – 1:30 am 2.) Sunday - Thursday 4:00 pm – 1:00 am 3.) Tuesday – Saturday 4:00 pm – 1:00 am 4.) Friday – Monday 6:00 am – 5:00 pm 5.) Friday – Monday 2pm – 1am 6.) Sunday - Thursday 6am - 3pm 7.) Sunday - Thursday 12pm - 9pm Full time, 9 months (9-month positions do not work during the summer months): 1.) Sunday – Thursday 3pm – 12 am Part time, 12 months (works year round): 1.) Monday and Friday 4pm – 9pm. Saturday and Sunday 12pm – 9pm. 2.) Tuesday – Saturday 9am -2:30pm 3.) Sunday and Monday 9am – 2:30pm. Tuesday/Wednesday/Thursday 12pm – 5:30pm 4.) Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Friday, and Sunday 6am - 3pm Part time, 9 months (9 month positions do not work during the summer months): 1.) Sunday – Thursday 5pm – 10:30pm 2.) Monday – Friday 7:30 am – 1pm 3.) Monday - Friday 9am - 2:30 pm Please note in your application which shift(s) you are available to work. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260342S Position Title: Dining Services Hospitality Associate -Villanova or Radnor, PA Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: Varies Avg Hours Week Department: 411-Dining Services Administration Position Summary: Founded in 1842 and recognized among the nation’s best colleges and universities, we are a mission-driven institution inspired by the values of truth, unity, love, and dedication to serving the common good. At Villanova, we believe our people are our most precious asset. That’s why we offer a vibrant and collaborative campus environment and invest in our employees through competitive compensation and comprehensive benefits that support your professional growth, personal well-being, and long-term success. Benefits include: • Generous paid time off and holidays • Tuition assistance for employees and eligible family members • Professional development opportunities • Retirement savings plan with University contributions • Well-being programs and resources • Flexible work options where appropriate We invite you to join a community where your contributions are valued, your growth is supported, and your work makes a meaningful difference. Learn more about the benefits of working at Villanova on our website. As a member of the Dining Services Department, the individual will work in any of the following positions: front of the house- food production/serving/cashier/barista and back of the house food production. As a Dining Services Hospitality Associate, you will serve customers in an efficient and courteous manner. The Dining Services Hospitality Associate will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the value of the Villanova Mission Statement and the Dining Services Mission Statement. The individual will focus on our Core Values: Safety and Sanitation, Friendly Courteous Service, and Excellence . All of our associates should improve our systems and overall operation. Why join our team? Our dining services team members receive: Increased hourly rate starting at $17.50/hour Generous vacation plan and holiday schedule Free meals during each shift Health and wellness resources plus discount programs Opportunities for advancement Various schedules available, including late-night positions with night differential Free uniforms, including footwear *Full-time employees also receive: 403b retirement plan with employer base and matching contributions, tuition remission for associates and dependents, medical, vision, and dental insurance with multiple health plan options Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Set-up, maintain, and break down all service lines. Ability to prepare and/or cook food for cold production and for pizza/grill lines. Stock, rotate and replenish merchandise as needed. Back of the house production includes salad and fruit bars, deli prep, desserts, and commissary items May work on any of the following stations serving our customers: sandwich/salad/pizza/grill/Holy Grounds areas/register stations Serves customers in an efficient and courteous manner in accordance with our mission. Responsible for serving the proper proportions and following all safety and sanitation practices. Is familiar with all menu items and recipes following our standards. Cleans and sanitizes food equipment and dining room tables and chairs NONESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Works special events/weekends as required Assists in the dish room area if needed including sweeping, mopping, disposing of trash/recycling Perform additional job duties as directed by supervisor or manager Minimum Qualifications: Work Skills: Basic reading and writing skills; basic communication skills Excellent customer service skills Practices excellent personal hygiene habits and follows and adheres to uniform standards Ability to: follow directions and complete assigned tasks, work with minimal supervision, and to interact with people on a constant basis Preferred Qualifications: Preferred – High school diploma or equivalent Preferred – Basic knowledge of food service safety and sanitation Preferred – Serv Safe Training and Allergy Awareness Training Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery, and equipment used: Knives, slicers, and all kitchen equipment Environmental conditions: Chemicals used for cleaning Weather exposure for special events Physical requirements: Ability to stand for extended periods Ability to lift, push/pull up to 10 pounds independently and up to 40 pounds with assistance Ability to withstand extreme temperatures Special Message to Applicants: Schedules available include: Full Time, 12 months (works year round): 1.) Sunday – Thursday 4:30 pm – 1:30 am 2.) Sunday – Thursday 4:00 pm – 1:00 am 3.) Tuesday – Saturday 4:00 pm – 1:00 am 4.) Friday – Monday 6:00 am – 5:00 pm 5.) Friday – Monday 2pm – 1am 6.) Sunday – Thursday 6am – 3pm 7.) Sunday – Thursday 12pm – 9pm Full time, 9 months (9-month positions do not work during the summer months): 1.) Sunday – Thursday 3pm – 12 am Part time, 12 months (works year round): 1.) Monday and Friday 4pm – 9pm. Saturday and Sunday 12pm – 9pm. 2.) Tuesday – Saturday 9am -2:30pm 3.) Sunday and Monday 9am – 2:30pm. Tuesday/Wednesday/Thursday 12pm – 5:30pm 4.) Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Friday, and Sunday 6am – 3pm Part time, 9 months (9 month positions do not work during the summer months): 1.) Sunday – Thursday 5pm – 10:30pm 2.) Monday – Friday 7:30 am – 1pm 3.) Monday – Friday 9am – 2:30 pm Please note in your application which shift(s) you are available to work. Posting Date: 10/12/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $17.50 per hour. Shift differential for qualifying shifts. Salary Grade: 8 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 1 Maximum Number of References Needed 1 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Which shift(s) are you available to work? Please select all that apply. Sunday - Thursday 4:30 pm - 1:30am Sunday - Thursday 4pm - 1:00am Tuesday-Saturday 4pm-1am Friday - Monday 6am - 5pm Friday-Monday 2pm-1am (2 openings) Monday/Tuesday/Wednesday/Saturday 9am - 6pm. Friday 7am - 4pm Sunday - Thursday 3pm - 12am Monday and Friday 4pm - 9pm. Saturday and Sunday 12pm - 9pm Tuesday - Saturday 9am - 2:30pm Sunday and Monday 9am - 2:30pm. Tuesday/Wednesday/Thursday 12pm - 5:30pm Sunday - Thursday 5pm - 10:30pm Monday - Friday 7:30am - 1pm * Please select the location you are interested in working at (select all that apply) Cabrini Campus (Radnor PA) Villanova Campus (Villanova PA) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
