    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36502": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty in Chemical and Biological Engineering",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Tenure-Track Faculty in Chemical and Biological Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Tenure-Track Faculty in Chemical and Biological Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Villanova is a Carnegie-classified doctoral university. From its founding in 1842 to its position today as a nationally recognized leading university, Villanova University has forged a path of academic excellence. The University is in the Philadelphia metropolitan area, home to a large concentration of universities, industries, and government labs. The Chemical and Biological Engineering department has 15 full-time faculty members, more than 200 undergraduate students, and over 60 graduate students, including MS and Ph.D. students. The department is committed to providing rigorous educational experience in the discipline of Chemical Engineering, graduating well-rounded leaders and life-long learners, who aspire to achieving professional excellence. We are equally committed to the discovery, dissemination, advancement, and application of cutting-edge research. Inspired by the Augustinian-Catholic tradition, we value an inclusive and diverse community in which we prepare our students to demonstrate the highest ethical conduct and contribute to the well-being of humankind. The Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering and the College of Engineering are deeply committed to work-life balance and family-friendly programs for our faculty. Please submit your application at: http://jobs.villanova.edu . Application packages must include: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Academic Transcripts Statements on Teaching Philosophy Detailed research plan including research areas, intellectual merit, broader impact, and integration into existing research strengths at Villanova. Contribution to University Mission Statement Names and contact information of three references The review process will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260089F Position Title: Tenure-Track Faculty in Chemical and Biological Engineering Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 203-Chemical Engineering Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2026 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering at Villanova University has an opening for a full-time tenure-track faculty position at all levels. Candidates will be considered for Assistant Professor or Associate Professor rank commensurate with their education and experience. The Department is looking for a creative and energetic faculty member that will complement and enhance the Program. The successful candidate will demonstrate exceptional potential with respect to research, scholarly activity, teaching and service within the Chemical Engineering discipline. Areas of interest include sustainability, advanced materials, systems engineering, computational chemistry, catalysis, energy, process design and optimization, AI applications in Chemical Engineering and other fields relevant to Chemical Engineering. Leadership and/or entrepreneurial experience within an academic, research, industry, or service environment is desired. This position is expected to support and contribute to the strategic plans for Villanova University, College of Engineering, and department of Chemical and Biological Engineering by addressing global challenges that include human health, water-energy-food nexus, environmental sustainability, advanced manufacturing and sustainable engineering. The candidate will also be expected to mentor undergraduate and graduate students. The appointment begins in August 2027. The University is strongly rooted in a sense of community, and the CBE Department and the College of Engineering are deeply committed to work-life balance . In addition, the University has also established the Center for Faculty Leadership and Success ( CFLS ), supported by an NSF ADVANCE Institutional Transformation Grant, to create meaningful learning and development opportunities for all faculty. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: The primary responsibilities include developing and sustaining an internationally recognized research program, collaborating with faculty and staff in the College of Engineering at Villanova and other Institutions, and teaching undergraduate and graduate courses (both in the core curriculum and on their research expertise). Candidates must also participate in departmental, college, and university service as it contributes to the mission and strategic goals. Supervisor research performed by undergraduate, Master’s and/or Ph.D. students. Minimum Qualifications: A PhD in Chemical and/or Biological Engineering or a closely related field A proven ability for high-quality research as evidenced by previous research publications and presentations. Preferred Qualifications: The ideal candidate will have expertise in sustainability, advanced materials, systems engineering, computational chemistry, catalysis, energy, process design and optimization, AI applications in Chemical Engineering and other fields relevant to Chemical Engineering. Leadership and/or entrepreneurial experience within an academic, research, industry, or service environment is desired. Teaching experience as an instructor, TA, instructional assistant, or research mentor. Associate Professor candidates are expected to have teaching experience and a previous record of research. A demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence and innovation. Potential to lead an externally funded research program. Experience mentoring others in research such as undergraduate or graduate students. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Villanova is a Carnegie-classified doctoral university. From its founding in 1842 to its position today as a nationally recognized leading university, Villanova University has forged a path of academic excellence. The University is in the Philadelphia metropolitan area, home to a large concentration of universities, industries, and government labs. The Chemical and Biological Engineering department has 15 full-time faculty members, more than 200 undergraduate students, and over 60 graduate students, including MS and Ph.D. students. The department is committed to providing rigorous educational experience in the discipline of Chemical Engineering, graduating well-rounded leaders and life-long learners, who aspire to achieving professional excellence. We are equally committed to the discovery, dissemination, advancement, and application of cutting-edge research. Inspired by the Augustinian-Catholic tradition, we value an inclusive and diverse community in which we prepare our students to demonstrate the highest ethical conduct and contribute to the well-being of humankind. The Department of Chemical and Biological Engineering and the College of Engineering are deeply committed to work-life balance and family-friendly programs for our faculty. Please submit your application at: http://jobs.villanova.edu . Application packages must include: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Academic Transcripts Statements on Teaching Philosophy Detailed research plan including research areas, intellectual merit, broader impact, and integration into existing research strengths at Villanova. Contribution to University Mission Statement Names and contact information of three references The review process will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Date: 10/06/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Interests Statement of Contribution to Mission Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33431": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Tax Program, School of Law",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Tax Program, School of Law Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Tax Program, School of Law To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. All applicants must apply online and must include: a letter of interest, including a description of your teaching philosophy, and the name and email address for at least 3 references. current curriculum vitae. academic transcripts; unofficial transcripts will be accepted to submit application; however, official transcripts are required if you are selected for an interview. Screening of submitted applications begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2020706F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty - Graduate Tax Program, School of Law Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: temporary Department: 241-Law School Instruction Position Summary: The Villanova Graduate Tax program seeks qualified individuals for its Adjunct Faculty Pool and welcomes applicants who have an interest in teaching courses in taxation. The Graduate Tax Program offers programs leading to a Masters of Laws in Taxation (LL.M.) and a Master in Taxation (MT). Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching graduate tax courses. Duties will vary with the specific courses being taught. Minimum Qualifications: An LLM , JD, and/or Master’s degree in a related discipline is required; Must be committed to excellence in graduate tax education. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: All applicants must apply online and must include: a letter of interest, including a description of your teaching philosophy, and the name and email address for at least 3 references. current curriculum vitae. academic transcripts; unofficial transcripts will be accepted to submit application; however, official transcripts are required if you are selected for an interview. Screening of submitted applications begins when a teaching vacancy arises. Posting Date: 03/13/2020 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position has a salary of $1,600.00 per credit hour. This may be pro-rated in the case of team-teaching scenarios where effort is shared. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
