    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/33451": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty- Civil &amp; Environmental Engineering",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Adjunct Faculty- Civil &amp; Environmental Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Adjunct Faculty- Civil & Environmental Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. *We will be accepting applications throughout the year and will only fill teaching needs as they arise.* Applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications are to include a letter of interest (including the name and contact information for at least 3 references), current and complete curriculum vitae, and a statement describing your teaching philosophy including courses you are interested in teaching. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 2013107F Position Title: Adjunct Faculty- Civil & Environmental Engineering Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: part-time/9-months Department: 202-Civil and Environmental Engineering Position Summary: Villanova University invites applications for adjunct teaching positions in Civil and Environmental Engineering for graduate courses taught in the evening and/or undergraduate courses taught during the day. The Civil and Environmental Engineering Department offers programs leading to the B.S. and M.S. degrees and participates in the College of Engineering Ph.D. degree program. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Teaching and other duties which vary with specific courses. Minimum Qualifications: * Master’s degree required. * The applicant must be committed to excellence in engineering education. Preferred Qualifications: * An earned doctorate in Civil Engineering or closely allied discipline is strongly preferred. * Previous teaching experience preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Undergraduate courses are offered during the day; graduate courses during the evening. Graduate courses include a synchronous component. Special Message to Applicants: We will be accepting applications throughout the year and will only fill teaching needs as they arise. Applicants must apply on line at https://jobs.villanova.edu and complete a faculty profile. Online applications are to include a letter of interest (including the name and contact information for at least 3 references), current and complete curriculum vitae, and a statement describing your teaching philosophy including courses you are interested in teaching. Posting Date: Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This adjunct position falls within the salary range of $1,650.00 – $2,600.00 per credit/contact hour. The final compensation will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s educational qualifications, course type (drill, lab, lecture), course level (undergraduate or graduate), and market benchmarks. Salary Band: Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed Maximum Number of References Needed Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * What is your area of expertise (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Transcripts © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
