    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36375": {
      "title": "Graduate Student Ambassador",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Graduate Student Ambassador Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Graduate Student Ambassador To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260402V Position Title: Graduate Student Ambassador Posting Type Graduate Assistant Hours/week: Graduate Hourly (GAH), 15 hrs/week Eligibility: Graduate Assistant Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Vasey Hall Detailed Work Schedule 15-20 hours/week, monday – friday (with some evenings and weekends for special events as needed). Number of positions: 1 Department: 936-Graduate Education - Provost Contact Name: Emily McCloskey Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-5174 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Center for Graduate Research and Education (Grad Center) seeks a year-round hourly graduate assistant ( GAH ) to join a dynamic, collaborative, student-centered team. This student will provide operational support to the Grad Center team and be the first point of contact for students in the Grad Center Lounge in Vasey Hall. Duties will include, but not be limited to, providing reception desk support to greet all visitors to the Grad Center, assist the Grad Center team with events and programming, act as an ambassador of the Grad Center to the University community, and assist with special research projects. Requirements: Requirements for this position include, but are not limited to: Superlative communication skills (written and oral) Research skills (online, data driven) A passion for graduate education and a commitment especially to Villanova’s graduate student community Excellent organization and time management skills Outgoing, friendly, and personable demeanor Additional Information: Students receiving a tuition scholarship are welcome to apply to this position, which would provide hourly pay to supplement tuition remission received through their home department. Applications will be accepting on a rolling basis until the position is filled. Exact start date can be flexible based on the student’s individual situation. Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: 18.00 Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
