    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36606": {
      "title": "Continuing Non-Tenure-Track Teaching Faculty Position - Electrical and Computer Engineering",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Continuing Non-Tenure-Track Teaching Faculty Position - Electrical and Computer Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Continuing Non-Tenure-Track Teaching Faculty Position - Electrical and Computer Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Villanova is a Carnegie-classified doctoral university. From its founding in 1842 to its position today as a nationally recognized leading university, Villanova University has forged a path of academic excellence. The University is in the Philadelphia metropolitan area, home to a large concentration of universities, industries, and government labs. There is easy access to the Philadelphia International Airport and to nearby cities such as New York and Washington, DC both by highway and by rail. More information about Villanova and its location is available on the Villanova website at https://www1.villanova.edu/university.html . Villanova University is classified as a Doctoral University by the Carnegie Foundation and ranked 42 among the Best National Universities by the 2027 U.S. News & World Report. Villanova provides a comprehensive education rooted in the liberal arts; a shared commitment to the Augustinian ideals of truth, unity and love; and a community dedicated to service to others. The College of Engineering’s success in living up to these ideals has made us one of the most respected engineering programs in the country, and our commitment to those values is evident in our excellent faculty and staff, innovative academic programs, cutting edge research and extensive service opportunities, which leave an impact on the world. In the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, our 22 full-time faculty members provide a rigorous educational experience for approximately 330 undergraduates and 130 graduate students, developing well-rounded leaders and life-long learners who aspire to achieve professional excellence in whatever field they choose. We are equally committed to the discovery, dissemination, advancement and application of cutting-edge research, as evidenced by our faculty, which includes three NSF CAREER Awards, three IEEE Life Fellows, a recipient of the IEEE Dennis Picard Gold Medal in Radar Technologies and Applications, a winner of the prestigious Humboldt prize, a Fulbright Distinguished Chair, and four IEEE Distinguished Lecturers. Further information about the department can be found at https://www.villanova.edu/university/engineering/academic-programs/electrical-computer.html . Please submit your application at: http://jobs.villanova.edu . Application packages must include: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Academic Transcripts Statements on Teaching Philosophy Names and contact information of three references Finalists must submit a Statement of Contribution to the University Mission (and enduring commitments) The review process will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260097F Position Title: Continuing Non-Tenure-Track Teaching Faculty Position - Electrical and Computer Engineering Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 204-Electrical and Computer Engineering Position Summary: Founded in 1842 and recognized among the nation’s best colleges and universities, we are a mission-driven institution inspired by the values of truth, unity, love, and dedication to serving the common good. At Villanova, we believe our people are our most precious asset. That’s why we offer a vibrant and collaborative campus environment and invest in our employees through competitive compensation and comprehensive benefits that support your professional growth, personal well-being, and long-term success. Benefits include: • Generous paid time off and holidays • Tuition assistance for employees and eligible family members • Professional development opportunities • Retirement savings plan with University contributions • Well-being programs and resources • Flexible work options where appropriate We invite you to join a community where your contributions are valued, your growth is supported, and your work makes a meaningful difference. Learn more about the benefits of working at Villanova on our website. The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering ( ECE ) at Villanova University invites applications for a continuing non-tenure-track Assistant Teaching Professor position in Electrical Engineering, beginning in Spring 2027 . We seek candidates with expertise in the broad areas of electrical engineering, with particular emphasis on circuits and control systems. The University is strongly rooted in a sense of community, and the ECE Department and the College of Engineering are deeply committed to work-life balance . In addition, the University has also established the Center for Faculty Leadership and Success ( CFLS ), focused on developing and expanding research-informed leadership development offerings for rising and mid-level academic leaders. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will primarily teach undergraduate and graduate courses at all levels of the electrical engineering curriculum. Responsibilities also include developing and/or delivering new courses as needed. Other responsibilities include mentoring and advising undergraduate students on plans of study, senior capstone or independent research projects, and professional development; and service to the department and college. The candidate is also expected to maintain a presence on campus and be responsive to students as a full-time member of the faculty for the duration of the appointment. Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. degree in Electrical Engineering. A demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence and innovation. Preferred Qualifications: Previous teaching experience in the relevant areas. Current or prior experience as an academic advisor for undergraduate engineering students. Evidence of research and scholarship in engineering education or pedagogical innovation. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Villanova is a Carnegie-classified doctoral university. From its founding in 1842 to its position today as a nationally recognized leading university, Villanova University has forged a path of academic excellence. The University is in the Philadelphia metropolitan area, home to a large concentration of universities, industries, and government labs. There is easy access to the Philadelphia International Airport and to nearby cities such as New York and Washington, DC both by highway and by rail. More information about Villanova and its location is available on the Villanova website at https://www1.villanova.edu/university.html . Villanova University is classified as a Doctoral University by the Carnegie Foundation and ranked 42 among the Best National Universities by the 2027 U.S. News & World Report. Villanova provides a comprehensive education rooted in the liberal arts; a shared commitment to the Augustinian ideals of truth, unity and love; and a community dedicated to service to others. The College of Engineering’s success in living up to these ideals has made us one of the most respected engineering programs in the country, and our commitment to those values is evident in our excellent faculty and staff, innovative academic programs, cutting edge research and extensive service opportunities, which leave an impact on the world. In the Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering, our 22 full-time faculty members provide a rigorous educational experience for approximately 330 undergraduates and 130 graduate students, developing well-rounded leaders and life-long learners who aspire to achieve professional excellence in whatever field they choose. We are equally committed to the discovery, dissemination, advancement and application of cutting-edge research, as evidenced by our faculty, which includes three NSF CAREER Awards, three IEEE Life Fellows, a recipient of the IEEE Dennis Picard Gold Medal in Radar Technologies and Applications, a winner of the prestigious Humboldt prize, a Fulbright Distinguished Chair, and four IEEE Distinguished Lecturers. Further information about the department can be found at https://www.villanova.edu/university/engineering/academic-programs/electrical-computer.html . Please submit your application at: http://jobs.villanova.edu . Application packages must include: Cover Letter Curriculum Vitae Academic Transcripts Statements on Teaching Philosophy Names and contact information of three references Finalists must submit a Statement of Contribution to the University Mission (and enduring commitments) The review process will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Date: 10/21/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Optional Documents Other Document Other Document (2) Statement of Contribution to Mission © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36608": {
      "title": "Continuing Non-Tenure Position Program of Italian Studies",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Continuing Non-Tenure Position Program of Italian Studies Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Continuing Non-Tenure Position Program of Italian Studies To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Application materials should be submitted on-line at http://jobs.villanova.edu by January 10, 2027. Please address questions about to Dr. James Kriesel, Director of the Italian Studies Program, at james.kriesel@villanova.edu. Candidates should include: · Cover letter · Curriculum vitae · Three confidential letters of recommendation · Teaching statement about pedagogy and curriculum · Sample syllabus for a first or second semester intermediate course with a content-forward component · Complete set of course evaluations (preferably with student comments) · Unofficial copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts (official transcripts will be required for finalists) · Finalists will be asked to provide a statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions may support the University mission (and enduring principles) . · Optional: Other materials related to a teaching portfolio Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260091F Position Title: Continuing Non-Tenure Position Program of Italian Studies Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 984-Italian Studies Position Summary: Founded in 1842 and recognized among the nation’s best colleges and universities, we are a mission-driven institution inspired by the values of truth, unity, love, and dedication to serving the common good. At Villanova, we believe our people are our most precious asset. That’s why we offer a vibrant and collaborative campus environment and invest in our employees through competitive compensation and comprehensive benefits that support your professional growth, personal well-being, and long-term success. Benefits include: • Generous paid time off and holidays • Tuition assistance for employees and eligible family members • Professional development opportunities • Retirement savings plan with University contributions • Well-being programs and resources • Flexible work options where appropriate We invite you to join a community where your contributions are valued, your growth is supported, and your work makes a meaningful difference. Learn more about the benefits of working at Villanova on our website. The Program of Italian Studies at Villanova invites applications for a continuing non-tenure-track ( CNT ) position at the rank of Assistant Teaching Professor, starting in Fall 2027. We seek a new colleague with expertise in introductory and intermediate Italian levels who can also contribute to the development of the undergraduate language program. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: We seek candidates who are committed to excellence in language teaching and can also design content-based courses. The candidate should be able to teach courses using student-centered, proficiency-oriented, and communicative approaches; develop language classes with varieties of culture; and collaborate on initiatives related to student programming and service. The typical teaching load is three courses per semester. Villanova encourages ongoing professional engagement by providing support at the departmental, college, and university levels for curricular innovation and conference travel. CNT faculty are eligible for promotion. Minimum Qualifications: The candidate should possess native or near-native fluency in both Italian and English, along with a PhD in Italian Studies or a related field. Additionally, they should demonstrate a strong commitment to language teaching and student mentoring. Preferred Qualifications: The successful candidate will have demonstrated expertise in instructional pedagogies and the ability to design language courses that incorporate diverse media and content from various historical periods. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Application materials should be submitted on-line at http://jobs.villanova.edu by January 10, 2027. Please address questions about to Dr. James Kriesel, Director of the Italian Studies Program, at james.kriesel@villanova.edu. Candidates should include: · Cover letter · Curriculum vitae · Three confidential letters of recommendation · Teaching statement about pedagogy and curriculum · Sample syllabus for a first or second semester intermediate course with a content-forward component · Complete set of course evaluations (preferably with student comments) · Unofficial copies of undergraduate and graduate transcripts (official transcripts will be required for finalists) · Finalists will be asked to provide a statement articulating how the candidate’s contributions may support the University mission (and enduring principles) . · Optional: Other materials related to a teaching portfolio Posting Date: 10/21/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 01/11/2027 Salary Posting Information: Competitive Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Writing Sample/Publications Statement of Teaching Philosophy Summary of Teaching Evaluations Transcripts Optional Documents Statement of Contribution to Mission Other Document Other Document (2) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36623": {
      "title": "Registered Nurse - Rotating Shifts",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Registered Nurse - Rotating Shifts Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Registered Nurse - Rotating Shifts To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260462S Position Title: Registered Nurse - Rotating Shifts Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Avg Hours Week Department: 322-Health Center Position Summary: The Rotating Shifts Registered Nurse (RN) cares for both outpatient and inpatient students within the Student Health Center and must be available for all shifts. This includes frequent and careful assessments of walk-in patients, caring for inpatients, consulting with providers, and referring students to the Emergency Department, when necessary. The RN often communicates with the families of students. Additionally, the RN reviews all active charts for completeness and prepares charts for future appointments. Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Assist doctors and nurse practitioners during clinic hours. Assess walk-in students and treat patient symptoms according to protocol. Consult on-call physician as needed. Refer to emergency department as needed. Admit students to Health Center as needed and treat appropriately. Provide ongoing care for patients already admitted to the infirmary. Follow-up of students sent to emergency department and notify Residence Life of student hospital admissions. Administer allergy injections and immunizations. Perform blood draws and prepare specimens for laboratory pick up. Review labs and notify students of results. Distribute lab results to appropriate providers on evening/night shift. Organize charts for following day (allergy, scheduled appointments, protocol signature, MD/NP signature of lab results). Weekly check of urinalysis controls, nightly checks of refrigerator temperature. Surface cleaning of exam rooms and waiting room, and stock supplies for exam rooms. Perform other duties and assist with projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Licensed as a Registered Nurse in the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania. Minimum of two years of recent clinical nursing experience. Experience with Phlebotomy, administration of immunizations, medications, allergy injections, and nebulizer treatments. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Excellent collaboration and interpersonal skills. Strong organizational and administrative management skills. Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Must convey highest degree of professionalism, be a team player, and have strong attention to detail. The individual must have a deep commitment to the flourishing of Villanova University, its students and mission, and an understanding of Villanova’s Augustinian and Catholic values and how these values inform our interactions with campus constituents. Equipment Knowledge Strong computer skills and ability to learn new technologies. Other: Genuinely cares about students, their well-being, and their success, along with their families. Demonstrated familiarity with and sensitivity to cultural diversity concerns and anti-racism. Preferred Qualifications: BSN preferred. Experience in emergency department, family practice, or college health center. Experience using electronic medical records. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: This position works four 10-hour shifts per week including weekends. Must be available for all shifts. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 10/23/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $40.24/hr. Shift differential for qualifying shifts. Salary Grade: 15 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 1 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36611": {
      "title": "Patrol Officer I",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Patrol Officer I Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Patrol Officer I To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260089S Position Title: Patrol Officer I Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 502-Public Safety Department Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Under general supervision; the Patrol Officer I maintains safety, enforces university rules and regulations, and protects life and property within the University community. Primarily responsible for staffing fixed posts, following established operating procedures to control access to restricted areas on campus. Occasionally conducts patrols of the campus on foot, vehicle, or bicycle, responding to general calls for service and preparing written reports of activities. Locks and unlocks buildings based on a pre-determined schedule or when dispatched to do so. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Staffs any number of fixed posts on campus, controlling access to campus based on established protocols. Greets visitors, students, and employees in a friendly professional manner. Respond to routine calls for service. Provide escorts for students, faculty, and staff as requested; provide transportation as needed; assist ill or injured persons as needed. Assists in the emergency evacuation of buildings or areas. Prepare written reports of work performed. Alerts supervisors to traffic hazards or violations that could result in a vehicle being towed and/or booted. Staffs special event assignments, including athletic competitions, homecoming and commencement. Regularly attends training and participates in departmental meetings. Assumes an active role in University and departmental quality improvement efforts. Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: High School Diploma or equivalent required. Must have the ability to become certified in CPR and First Aid. Demonstrated ability to be customer service oriented Must have professionally interacted with customers, guests and/or fellow employees of individuals in a courteous manner and to de-escalate situations before they become unsafe Understanding of written instructions. Ability to prepare written reports of activities. Strong verbal and interpersonal communication skills. Strong active listening and problem solving skills Good decision making and judgment. Ability to professionally and effectively interact with members of the University community, including people from diverse backgrounds in a courteous manner, to ensure a positive experience on campus Strong service orientation commitment. Preferred Qualifications: Knowledge of safety and security practices in a college setting. Some experience in a security, police, EMS , or fire setting preferred. Comparable duties in the military accepted Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery and equipment used: Two-way radio, cellular phone, fire and burglar alarm systems, digital camera, hand-held parking ticket unit, PC and laptop computers, and fire extinguishers. Environmental conditions: (any unusual/adverse conditions such as exposure to chemicals, noise, illumination, air quality, weather exposure etc.) Work in outdoor as well as indoor venues year-round. At times, environmental conditions are poor in terms of exposure to weather or extreme heat or cold during normal shifts, as well as during special details and events. Physical requirements: ) Must be willing to work overtime details as needed or assigned. Ability to work round the clock shift-work. Walking/Standing for extended periods of time; Both gross and fine motor skills are needed, as well as visual, hearing, speaking, touching, tasting, and smelling sensory skills. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 08/17/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $18.98 an hour Salary Grade: 9 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a High School Diploma or equivilent? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36625": {
      "title": "Associate Athletics Director for Ticket Operations",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Associate Athletics Director for Ticket Operations Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Associate Athletics Director for Ticket Operations To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260478S Position Title: Associate Athletics Director for Ticket Operations Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 728-Athl - Ticket Office Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . Responsible for the day-to-day activities of the athletic ticket office including but not limited to the building of ticketed athletic events (full season/partial season/single game/group tickets) as well as the processing of tickets, renewals, and financial reporting of ticketed athletic events. This position will work closely with the Associate AD/Ticket Sales & Service, the Deputy AD/ CRO , the Director of Ticket Sales Marketing, the Associate AD/Business Operations, the Assistant VP/Athletics Development, and the President’s Office while ensuring a high level of customer and donor service. This position will also work on the integration of donor and season ticket databases and collaborate with marketing staff to generate effective ticketing strategies. In addition, the role will coordinate the distribution of student, community, and player-complimentary digital tickets for football, men’s and women’s basketball and other ticketed athletic events and selected outside events in Athletics venues. All duties must be performed in accordance with University, Conference, and NCAA policies and regulations. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Oversight of Ticket Operations and Team Members Manage and oversee the operations side of the Ticket Office including building, processing, and facilitating digital ticket distribution for athletic events; and management of full-time, part-time, student and volunteer staff. Coordinate with the President’s Office and the University Advancement Office for ticketing needs and seating assignments related to home, away, and Tournament games. Run reports including but not limited to, NCAA and internal revenue reports, and daily/weekly fiscal year reports for the Athletics Business Office. Work cooperatively with Internal Audit, as needed. Coordinate with third party ticket vendors, including managing the digital ticketing process. Maintain data in the ticketing database. Coordinate with University Technology Services for technical needs for the Ticket Office. Take part in meetings with the marketing and ticket sales team to develop ticket promotions to increase revenue. Manage ticketing system contract, relationship and technology for all ticketing and development services. Develop suggested ticket pricing based on historical data. Facilitate ticket renewal and on sale timelines. Serve as ticketing point person for basketball games played off campus at Xfinity Mobile Arena. Provide direction related to new ticketing revenue-generating initiatives and suggest best practices for utilizing the ticketing system and database. Assist with overseeing all ticket operations and customer service. Other Other duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: Bachelor’s degree is required. Work Experience: 6+ years of ticket operations experience including a minimum of 2 years spent running and overseeing a Ticket Operations Office. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills): Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Excellent organization skills. An ability to provide a high level of customer service Strong analytical skills and understanding of accounting principles. Equipment Knowledge: Proficiency with Paciolan operating and reporting system preferred, or other automated ticketing system, as well as personal computer applications (word processing, spreadsheets, database.) Other: Interest in and knowledge of Villanova and its athletic programs. Preferred Qualifications: Work Experience: Experience in professional/college sports, specifically related to ticket operations is preferred. Interest in and knowledge of Villanova Athletics and its programs. Collaborative team player with the ability to work effectively with staff and campus partners. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Working conditions are normal for an office environment. Professional work environment. Significant night and weekend work required. Occasional travel may be required. Occasional lifting and carrying. Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 10/23/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: The approved range for this position is up to $110,000. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity.” Salary Grade: 17 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 5 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as: • Any person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and • Such contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU. Examples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following: • Parents/Legal Guardians • Coaches (high school, college, club) • Personal/Skills Trainers • Relatives • Strength Coach • Advisors Consistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any: • Basketball (men’s or women’s) prospective student-athletes (grades 9-12) or their parents, relatives or coaches? Y N Yes No * An individual associated with a prospective student-athlete is defined as: • Any person who maintains or directs others to maintain contact with a prospective student-athlete, the prospective student-athlete’s parents or legal guardians, or the prospective student-athlete’s coach; and • Such contact is directly/indirectly related to the prospective student-athlete’s athletics skills/abilities or for recruitment/enrollment at VU. Examples of individuals associated with a prospect could be any of, but not limited to, the following: • Parents/Legal Guardians • Coaches (high school, college, club) • Personal/Skills Trainers • Relatives • Strength Coach • Advisors Consistent with the above definition for what constitutes associated, are you associated with any: • Current VU basketball (men’s or women’s) student-athletes? Y N Yes No Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
