    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36615": {
      "title": "Tenure-Track Faculty in Mechanical Engineering",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Tenure-Track Faculty in Mechanical Engineering Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Tenure-Track Faculty in Mechanical Engineering To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Villanova is a Carnegie-classified doctoral university. From its founding in 1842 to its position today as a nationally recognized leading university, Villanova University has forged a path of academic excellence. The University is in the Philadelphia metropolitan area, home to a large concentration of universities, industries, and government labs. The Department of Mechanical Engineering has 24 full-time faculty members, 316 undergraduate students, and 120 graduate students, including 56 Ph.D. students. Faculty in the department are internationally recognized for their research achievements. Research in the department is poised for further growth with the recent opening of Drosdick Hall, the new home of the College of Engineering, which features state-of-the-art, collaborative research and educational spaces. The department is committed to providing a rigorous educational experience in the discipline of mechanical engineering, graduating well-rounded leaders and life-long learners who aspire to achieve professional excellence. We are equally committed to the discovery, dissemination, advancement, and application of cutting-edge research. Inspired by the Augustinian-Catholic tradition, we value an inclusive and diverse community in which we prepare our students to demonstrate the highest ethical conduct and contribute to the well-being of humankind. Please submit your application at: http://jobs.villanova.edu . Application materials should include: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Academic transcripts Statement of research interests Statement of teaching philosophy Names and contact information for three references Finalists will be required to submit a Contribution to University Mission Statement The review process will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260094F Position Title: Tenure-Track Faculty in Mechanical Engineering Position Type: Faculty Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/9-months Department: 205-Mechanical Engineering Position Summary: Founded in 1842 and recognized among the nation’s best colleges and universities, we are a mission-driven institution inspired by the values of truth, unity, love, and dedication to serving the common good. At Villanova, we believe our people are our most precious asset. That’s why we offer a vibrant and collaborative campus environment and invest in our employees through competitive compensation and comprehensive benefits that support your professional growth, personal well-being, and long-term success. Benefits include: • Generous paid time off and holidays • Tuition assistance for employees and eligible family members • Professional development opportunities • Retirement savings plan with University contributions • Well-being programs and resources • Flexible work options where appropriate We invite you to join a community where your contributions are valued, your growth is supported, and your work makes a meaningful difference. Learn more about the benefits of working at Villanova on our website. The Department of Mechanical Engineering at Villanova University invites applications for a tenured or tenure-track faculty position in the general areas of dynamical systems and control theory, with an emphasis on autonomy, robotics, and multi-agent systems. We seek candidates with demonstrated expertise and potential for excellence in research, teaching, and mentoring. We are particularly interested in candidates whose research advances robotics and autonomous systems. Areas of interest include, but are not limited to: (1) AI-enabled, adaptive, and intelligent robotic systems (2) Autonomous and unmanned systems (3) Human-robot interaction, and (4) Multi-robot, multi-agent systems. This appointment begins in August 2027. The University is strongly rooted in a sense of community, and the Mechanical Engineering Department and the College of Engineering are deeply committed to work-life balance . In addition, the University has a Center for Faculty Leadership and Success ( CFLS ), focused on developing and expanding research-informed leadership development offerings for rising and mid-level academic leaders. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Primary responsibilities include establishing a vibrant, externally funded research program in dynamics and control. Contributing to the department’s growing strengths in this area; collaborating nationally and internationally and with departmental faculty. Supervising graduate students and mentoring undergraduate research students. Teaching and developing undergraduate and graduate courses in dynamics and control and related areas. Engaging in impactful service. Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Mechanical Engineering, Aerospace Engineering, Electrical Engineering, or a closely related field, completed by the time of appointment. A proven ability for high-quality research as evidenced by previous research publications and presentations. Preferred Qualifications: Candidates whose research advances robotics and autonomous systems. Leadership and/or entrepreneurial experience within an academic, research, industry, or service environment is desired. Teaching experience as an instructor, TA, instructional assistant, or research mentor. Associate Professor candidates are expected to have teaching experience and a strong record of research. A demonstrated commitment to teaching excellence and innovation. Potential to lead an externally funded research program. Experience mentoring others in research such as undergraduate or graduate students. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Villanova is a Carnegie-classified doctoral university. From its founding in 1842 to its position today as a nationally recognized leading university, Villanova University has forged a path of academic excellence. The University is in the Philadelphia metropolitan area, home to a large concentration of universities, industries, and government labs. The Department of Mechanical Engineering has 24 full-time faculty members, 316 undergraduate students, and 120 graduate students, including 56 Ph.D. students. Faculty in the department are internationally recognized for their research achievements. Research in the department is poised for further growth with the recent opening of Drosdick Hall, the new home of the College of Engineering, which features state-of-the-art, collaborative research and educational spaces. The department is committed to providing a rigorous educational experience in the discipline of mechanical engineering, graduating well-rounded leaders and life-long learners who aspire to achieve professional excellence. We are equally committed to the discovery, dissemination, advancement, and application of cutting-edge research. Inspired by the Augustinian-Catholic tradition, we value an inclusive and diverse community in which we prepare our students to demonstrate the highest ethical conduct and contribute to the well-being of humankind. Please submit your application at: http://jobs.villanova.edu . Application materials should include: Cover letter Curriculum Vitae Academic transcripts Statement of research interests Statement of teaching philosophy Names and contact information for three references Finalists will be required to submit a Contribution to University Mission Statement The review process will begin immediately and will continue until the position is filled. Posting Date: 10/22/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: Competitive. Salary Band: Job Classification: faculty References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcripts Statement of Research Interests Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) Other Document Other Document (2) Statement of Contribution to Mission © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36618": {
      "title": "Associate Business Intelligence Analyst (Internal Only)",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Associate Business Intelligence Analyst (Internal Only) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Associate Business Intelligence Analyst (Internal Only) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Please Note: To be considered for this role, candidates must live within a commutable distance to Villanova University in Villanova, PA. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260338S Position Title: Associate Business Intelligence Analyst (Internal Only) Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal Applicants Only Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week IMPORTANT: This is a limited-term position of no more than one year. Department: 713-UTS-UIS - Data Base Administration Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Associate Business Intelligence Analyst ( ABIA ) is a professional role responsible for analyzing, designing, and executing business workflow processes and procedures related to data analysis, including reporting, trending, and data mining for business units and enterprise-wide initiatives. The ABIA applies systems analysis techniques to translate business requirements into scalable reporting and analytics solutions. This role partners with business users to define reporting needs and designs and develops data models, dashboards, and analytics solutions to support decision-making. The ABIA contributes to the development, documentation, and testing of processes and procedures related to the maintenance, upgrades, and patching of business intelligence environments. The role collaborates across stakeholders to support the development and delivery of data and reporting solutions. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Collaborates with business users to define and analyze reporting and data needs using systems analysis techniques, translating requirements into scalable analytics solutions. Designs, develops, and implements reports, dashboards, forecasting models, and data mining solutions. Analyzes and profiles source system data to identify trends and recommend business intelligence and analytics solutions, and designs and migrates reporting from legacy systems to modern BI platforms. Develops and maintains technical and functional documentation for business intelligence reporting systems and data solutions. Provides guidance to users on BI tools, including reporting capabilities and data interpretation, to support effective use of reporting and analytics environments. Contributes to special projects and initiatives related to data and reporting solutions while participating in ongoing professional and technical development to build skills and maintain awareness of emerging tools and practices. Perform other duties and assist with projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field; equivalent experience and/or industry certifications will be considered. Work Experience 0–2 years of experience in business intelligence and analytics tools (e.g., Power BI) with report development and data analysis, or relevant coursework/projects Experience designing and developing reports, dashboards, or data visualizations using Power BI or similar tools Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Ability to analyze business needs and apply systems thinking to develop data and reporting solutions Ability to collaborate effectively with both technical and non-technical stakeholders Strong verbal and written communication skills Strong analytical and quantitative skills with attention to detail Ability to manage multiple projects and priorities simultaneously Demonstrated problem-solving skills and ability to exercise sound judgment Ability to evaluate, adopt, and apply emerging technologies, including AI, in an ethical and responsible manner Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Working knowledge of data analysis, data modeling, and business intelligence tools Working knowledge of relational databases and data structures Working knowledge of SQL or similar query languages Understanding of data analysis concepts, including data profiling and trend analysis Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education Master’s degree Project Management Institute ( PMI ) Project Management Professional ( PMP ) preferred, or related experience Work Experience Experience working in higher education Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Experience creating and maintaining Power BI reports in an enterprise environment Experience migrating reports from legacy to modern, cloud-based tools Working knowledge of data concepts as they relate to AI enablement Experience with Microsoft 365 environment such as SharePoint, PowerApps, Power Automate, Copilot, and Teams Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery and equipment used: N/A Environmental conditions: (any unusual/adverse conditions such as exposure to chemicals, noise, illumination, air quality, weather exposure etc.). N/A Physical requirements: (items such as lifting, pushing, pulling, standing or sitting for extended periods of time, manual dexterity, walking etc.) N/A Special Message to Applicants: Please Note: To be considered for this role, candidates must live within a commutable distance to Villanova University in Villanova, PA. Posting Date: 07/08/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): 09/03/2026 Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 15 and the range is $64,000-80,000. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 15 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * This is a hybrid position that requires on-campus presence. Do you currently live within a commutable distance to Villanova University, or would you be willing to relocate at your own expense? (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Resume / Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Optional Documents Other Document © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36629": {
      "title": "General Cook II",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | General Cook II Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us General Cook II To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The schedule for this role varies. This is based on events of the Inn. Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260149S Position Title: General Cook II Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 507-Inn at Villanova University Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The General Cook II performs a variety of task including, but not limited to food prep, grill cooking, cleaning and sanitation of kitchen area with minimal supervision. This person has in-depth knowledge of food safety and sanitation under guidelines set by The Inn at VU. This person works with chefs, managers and other staff to ensure the success of the Inn. All team members should improve our systems and overall operation. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: 1. Work assigned areas such as main kitchen, buffets, action stations, etc. Ability to identify needs for various stations, with minimal supervision. This includes small ware needs, equipment needs and settings, portion controls, and overall quality of ingredients. 2. Follow recipes and produce food items as assigned by Chefs. Maintain proper food temperatures and appearance of food. Record and maintain food production records. Be responsible for gathering ingredients, utensils, pots, pans and food from walk-ins and freezers for preparation of product. 3. Clean and sanitize equipment including but not limited to hoods, ovens, grills, floors, walls, hot trucks, kettles, prep tables, broilers, char broilers and other cleaning task as assigned by chefs/ managers. OTHER DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES 4. Work special functions if requested. 5. Ability to lead the kitchen team without Manager presence. Additional duties as assigned by chefs/managers that may include utility and pantry duties. Minimum Qualifications: POSITION SPECIFICATIONS : Formal Education: (e.g., degree) High School Graduate or Formal GED Current Serve Safe Certification (a plus) Specific Job Knowledge: (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) In-depth knowledge of food service safety and sanitation procedures. Minimum Work Experience: (type and number of years) Must have at least three years of basic food service experience. Work Skills: (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Ability to read and interpret recipes and adjust scale to yield requirement Practices excellent personal hygiene habits; follows and adheres to uniform standards daily. Basic communication skills. Ability to work with minimal supervision. Ability to interact with people on a constant basis. Equipment Knowledge: In-depth knowledge of operating commercial kitchen equipment and their functions. Ability to set-up, operate, break down and clean. Ability to properly use knives, slicer, ovens and other equipment as directed by chef/managers. Working Conditions/Environment: (conditions, if known, which may impact the incumbent working in this position) Tools, machinery and equipment used: Knives, oven, grill, fryer, slicer, broiler, rational oven, dish machine, floor cleaning machines such as wrangler. Environmental conditions: (any unusual/adverse conditions such as exposure to chemicals, noise, illumination, air quality, weather exposure etc.) Ability to use chemicals daily as required. Will use proper protective equipment as called for by the specific chemical and task. Physical requirements: (items such as lifting, pushing, pulling, standing or sitting for extended periods of time, manual dexterity, walking etc.) Ability to lift up to 40 pounds independently, sit stand for extended periods, push/pull up to 40 pounds independently, use various chemicals Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: The schedule for this role varies. This is based on events of the Inn. Posting Date: 10/05/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $18.98 per hour / shift differential added for qualifying shifts updated LS on 7/22 Salary Grade: 9 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a High School Diploma or equivilent? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have at least three years of basic food service experience? (Open Ended Question) * Do you have 3 years experience in catering? (Open Ended Question) * Are you able to work nights and weekends (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Letters of Reference (uploaded by applicant) © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36633": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Career Development &amp; Pre-Law Advising",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Assistant Director, Career Development &amp; Pre-Law Advising Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Assistant Director, Career Development & Pre-Law Advising To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260477S Position Title: Assistant Director, Career Development & Pre-Law Advising Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 323-Career Services Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Assistant Director, Career Development & Pre-Law Advising is responsible for the counseling and coaching of Villanova students and recent alumni on career decisions, job search strategies, and graduate/law school preparation. This individual will lead the Career Center’s services, programs, and events designed to support students pursuing law school and other graduate study and serve as the pre-law advisor for the University. The Assistant Director will collaborate with campus partners to develop community-focused career initiatives, programs and services to support a variety of student populations. This role will develop partnerships with faculty and staff across the university to deliver presentations and programming, create and plan events, and enhance career education and pre-law opportunities. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Career/Pre-Law Counseling and Coaching Counsel and coach students and recent alumni in all areas of career and professional development, including major exploration, successful strategies for seeking jobs and internships, developing application materials (resumes/CVs, cover letters), and practice interviews. Advise students interested in pursuing law school and other graduate programs, including guidance for writing personal statements, resumes, cover letters, and other application materials. Educate and coach students through individual appointments, drop-in hours, group presentations, and virtual resources/training. Career/Pre-Law Programming and Events Develop and support university career events (networking, panels, career fairs, classroom presentations, etc.). Create and deliver programs, events, and workshops for students and alumni interested in pursuing law school and other graduate study (i.e. Law School Fair, Pre-Law Workshop Series, Grad School 101). Coordinate programs and services with student organizations such as the Pre-Law Society, Pre-Law Black Students Association, and Mock Trial. Campus and Community Engagement Build relationships and manage engagement/outreach for specific career communities by serving as liaison to assigned student populations and campus partners. Develop and maintain relationships with law school admissions and pre-law professionals to provide relevant and timely advice to students and alumni on the law school process, including development of print and web resources. Maintain engagement with faculty and staff to promote services and support programming needs. Represent the Career Center on campus committees and with off-campus consortia, including Northeast Regional Pre-Law Advisors ( NAPLA ) and LSAC . Perform other duties and assist with projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Master’s degree required. Combination of a bachelor’s degree and relevant experience, in addition to the experience requirements listed below, may be considered in lieu of graduate level degree. Work Experience Minimum 2 years of experience in education, human resources, communication, non-profit, or related field. Work experience may include graduate assistantships and internships. Event coordination and programming experience. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Counseling/coaching skills. Event coordination and programming experience. Written, verbal and presentation skills. Collaboration and relationship management skills. Strong digital fluency with collaboration tools (Outlook, Teams, Zoom) and the ability to adapt to and effectively use new and emerging technologies, including AI tools. Knowledge of employment and career services management software preferred (i.e. Handshake). Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Understanding of student career development process, current job market trends, and hiring/graduate admissions processes – especially as it relates to undergraduate student populations Other: Ability to work some evenings and weekends required. Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education Master’s degree in areas of Counseling, Higher Education, or Human Resources preferred. Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Understanding of law school admissions process preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 10/26/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: The approved range for this position is $63,000-66,000. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 14 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
