    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36598": {
      "title": "Doctoral Research Assistant – Lung Transplant Research Study (Dr. Koons)",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Doctoral Research Assistant – Lung Transplant Research Study (Dr. Koons) Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Doctoral Research Assistant – Lung Transplant Research Study (Dr. Koons) To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260400V Position Title: Doctoral Research Assistant – Lung Transplant Research Study (Dr. Koons) Posting Type Graduate Assistant Hours/week: 20 Eligibility: Graduate Assistant Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location Driscoll Hall Detailed Work Schedule Flexible. Mostly remote. 20 hours per week. 12-month position Number of positions: 2 Department: 948-Nursing-Research & Innovation Contact Name: Brittay Koons (please add as job approver) Contact Phone/Extension: 610-519-7127 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: The Doctoral Research Assistant will work with Dr. Koons and the research team on an NIH -funded study focused on improving outcomes for lung transplant patients and their caregivers. This position provides doctoral students with hands-on experience in clinical research, including participant recruitment, longitudinal data collection, qualitative data collection and analysis, and dissemination of research findings. Requirements: • Conducting study visits with patients and caregivers • Administering study measures and collecting research data in accordance with study protocols • Entering and maintaining study data in a database (REDCap) • Taking the lead in conducting qualitative interviews with patients and caregivers • Assisting Dr. Koons with qualitative data analysis • Participating in weekly research team meetings • Assisting with the preparation of manuscripts, conference abstracts, and research presentations throughout the study • Assisting with other research activities as needed Additional Information: The Doctoral Research Assistant will receive mentorship in clinical mixed methods research and will have opportunities to contribute to presentations and peer-reviewed publications resulting from the study. • Requirements for the position: o Current doctoral student in nursing, psychology, or a related health or behavioral science field o Strong interpersonal and communication skills and comfort working with patients and caregivers o Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to work independently and collaboratively o Strong academic writing skills and interest in contributing to manuscripts, abstracts, and presentations o Ability to maintain confidentiality and follow human-subjects research protocols o Ability to commit approximately 20 hours per week for 12 months. • Preferred: Prior experience with clinical research, REDCap, qualitative analysis software, or manuscript preparation and experience or training in qualitative research methods, including interviewing and/or qualitative data analysis. • 12-month stipend with tuition remission. Eligible for need-based health benefit subsidy Physical Demands Summary: Wage Rate: $38,298.00 ($1,473.00 per pay period) Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36600": {
      "title": "General Office Assistant",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | General Office Assistant Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us General Office Assistant To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Position Information Posting Number: 20260420V Position Title: General Office Assistant Posting Type Student Hours/week: 6.5 - 7 hours/week Eligibility: Work study preferred but open to all students Semester 2026-2027 Academic Year Location St. Augustine Center Detailed Work Schedule Student worker must be available to work from 3:00 or 3:30 to 5:00 on Tuesdays, Wednesdays, and possibly Fridays. Number of positions: 1 Department: 141-Philosophy Contact Name: Alexandra Penkalskyj Contact Phone/Extension: 94690 Position Summary Information Job Description Summary: Student office worker responsibilities include phone coverage, scanning and copying, mail sorting, office supply management, and errands, as well as other light duties as needed. Requirements: Student must be dependable, responsible, able to interact with faculty and students. Additional Information: Applications will start to be reviewed immediately. Physical Demands Summary: Sitting, manual dexterity in using a copier. Wage Rate: $10.00/hour Posting Detail Information Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Open Until Filled Yes Posting Specific Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently a registered Villanova student? Yes No * Are you eligible for work study? Yes No I don't know * What is your availability? (days and times) (Open Ended Question) * Have you ever worked on campus before? If “Y”, what department and semester/year? (Open Ended Question) Optional Applicant Documents: Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
