    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36650": {
      "title": "Training Specialist",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Training Specialist Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Training Specialist To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260455S Position Title: Training Specialist Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 401-Human Resources Position Summary: The Training Specialist plays a vital role in designing and delivering comprehensive training programs for Villanova staff and managers, and provides support for the function through a variety of administrative, technical, and creative responsibilities. Works closely with the Director of Talent Development and the E-Learning Specialist to strategize, design, and deliver live in-person and virtual training events, such as workshops and departmental training programs, and participates in the creation and management of compliance-related online learning content. Coordinates logistics for live trainings and Human Resources-sponsored events, including the weekly new employee orientation and annual New@Nova Luncheon. Collaborates with stakeholders in HR and across the University to conduct needs assessments and identify skill and compliance knowledge gaps, ensuring training is tailored to the unique job functions of a diverse workforce. Utilizes LMS analytics and evaluation data to continuously improve program design. Contributes to talent development-related content on the Human Resources webpage and identifies professional development resources to support future staff training initiatives. Founded in 1842 and recognized among the nation’s best colleges and universities, we are a mission-driven institution inspired by the values of truth, unity, love, and dedication to serving the common good. At Villanova, we believe our people are our most precious asset. That’s why we offer a vibrant and collaborative campus environment and invest in our employees through competitive compensation and comprehensive benefits that support your professional growth, personal well-being, and long-term success. Benefits include: • Generous paid time off and holidays. • Tuition assistance for employees and eligible family members. • Professional development opportunities. • Retirement savings plan with University contributions. • Well-being programs and resources. • Flexible work options where appropriate We invite you to join a community where your contributions are valued, your growth is supported, and your work makes a meaningful difference. • Learn more about the benefits of working at Villanova on our website. Duties and Responsibilities: Training Design and Delivery: Design, coordinate, and deliver live in-person and virtual training and change management events (e.g., workshops, webinars, departmental training programs) for Villanova staff and people-managers, including mandatory training for all people-managers. Collaborate with the E-Learning Specialist to design relevant and timely training modules for staff; participate in the creation of new compliance-related learning content (including mandatory manager training) based on trends and topics that arise. Manage compliance-related content on Villanova’s employee learning management system ( LMS ). Troubleshoot issues; monitor and report on records of staff participation in training modules. Training and Event Logistics: Coordinate logistics as needed for live training events including written communications, presenters, catering, room set-up, and materials; monitor and maintain records of staff participation in training events. Collaborate with members of the Talent team to coordinate speakers, catering, room set-up, and materials for Human Resources events, including weekly new employee orientation and yearly New Staff Welcome Event; serve as back-up support staff for other Human Resources events. Needs Assessment and Strategy: Collaborate with stakeholders in HR and across the University to identify specific skill gaps and training needs within various campus units; conduct needs assessments to ensure training events are tailored to the unique job functions of the diverse University workforce; and strategize with stakeholders to align learning interventions with departmental and University-wide goals. Data Management: Utilize LMS analytics and survey data from training participants to continuously improve design and delivery of training content and programs. Ensure effective stewardship of Villanova’s talent development function. Professional Development: Identify and research resources (books, articles, etc.) for own professional development and for potential future use in staff training and development programs. Website: Maintain and regularly update portions of the Talent Development section of Villanova Human Resources website. Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education: Bachelor’s degree required. Specific Job Knowledge: Ability to effectively design, lead and facilitate live training events required. Basic understanding of adult learning principles and instructional design required. Knowledge of Human Resources functions and principles required. Working knowledge of a learning management system required. Must be able to learn and apply new technologies. Experience with Microsoft Office and basic AI literacy required. Knowledge of and experience with multimedia technologies, particularly video production and editing preferred. Minimum Work Experience: Minimum two years of experience in Human Resources, education, compliance, communications, instructional technologies, or related field, with at least one year in Human Resources required. Combination of experience and relevant post-high school education considered. Experience in higher education or non-profit environment preferred. Experience teaching or facilitating group learning required. Experience in event planning or management preferred. Work Skills: Demonstrated organizational skills; strong attention to detail. Ability to learn new skills and new technologies. Ability to work independently and take initiative. Proactive in identifying problems and solutions; forward-thinking orientation. Prefer creative or artistic skills, especially in writing, graphics and slide/video presentation aesthetics. Ability to produce reports and provide basic analyses of results. Ability to organize materials and records. Ability to form partnerships, work collaboratively, and engage people at all levels. Ability to plan and manage programs and events. Ability to communicate with vendors, employees, prospective employees, students, and administrators with tact and diplomacy. Must be able to understand, appreciate, and contribute to Villanova’s Augustinian mission and values. Equipment Knowledge: Ability to use computers, projectors, and other training tools. Working Conditions/Environment: a.) Tools, machinery and equipment used: computer, projectors, tablets, printer/copier/scanner/fax, and other general office equipment b.) Physical requirements: (items such as lifting, pushing, pulling, standing or sitting for extended periods of time, manual dexterity, walking etc.) sitting for long periods of time at computer terminal. ability to work at a computer station, lift and carry up to 15 pounds, and travel to other buildings on campus. Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education: Master’s or advanced degree. Specific Job Knowledge: Knowledge of and experience with video production and editing. Work Experience: Experience in higher education or non-profit environment preferred. Experience in event planning or management preferred. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 10/28/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: The approved range for this position is $65,000-70,000. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 13 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36653": {
      "title": "Dining Services Associate - Bellesini Cabrini Campus",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Dining Services Associate - Bellesini Cabrini Campus Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Dining Services Associate - Bellesini Cabrini Campus To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The start date for this position is on or after June 1, 2026. SCHEDULE during normal operating hours: Tuesday - Saturday 6am - 3pm Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260179S Position Title: Dining Services Associate - Bellesini Cabrini Campus Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal Applicants Only Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 837-Dining Services- Cabrini Campus Position Summary: Founded in 1842 and recognized among the nation’s best colleges and universities, we are a mission-driven institution inspired by the values of truth, unity, love, and dedication to serving the common good. At Villanova, we believe our people are our most precious asset. That’s why we offer a vibrant and collaborative campus environment and invest in our employees through competitive compensation and comprehensive benefits that support your professional growth, personal well-being, and long-term success. Benefits include: • Generous paid time off and holidays • Tuition assistance for employees and eligible family members • Professional development opportunities • Retirement savings plan with University contributions • Well-being programs and resources • Flexible work options where appropriate We invite you to join a community where your contributions are valued, your growth is supported, and your work makes a meaningful difference. Learn more about the benefits of working at Villanova on our website. As a Dining Services Associate you will be responsible for maintaining the overall cleanliness, sanitation, and food safety of the dining operations. This includes front of the house and back of the house areas along with receiving and stocking duties. Stocks, rotates, and replenishes merchandise The Dining Services Associate will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the value of the Villanova Mission Statement and the Dining Services Mission Statement! The individual will focus on our Core Values: Safety, Sanitation, and Excellence. All of our associates will work hard to improve our systems and overall operation. Why join our team ? Our dining services team members receive: Increased hourly rate starting at $17.50/hour Generous vacation plan and holiday schedule Free meals during each shift Health and wellness resources plus discount programs Opportunities for advancement Various schedules available, including late night positions with night differential Free uniforms, including footwear *Full-time employees also receive: 403b retirement plan with employer base and matching contributions, tuition remission for associates and dependents, medical, vision, and dental insurance with multiple health plan options Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Scrapes, cleans, sanitizes, and replenishes all dishes, silverware, cups, glasses, pots, and pans etc. Properly stores all clean items. Operates dish machine or pot machine and is responsible to record proper temperatures and correct levels of chemical sanitizers according to regulations. Loads and unloads dish machine. Disposes of food waste and trash both front of house and back of house as needed. Sweeps and mops all floors and walk in refrigerators. Separates recycling from trash. Assists in receiving, storing, transporting and stocking of food and nonfood items. NONESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Assists in transporting supplies from storage areas to work areas as required. Fills juices, milk, and soda machines as needed. Assists on serving lines or back of the house prep work if needed. Acts as a runner to replenish food supplies on service lines. Communicates with cooks concerning amounts of food on service lines. Works special events/weekends as required Perform additional duties and assist with special projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Work Skills: Basic reading and writing skills; basic communication skills. Excellent customer service skills. Practices excellent personal hygiene habits and follows and adheres to uniform standards. Ability to: follow directions and complete assigned tasks, work with minimal supervision, and to interact with people on a constant basis. Preferred Qualifications: Preferred – High school diploma or equivalent Preferred – Basic knowledge of food service safety and sanitation Preferred – Serv Safe Training and Allergy Awareness Training Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery, and equipment used: Knives, slicers, and all kitchen equipment Environmental conditions: Chemicals used for cleaning and weather exposure for special events. Physical Requirements: Ability to stand for extended periods Ability to lift, push/pull up to 50 pounds independently Ability to withstand extreme temperatures Special Message to Applicants: The start date for this position is on or after June 1, 2026. SCHEDULE during normal operating hours: Tuesday – Saturday 6am – 3pm Posting Date: 10/28/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: $17.50 per hour. Shift differential for qualifying shifts. Salary Grade: 8 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 0 Maximum Number of References Needed 0 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Optional Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36656": {
      "title": "Kitchen Supervisor - Cabrini",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Kitchen Supervisor - Cabrini Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Kitchen Supervisor - Cabrini To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Schedule during normal operating hours Friday/Saturday/Sunday/Monday 2pm - 1am Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260480S Position Title: Kitchen Supervisor - Cabrini Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 837-Dining Services- Cabrini Campus Position Summary: Founded in 1842 and recognized among the nation’s best colleges and universities, we are a mission -driven institution inspired by the values of truth, unity, love, and dedication to serving the common good. At Villanova, we believe our people are our most precious asset. That’s why we offer a vibrant and collaborative campus environment and invest in our employees through competitive compensation and comprehensive benefits that support your professional growth, personal well-being, and long-term success. Benefits include: • Generous paid time off and holidays • Tuition assistance for employees and eligible family members • Professional development opportunities • Retirement savings plan with University contributions • Well-being programs and resources • Flexible work options where appropriate We invite you to join a community where your contributions are valued, your growth is supported, and your work makes a meaningful difference. Learn more about the benefits of working at Villanova on our website. This leadership position assists the Culinary and Management team in the overall operation of the dining hall/unit. Supervises all personnel, including training and discipline, as well as the preparation and service of food in the unit while adhering to safety and sanitation procedures. Oversees distribution of recipes, work sheets, and production schedules. Assumes opening and closing responsibilities for the unit as required. Assumes responsibility for the kitchen in the chef’s or chef manager’s absence. Ensures food is fresh, well prepared according to the recipes, tasty and well-presented and food production is organized and on track to meet daily demands. This position will work with management and co-workers to instill and foster the values of the Villanova Mission and the Dining Services Mission Statement. This position will focus on our Core Values: Sanitation/Safety Friendly Courteous Service, and Excellence. Positions Supervised: Associates, Hospitality Associates, General Cooks. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: Essential Job Functions: Food Preparation Assists Executive Chef and Chef manager in daily food production Co -responsibility for the overall food quality Enforces and supports departmental quality assurance by adhering to VDS best practices for food handling, safety and sanitation. Assures compliance with standard recipes and production methods. Assists in the production and support areas as necessary which includes commissary and catering. Assists chef with the pot sink area including staffing, cleanliness and sanitation procedures. Assistance in the dish room area may also be required. Assists in the training of kitchen staff. Records and monitors food temperatures. Ensures production is organized and on track to meet daily demands, adjusting staff and/or menu as required. Assists leading a kitchen team with support, guidance, positive attitude and good communication skills. Menu Development Recommend changes in procedures and ingredients to assist with menu planning. Test new standardized recipes and make recommendations to the Executive Chef. Continuously research, train, and update techniques, skills and recipes through attending conferences, workshops (including virtual) and reading magazines/journals. Inventory Control Forecast food production quantities of needed products and supplies to ensure proper execution. Complete transfers and requisitions when necessary. Assist in the inventory process to provide accurate reports to assist with food cost analysis. Human Resources and Leadership Provide functional and/or administrative supervision of staff. Provides direction, assignments, feedback, coaching and counseling to assure outcomes are achieved. Assists with Performance reviews. Assists Executive chef and Chef Manager with scheduling. Trains all in safe operating procedures of all equipment and machinery. Includes proper safety training in lifting, carrying, chemical control, first aid and fire prevention/extinguishing. Responsible for opening and/or closing of the unit. Nonessential Job Functions: Performs other duties and assists with projects as assigned including special events for the university and for catering. Assist with scheduling repairs of kitchen equipment, special cleaning projects and pest control management. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Culinary degree/Associate degree or 5 years supervisory kitchen experience. Serv Safe Certification. Work Experience Minimum of 5 years total food service cooking experience preferably in a non fast food environment or high volume operation with progressive responsibilities. Experience with food service software systems. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Excellent written and oral skills. Able to work with a diverse work force. Ability to work independently. Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Extensive knowledge of Food Safety and Sanitation. Advanced food preparation and production skills. Ordering and inventory management. Attention to detail in food presentation, flavor and consistency. Proper knife skills ie diced, julienne, chiffonade, mince, etc Equipment Knowledge All kitchen equipment including combi ovens, convection ovens, induction burners, Anliker (Vegetable prep machine), broilers, large batch kettles and slicers, etc. Computer skills required. Preferred Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelor’s degree in hospitality or culinary field. Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery and equipment used: All kitchen equipment Environmental conditions: (any unusual/adverse conditions such as exposure to chemicals, noise, illumination, air quality, weather exposure etc.) . Exposure to cleaning chemicals, noise, air quality, and ability to withstand temperature extremes in refrigerator and freezer conditions. Physical requirements: (items such as lifting, pushing, pulling, standing or sitting for extended periods of time, manual dexterity, walking etc.) Must be able to lift pots, pans, etc up to 50 lbs. Must be able to stand and exert well-paced mobility for periods for up to 4 hours in length at a time. Special Message to Applicants: Schedule during normal operating hours Friday/Saturday/Sunday/Monday 2pm – 1am Posting Date: 10/28/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: The approved range for this position is $21.36-23.38/hr. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity.” Salary Grade: 11 Job Classification: non-exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
    },
    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36635": {
      "title": "Unit Chef - St Mary&#39;s",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Unit Chef - St Mary&#39;s Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Unit Chef - St Mary's To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Schedule during normal operating hours: Sunday - Thursday 11:30am - 8:30pm Special events and flexibility as needed Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260468S Position Title: Unit Chef - St Mary's Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 412-Dining Services Operations Position Summary: Founded in 1842 and recognized among the nation’s best colleges and universities, we are a mission-driven institution inspired by the values of truth, unity, love, and dedication to serving the common good. At Villanova, we believe our people are our most precious asset. That’s why we offer a vibrant and collaborative campus environment and invest in our employees through competitive compensation and comprehensive benefits that support your professional growth, personal well-being, and long-term success. Benefits include: • Generous paid time off and holidays • Tuition assistance for employees and eligible family members • Professional development opportunities • Retirement savings plan with University contributions • Well-being programs and resources • Flexible work options where appropriate We invite you to join a community where your contributions are valued, your growth is supported, and your work makes a meaningful difference. Learn more about the benefits of working at Villanova on our website. The Unit Chef provides culinary and operational leadership for St. Mary’s Dining Operations, supporting high-quality food production and an exceptional dining experience for students and the university community. This position leads daily kitchen operations, including menu execution, food production, staffing, training, scheduling, food quality, food safety, sanitation, inventory, and equipment oversight. The Unit Chef works closely with the Chef Manager and Dining Services Leadership to ensure consistent execution of menus and recipes, effective use of resources, and compliance with Dining Services standards and university policies. The Unit Chef leads and develops kitchen staff, promotes a positive and collaborative work environment, and ensures the kitchen is organized, efficient, and prepared to meet operational needs. This position may also support special events, catering, and other Dining Services operations as needed and may work directly in food production or on the service line to support the operation. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Provides day-to-day leadership and direction to kitchen staff, including participating in recruitment, hiring, scheduling, onboarding, training and performance management. Develops and supports employees by providing training on food preparation, recipes, food safety, sanitation, equipment operation, and Dining Services standards. Promotes a safe, respectful, and collaborative work environment and holds staff accountable for established operational standards. Ensures kitchen staff are prepared to consistently execute menus and recipes in accordance with established quality standards. Responsible for planning daily production and work schedules for cooks and related production associates. Collaborates with Dining Services managers to forecast production needs and prepare for upcoming menus. Maintains all production records for the Unit. Supports food cost management by standardization of recipes, waste reduction. Inventory management, and appropriate utilization of product. Evaluates menu items and recipes for production efficiency, food quality, taste, presentation, and customer response. Provides feedback on menu performance and participates in ongoing menu and recipe improvement in collaboration with Dining Services leadership and appropriate culinary partners . Coordinates effectively between back-of-house food production and front-of-house service to ensure a consistent and positive dining experience. Oversee food presentation, service line appearance and garnishing. Responsible for all equipment in the kitchen. Assists with scheduling repairs and special cleaning projects. Trains all staff in safe operating procedures of all equipment, utensils, and machinery. Provides safety training in lifting, carrying, chemical control, first aid, and fire prevention and extinguishing. Responsible for the Pot sink area including staffing, cleanliness, and sanitation. Must provide assistance in dish room area as needed. NONESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS : Coordinates special events with the Executive Chef and Special Events Manager. Must be available for special functions (catering) to assist in food production and service. Orders small wares and supplies as needed. Responsible for providing cooks with proper tools to perform their job tasks. Perform other duties and assist with projects assigned including opening and/or closing of unit. Minimum Qualifications: Formal Education Bachelor’s degree, culinary degree or equivalent combination of education and relevant work experience. Work Experience 3 – 5 years minimum experience in food service, including supervisory experience. Experience working in a high-volume food service operation, preferably in higher education, hospitality, or similar institutional dining experience preferred. Work Skills: Demonstrates the ability to lead and collaborate with a diverse team. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to work independently and respond effectively to changing operational needs. Strong organizational and time-management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Demonstrated commitment to food quality, customer service, teamwork, and continuous improvement. Specific Job Knowledge: Must be Serve Safe certified. Must have strong knowledge of food ordering, production, preparation techniques, and team supervision, with proven ability to delegate and manage tasks effectively while maintaining a consistent commitment to quality. Equipment Knowledge: Knowledge of kitchen equipment and maintenance requirements. Knowledge of computers for performing daily routines. Computer basics and software programs such as Microsoft Excel and Word. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Tools, machinery, and equipment used: kitchen equipment Environmental conditions: Exposure to chemicals associated with food service industry Physical requirements: Standing for long periods of time, ability to lift a minimum of 30 pounds, requires bending, climbing, reaching, standing, walking, sitting, grasping, carrying, repetitive motions, visual acuity, hearing, good verbal skills and occasional exposure to extreme temperatures -10 degrees in the freezers and coolers Special Message to Applicants: Schedule during normal operating hours: Sunday – Thursday 11:30am – 8:30pm Special events and flexibility as needed Posting Date: 10/26/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: The approved range for this position is $59,800-66,900. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity.” Salary Grade: 13 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
