    "https://jobs.villanova.edu/postings/36661": {
      "title": "Corporate Sales Manager",
      "description": "Villanova University Employment Site | Corporate Sales Manager Skip to Main Content Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Applicant FAQ HR Homepage Security report Title IX About Us Corporate Sales Manager To apply to this position, click on the Apply for this Job button below. If you have questions about the application process, please refer to the Applicant FAQ link on the sidebar. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Posting Details Do you have questions about the application process? If so, please refer to the Applicant FAQ’s. Posting Details (Default Section) Posting Number: 20260439S Position Title: Corporate Sales Manager Position Type: Staff Location: Villanova, PA Recruitment Type: Internal/External Applicants Work Schedule: full-time/12-months Avg Hours Week Department: 507-Inn at Villanova University Position Summary: Why work at Villanova? Join a mission-driven organization. Since Villanova University’s founding in 1842, we have been inspired by the values of truth, unity, and love, and are a community dedicated to service to others. Villanova has been included among the nation’s best colleges and universities. VU’s inclusion again in U.S. News & World Report’s 2025 “Best Colleges” rankings is another indication of the University’s continued prominence and forward momentum. Villanova’s most precious asset is our people . As an employee, you will receive a holistic benefits package, generous paid time off, a competitive retirement savings plan, flexible work options, wellness programs including gym membership, professional development, tuition assistance, and more . The Corporate Sales Manager serves as the liaison for corporate group sales and corporate transient business. This position is responsible for maintaining existing business, soliciting new business, and market analysis to maximize revenue. The Corporate Sales Manager utilizes traditional and non-traditional sales techniques to generate revenue, establish new accounts, and identify opportunities within the competitive market. Key responsibilities include developing strategies to capture available market share, monitoring transient production and pricing, securing meeting and event space bookings, maintaining repeat business, and conducting sales presentations, sales calls, and site tours, while maintaining a high level of service and quality. This position contracts and closes group and transient business, ensuring that business is turned over properly and in a timely fashion for quality service delivery. Achieve goals by seeking business opportunities that maximize revenues. Provides periodic reporting and analysis of market booking patterns and trends and builds customer loyalty through excellence throughout each customer experience. Villanova is a Catholic university sponsored by the Augustinian Order. The University is an equal opportunity employer and seeks candidates who understand, respect and can contribute to the University’s mission and values. Duties and Responsibilities: ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS (Basic/Critical Responsibilities/Duties) % of Time 10% – Achieving or exceeding individual sales goals. 20% -Responding to group/meeting leads while drilling to capture LNR (negotiated rate) opportunities. 5% – Trend marketing to entice and promote location for corporate meetings, receptions, dinners, trainings, retreats, overnight rooms, etc. 40% – Prospect, identify and secure all corporate business including meetings, trainings, retreats, receptions, LNR and all other aspects of the corporate market. Actively solicit new business through phone calls, correspondence, networking, and on site tours in order to secure contracts and support guest satisfaction. 5% – Participate in professional membership organizations to develop prospective client relationships and remain current on industry information, practices and trends. 5%- Enter and maintain data to generate contracts, update client files, and record information into booking software. 5% – Generate updates on transient segment each period to continually analyze transient booking patterns for trends, future need periods and obstacles to achieving goals. This role includes on-site event support as needed, with evening and weekend availability required approximately 25% of the time. PART IV: NONESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS (Less Critical Duties etc.) % of Time 5%- Perform other duties and assist with projects as assigned. 2% – Training and empowering sales team members to exercise good judgement to make profitable business decisions. 3% – Ensuring that the property is maximizing the use of all Villanova University and local programs (i.e. CVB’s, PAMPL , networking memberships) 100 % OVERALL TOTAL ( ESSENTIAL & NON - ESSENTIAL ) Minimum Qualifications: Minimum Requirements: Formal Education High School diploma or equivalent required. Bachelor’s degree preferred but experience considered in lieu of a degree. Work Experience: 3-5 years of combined sales, leadership, and development experience. Work Skills (e.g., written and verbal communication skills) Strong written and verbal communication, interpersonal, organization, and customer service skills. Ability to use Word, Excel, PowerPoint and reporting tools. Ability to learn and effectively use technology platforms, including PMS , POS , TBD booking software, etc. Ability to prepare and confidently deliver professional client presentations, from initial development through execution. Specific Job Knowledge (e.g., knowledge of principles and procedures related to field and area) Ability in strategic planning, staff development, marketing, budgeting and analytics to drive measurable results and focus resources on work that will excel revenue growth. Knowledge of sales and marketing principles and practices. Ability to develop clients relationships, identify business opportunities, analyze sales and booking trends, and support revenue goals. Ability to organize and prioritize multiple sales activities and respond effectively to changing business needs. Equipment Knowledge: PC and general audiovisual equipment Other: This roles includes on-site event support as needed, with evening and weekend availability required approximately 25% of the time. Proper business attire is required for in house and networking events. Preferred Qualifications: Physical Requirements and/or Unusual Work Hours: Special Message to Applicants: Posting Date: 10/07/2026 Closing Date (11:59pm ET): Salary Posting Information: This position falls within salaried grade 15 and the range is $65,300-81,600. The final salary will be determined with consideration of several factors including the selected candidate’s qualifications, department budget availability, market data, and internal equity. Salary Grade: 15 Job Classification: exempt References Needed References Needed Minimum Number of References Needed 3 Maximum Number of References Needed 3 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first hear of this employment opportunity? Indeed.com Higheredjobs.com LinkedIn Glassdoor Chronicle Vitae Academic Keys PA CareerLink/JobGateway Professional Affiliation/Trade Website Diversity Association/Publication Website Advertisement in Academic or Professional Publication Referred by a current employee Referred by a friend, family member, or former employee Heard about it at a conference or career fair Browsing the Villanova website Cabrini University employee Other * If your answer to the above question is \"Other\", please specify the source below. If this question does not apply to you, enter N/A. (Open Ended Question) Documents needed to complete your application: Required Documents Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Resume / Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents © 1990-2022 Villanova University. All Rights Reserved. 800 Lancaster Avenue · Villanova, PA 19085 · (610) 519-6000 · Privacy & Security Return to the Top    Villanova University To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
